[11511]={"Find a suitable place to <rgb=#FF0000>Cheer</rgb> or <rgb=#FF0000>Laugh</rgb> at the fighters","Thorzhaf can be found in Talath Úrui.\
\
You should find a suitable place to help sway the current fighting match.","Swaying the Match","This looks like a good place to <rgb=#FF0000>Challenge</rgb> or <rgb=#FF0000>Roar</rgb> at the fighters","A conniving goblin sees opportunity in your presence and seeks an unlikely pact.","You have successfully swayed the fight!","The fighter has gained confidence","Párgrub can be found near Thorzhaf.\
\
You should speak with Párgrub about the match.","Talk to Párgrub","Find a suitable place to <rgb=#FF0000>Challenge</rgb> or <rgb=#FF0000>Roar</rgb> at the fighters","'Listen good, ${RACE}. This poor snaga bet some supplies on the fights in Thorzhaf right now. Can't afford to lose these supplies, you understand. Maybe you sneak in there and sway the fights? Yes, then maybe this poor snaga be less poor!'","This looks like a good place to <rgb=#FF0000>Cheer</rgb> or <rgb=#FF0000>Laugh</rgb> at the fighters","'Oh you help Párgrub much! Now less poor and more supplies and power come this way, yes. Very good bet, this poor snaga made.'","This looks like a good place to <rgb=#FF0000>Cheer</rgb> or <rgb=#FF0000>Roar</rgb> at the fighters","The fighter has lost confidence","Find a suitable place to <rgb=#FF0000>Cheer</rgb> or <rgb=#FF0000>Roar</rgb> at the fighters"},
[11513]={"'¡Amdir se ve tan cambiado desde anoche! Casi siento que no es más que una sombra cuando lo miro, como si en verdad no estuviera allí... ¡cómo me hace temblar!\
\
'Vi a Trancos preparar un ungüento de hoja de rey para su herida, pero mi Abuela siempre usaba un remedio distinto cuando un joven Brandigamo se hacía una astilla terrible: ¡té dulce de arándano!\
\
'Olfateé arándanos junto al agua al este de aquí cuando pasamos anoche, lo que significa que están en temporada. Me encantaría preparar un té para el pobre Amdir.'","Celandine Brandigamo cree que las propiedades medicinales de los arándanos harán un excelente té para combatir la aparente infección de Amdir.","Celandine olió arándanos junto al agua al este de Archet cuando pasó anoche.\
\
Debes recolectar arándanos, pues hacen un té dulce que combate la infección, o eso dice la sabiduría hobbit.","Celandine Brandigamo te espera en el centro de Archet.\
\
Debes llevarle a Celandine los arándanos que recolectaste, pues piensa preparar un dulce té medicinal para ayudar a fortalecer la voluntad de Amdir.","Racimos de arándanos recolectados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lleva los arándanos a Celandine","Esta misión no puede completarse fuera de la introducción.","'¡Bien hecho! Has encontrado más que suficiente para un té fuerte y sabroso. ¡Seguro que esto animará a Amdir! Dame un momento y pondré a infusionar las bayas en agua hirviendo.'","Recolecta arándanos para el té medicinal de Celandine (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Té Dulce de Arándano","'Espero que el té de mi Abuela haga que Amdir se sienta un poco mejor. ¡Siempre me animaba cuando estaba enferma!'"},
[11514]={"Bring the honeycombs to Meliri","You have visited each of the five beehives around the orange groves of Burukíri in Ambarûl, from which you collected honeycombs. You bring them to Meliri.","'Beautiful!\
\
'Not you, lûkal, the honey. I mean no insult, but you do look somewhat strange. Which is fine for a stranger. Anyway, here is your coin.'","Meliri informed you they keep beehives around the orchard to pollinate the trees. They produce enough extra honey that they are able to sell some of it at the market.","'If you want to make the coin you must do the work! Say hello to the bees at each hive and collect honeycombs.'","Meliri has tasked you with visiting each of the five beehives around the orange groves of Burukíri in Ambarûl, from which you are to collect honeycombs.","Collect honeycombs from beehives (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I have another job that needs doing. Not afraid of bees, are you? We keep bees here at the orchard to help pollinate the trees. As a nice little extra, we get enough honey from them that we can sell some of it at the market. There are five beehives around Burukíri. Visit each one, collect some honeycomb, and bring them to me.'","Sweet Extras","Collected honeycombs from beehives (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[11516]={"'Only the sweet waters of the clearest spring are worthy for our cistern.'","Bring the water back to the Vineyards' cistern","Maliriel has asked you to help her companions finish preparations for the upcoming banquet.","Sweet Water","The spring lies directly west of the Vineyards of Lórien.\
\
The Elves of Lothlórien draw water for their feasts from the clearest and sweetest spring in the forest. Glasnír has asked you to draw some water and return it to the cistern in front of the Vineyards.","Glasnír is at the Vineyards of Lórien, east of the spring.\
\
You should speak with Glasnír regarding your task.","Habla con Glasnír en los Viñedos de Lórien","'If it is not too onerous a task, my good ${CLASS}, may I ask you fetch water for me? We will need much for the banquet.\
\
'The water of the Anduin is fine for most uses, but for our festivities, we prefer to use water drawn from the clearest spring in the forest of Lothlórien. It is not too far at all, simply proceed west from here, and you will find the spring tucked away along the side of the southern ridge.\
\
'Be careful not to spill too much on the way back... I expect a thirsty crowd this evening!'","'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. Thirsty guests will toast your name tonight!'"},
[11517]={"Enswith awaits at her farmstead, north-east of the meadhall of Faldham.","'I know that nothing will bring Adléod back to me, but I feel a sense of closure in knowing that he has been avenged.\
\
'Thank you, ${PLAYER}, for accepting my request. I shall depart for the King's city, but will honour Adléod's memory with each passing day.'","Return to Enswith with news of Gat's defeat","You have defeated Gat","'Adléod, oh, dear Adléod. He was my husband... killed by Orcs during our walk along the western hillside. He stood alone against them so that I might escape, but now, everything in Faldham reminds me of his tragic death. I cannot bear to stay here much longer.\
\
'Please, traveller, I beg of you this one favour. Before I flee, to start a new life in Edoras, I  ask for vengeance for Adléod. The Orc who slew my husband was a large brute, called Gat by those with him. Ensure that Gat is never able to harm another man, and I will see you to your reward.'","Defeat Gat, the Orc brute","Enswith seeks revenge against the Orc-marauder who was responsible for the loss of her husband.","Gat and his Orc allies have been seen wandering the hills north and west of the mead hall.\
\
Enswith has described the Orc brute, Gat, and has encouraged you to defeat the Orc, in order to avenge her belated husband.","Swift Revenge"},
[11519]={"Sword of the Fathers","Bring Helvorlim to Thane Béortnoth","Helvorlim should be in a coffer or box somewhere in Thornhope.\
\
Thane Béortnoth has asked you to find Helvorlim, his family's heirloom sword.","'It must be there still! The Orcs may have taken it -- or the tree when it took me -- but I think not. It was hidden well, and they would have to dig deep to find it, I am sure.\
\
'What? Helvorlim, my family's heirloom sword, of course! It is the token of my birthright.\
\
'I am not yet strong enough to fight the Orcs... will you enter Thornhope and search for Helvorlim? I will make it worth your while!'","You have found Helvorlim","Helvorlim is not here","'Ah yes, this is it! You have found Helvorlim! With this sword, I will bring my vengeance down upon the heads of the Orcs!'","Thane Béortnoth was rendered half-mad, following the Orcs' assault on Thornhope.","'Have you found Helvorlim yet?'","Thane Béortnoth is encamped outside of Thornhope.\
\
You should bring Helvorlim to Béortnoth at once.","Search for Helvorlim, the heirloom sword of Béortnoth's family"},
[11520]={"'This camp has drawn a lot of attention from those who are not on friendly terms with the hobgoblins. I've spotted quite a few Orcs spying from the shadows. The weapons they carry will be vital to giving the damage you're about to do the proper framing!\
\
'Yes, we're going to make this look like an Orc plot, rather than the work of dwarves! I hope your acting is up to the challenge, friend! Actually, perhaps I will teach you a thing or two about it. I have received many compliments for my ability to throw my voice, making it seem as if I am speaking from some distance away.\
\
'Your part in this play will be to collect weapons from the Orc-spies hereabout, and then I will scatter them around to make it look like the Orcs ambushed this camp. What can go wrong? Nothing, ${PLAYER}. Nothing can go wrong.'","'Ah, good work! I'll place these next to some of the defeated hobgoblins to set the scene. Let the master show you how it's done!'","Talk to Klúso near Stazg Vozag","Orc spies surround the out-camp of Stazg Vozag, carrying swords of jagged metal.","Swords in the Shadows","Klúso is scouting near Stazg Vozag.","Collect weapons from Orc-spies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected weapons from Orc-spies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Orc-spies near Stazg Vozag carry the weapons Klúso will need for the plan."},
[11521]={"Léofcetel can be found at the western watch-tower, just west of Cliving.\
\
Garmund has asked you to convince the Rider Léofcetel to join him on his errand.","Léofcetel has refused to go against the orders of Reeve Athelward","'It weighs heavy upon my heart to see the lands I have sworn to protect in such ruin and abandonment. Slowly may we overcome the numbers of the Orcs and their trail of wreckage, but not if we are shut behind our city walls.\
\
'I thank you for accompanying me, ${PLAYER}. It is no small comfort to know that there are others who know the importance of protecting one's home.'","'Let us set forth. Upon your steeds, men! Ready yourself, ${PLAYER}!'","Garmund believes that the men in his éored must act for the sake of the Norcrofts, even against the will of Reeve Athelward. Not all men share his sentiments, and some refuse to disobey the Reeve.","'Garmund oversteps his bounds! We are under direct orders from Reeve Athelward himself; we are to guard the city walls and never to patrol beyond.\
\
'I will not take part in this disobedience. I understand that it is a noble undertaking, but we have our commands, and we must follow them.\
\
'I suggest you inform Garmund that I will be reporting to Athelward the moment he abandons his post. Do not take part in his foolishness, ${PLAYER}.'","'Reeve Athelward has asked us to remain on watch against the Orcs and to ensure the safety of the city. We repelled the single attempted infiltration of Cliving, and in the time since, no Orcs have dared to try again. All the while, the Orcs are free to roam our lands, pillaging and raiding as they see fit.\
\
'I mean no disrespect to Reeve Athelward, but I know that we could greatly benefit were we to ride against the Orcs in the fields. My men all agree, save Léofcetel. Please speak with him and convince him that riding against our foes is the correct course of action.'","Ride with Captain Garmund across the plains","Talk to Captain Garmund","Captain Garmund can be found at the western watch-tower, just west of Cliving.\
\
Garmund wishes to convey thanks after the difficult encounter on the fields outside Cliving.","Captain Garmund can be found at the western watch-tower, just west of Cliving.\
\
Léofcetel has refused to ride along with Garmund and his men and has asked the Captain to consider the consequences.","'I cannot fault Léofcetel for his loyalty to the Reeve, but there is more to duty than simply following commands. We have all sworn oaths to protect these lands and the people that live upon them. I wish to uphold those oaths and to bring justice to the trespassers against the plains of Rohan. I will gladly face the consequences, if my deeds preserve even a yard of my homeland.\
\
'I welcome you to ride with us, ${PLAYER}. We intend to strike fear into these brutes and pillagers.'","Talk to Captain Garmund outside Cliving","Sworn Oaths","Talk to Léofcetel and convince him to ride along with Captain Garmund","Captain Garmund can be found at the western watch-tower, just west of Cliving.\
\
Captain Garmund wishes to set forth at once, to prevent further destruction to the farms of the crofters of Cliving."},
[11522]={"Angbor can be found outside Tumladen in Upper Lebennin.\
\
You have delivered Terenis's warning to Lord Angbor. He bears a missive from Aragorn that must be brought to the Lady at once.","Talk to Angbor","'Aragorn has told me much of Lady Terenis, though she was much younger when last they knew each other. Even then, she had a keen wit about her and when that failed, a decidedly sharp tongue.\
\
'You say she noticed the ships as they sailed, as he expected, and he will see that she learns of the fate of Pelargir before her curiosity drives these people into a misplaced fervour. The true challenge for her, I suspect, will be keeping such knowledge to herself. As it is with you and I, she too shall be bound by an oath to Aragorn... an oath to a King. \
\
'We shall go to her in her hall, and speak of this when you are ready. Let us be done with this errand, ${PLAYER}, for four thousand men should not wait upon the meddling of nosey folk - even if they are kin of the Steward!'","Lady Terenis can be found in her hall in the rear of Tumladen in Upper Lebennin.\
\
You have delivered Aragorn's missive to Lady Terenis, and should now aid her as Lord Angbor requested.","At the request of Aragorn, Lord Angbor has come to Tumladen to privately deliver a message of victory to Lady Terenis.","Talk to Lady Terenis","Sworn to Secrecy","'I... am sorry for the manner of our meeting, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Surely, you realize my threats were empty and borne only out of desperation! I welcome any aid that you can offer to my people.'","'Let us ease the Lady's curiosity, shall we?'"},
[11524]={"'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. Destroying those totems soothes me, though I worry we may yet encounter the being they depict.'","'I noticed that the village of infected Orcs is full of unfamiliar totems. I suspect the Orcs may worship the bat-like creature carved into them. Something does not feel right about this and it would be a relief to see these totems destroyed.'","The Orcs of Faltor Gâm seem to worship someone or something, and their totems give you a bad feeling. Faeron has asked you to destroy them while you are there.","Destroy Stained Totems (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Symbols of the Stained","Talk to Faeron","Stained Totems can be found in Faltor Gâm, the village of the Infected Orcs.\
\
You should destroy Stained Totems.","Faeron can be found at Viznak's Hideout.\
\
You should talk to Faeron."},
[11525]={"Encuentra la parte del manuscrito que habla de la partida de Bingo de la Comarca","'Has encontrado algunas de las páginas perdidas del primo Bingo en el sendero del norte, ¿no? ¡Ese camino conduce a las Quebradas de los Túmulos! Si vas a aventurarte en ese terrorífico lugar, ¡yo también! ¡Una heroína nunca huye de un desafío, sin importar lo aterrador que sea!\
\
'He oído que criaturas terroríficas tienen su hogar en los túmulos de los hombres en las Quebradas de los Túmulos, y que tendremos que enfrentarnos a algunas de ellas si vamos allí. Ten cuidado con los voraces barghests y los gusanos gigantes, ¡porque podríamos llamar su atención!'","Tom Bombadil podría haber dejado el manuscrito de Bingo fuera, cerca de su casa, y Bingo te ha preguntado si puedes buscarlo.","'He oído que criaturas terroríficas tienen su hogar en los túmulos de los hombres en las Quebradas de los Túmulos, y que tendremos que enfrentarnos a algunas de ellas si vamos allí. Ten cuidado con los voraces barghests y los gusanos gigantes, ¡porque podríamos llamar su atención!'","Caléndula y Prisca Boffin están en el exterior de su casa en Norburgo, y cada una de ellas desea hablar contigo.","Le preguntas a Tom qué pensó del manuscrito de Bingo, pero el extraño individuo parece confuso.\
\
'Tus palabras están todas revueltas, joven. Tom recuerda muchas cosas: el sol en la mañana, las brisas del mediodía, el bochorno de la tarde y el fresco de la noche; pero no sabe nada de las páginas de las que hablas. ¡No es necesario escribir! Si pasas todo el día escribiendo, ¡es un día que has perdido!\
\
'¡No pongas esa cara! Estoy seguro de que las páginas aparecerán. Puede que lo haya dejado fuera. Hay tantas cosas que ver, distracciones felices todas ellas, y a veces las cosas se pierden. ¡Al final todo aparece, ja!'","Bingo quiere llevar a Caléndula de vuelta a su casa en Norburgo antes de continuar su viaje.","Derrota a los barghests en las Quebradas de los Túmulos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con Caléndula en el exterior de la casa de Tom Bombadil","Has encontrado las páginas sobre la lección de natación de Bingo","Habla con Tom Bombadil y recupera el manuscrito de Bingo","Bingo te ha dicho que se reuniría contigo en el exterior de la casa de su prima Prisca en Norburgo una vez que terminaras en las Quebradas de los Túmulos.","'Tom está casi siempre fuera de casa. Quizá lo dejó olvidado en algún lugar cercano. ¿Puedes buscar en los alrededores por si encuentras algunas páginas de mi manuscrito? ¡No quiero perder el registro de este viaje tan cerca de su comienzo!'","Barghests derrotados en las Quebradas de los Túmulos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con Prisca Boffin en el exterior de su casa en Norburgo","Deberías llevar estas páginas de vuelta a Bingo","Habla con Caléndula Boffin en el exterior de la casa de su madre en Norburgo","Has encontrado algunas páginas del manuscrito de Bingo en el sendero que lleva hacia el norte desde la casa de Tom Bombadil. ¿Quizá el viento haya arrastrado más páginas en esa dirección?","Has encontrado algunas páginas del manuscrito de Bingo, pero todavía faltan algunas páginas. Deberías volver a hablar con Bingo y Caléndula en el exterior de la casa de Tom Bombadil para decidir el curso de acción.","Busca al norte de la casa de Tom Bombadil más páginas del manuscrito de Bingo","'¿Te importaría hablar con Tom y recuperar mi manuscrito? ¡Estoy muy interesado por oír lo que piensa de él, ahora que ha tenido tiempo de sobra para leerlo!'","Has encontrado algunas de las páginas de Bingo. Quizá el viento llevó las otras hacia el norte.","Habla con Bingo en el exterior de la casa de Tom Bombadil","'¡Tenemos que buscar en las Quebradas de los Túmulos las páginas restantes! Parece que me falta la sección de mi diario donde describía la lección de natación y la sección que narraba nuestra salida de la Comarca. Cuando hayamos terminado en las Quebradas de los Túmulos, deberíamos volver a Norburgo para llevar a Caléndula a casa. Te veré allí.'","'Prisca piensa que fue idea mía ir de excursión por las Quebradas de los Túmulos, cuando era lo último que se me pasó por la cabeza. ¡La idea fue principalmente de Caléndula!'","'Ah, Prisca se calmará con el tiempo. Siempre lo hace. Ahora visitaré a todos mis primos segundos, y haré todo lo posible por quitarle a Caléndula la idea de dedicarse a ir de aventuras.\
\
'No creo que tenga éxito, y entre tú y yo, ${PLAYER}, ¡tampoco quiero tenerlo! Será una buena heroína, si es lo que quiere ser, ¡y Prisca tendrá que acostumbrarse!\
\
'Pero no le digas que he dicho eso. ¡Todavía necesitamos tener un lugar donde quedarnos hasta que continuemos nuestro viaje!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>La semana que viene: 'Las dos posadas' (Nivel recomendado: 24)</rgb>","'Gracias por encontrar parte de mi manuscrito, ${PLAYER}. Tom debe haberlo dejado fuera y el viento lo arrastró, llevándose las páginas hacia el norte hacia los árboles. Has encontrado algunas de ellas, pero parece que el resto de las páginas han sido arrastradas más hacia el norte... hacia las Quebradas de los Túmulos.'\
\
Bingo se estremece.\
\
'Ese lugar tiene una aterradora reputación y no planeaba explorarlo, ¡pero parece que ahora no tengo opción! ¡Tenemos que buscar en las Quebradas de los Túmulos las páginas que faltan! Parece que me falta la sección de mi diario donde describía la lección de natación y la sección que narraba nuestra salida de la Comarca. Cuando hayamos terminado en las Quebradas de los Túmulos, deberíamos volver a Norburgo para llevar a Caléndula a casa. Te veré allí.'","Habla con Bingo en el exterior de la casa de Prisca, en Norburgo","'Muy bien, ${PLAYER}. Diría que ya es hora de que Caléndula esté sana y salva de vuelta en Norburgo, ¡y de que nuestro viaje continúe! He disfrutado de esta breve estancia en la casa de Tom Bombadil, ¡pero hay muchos otros lugares que ver y gente que conocer!\
\
'¿Te importaría hablar con Tom y recuperar mi manuscrito? ¡Estoy muy interesado por oír lo que piensa de él, ahora que ha tenido tiempo de sobra para leerlo!'","'¡Ha sido increíble, ${PLAYER}! ¡Las Quebradas de los Túmulos son exactamente lo que esperaba! Nunca estuve asustada, en realidad.\
\
'¡Tendré que idear algo realmente emocionante para superar esta última aventura!'","Bingo está en el exterior de la casa de su prima Prisca, en Norburgo, al otro lado del Puente del Brandivino viniendo desde la Comarca.","'Hemos vuelto sanos y salvos de las Quebradas de los Túmulos, ¡y he agotado mi reserva de adjetivos para describirlas, ${PLAYER}! ¡Hay tantas formas de describir cómo de infeliz me hacía caminar sobre esos túmulos..!\
\
'He aprendido una valiosa lección: ¡no dejar que la gente lea mi libro antes de que esté terminado! Tom no pretendía hacer ningún daño, pero no quiero arriesgarme a perder más páginas en lugares aterradores. Seguirle la pista a las páginas ha sido una actividad extenuante, ¿no crees?\
\
'Prisca está bastante enfadada conmigo, además. Piensa que fue idea mía ir de excursión por las Quebradas de los Túmulos, cuando era lo último que se me pasó por la cabeza. ¡La idea fue principalmente de Caléndula!'","Gusanos derrotados en las Qeubradas de los Túmulos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bingo está en el exterior de la casa de Tom Bombadil. Deberías darle las malas noticias de que Tom ha perdido su manuscrito.","Sinóminos para siniestro","'Ha estado bien ver a mi primo Bingo, pero debo pedirle que se vaya tan pronto como pueda. O ha sido una mala influencia para Caléndula o ella lo ha sido para él, ¡pero de cualquier manera hay demasiado espíritu aventurero entre esos dos!\
\
'Los Boffins hemos sido muchas cosas, ¿pero héroes? ¡No que yo sepa!'","Has encontrado las páginas que trataban sobre la partida de Bingo de la Comarca","El viento ha arrastrado algunas páginas del manuscrito de Bingo al norte de las Quebradas de los Túmulos, y debes buscarlas. Caléndula te ha pedido también que derrotes barghests y gusanos mientras buscas.","Tom ha dejado por descuido en algún lugar el manuscrito de Bingo","Derrota a los gusanos en las Quebradas de los Túmulos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡No pongas esa cara! Estoy seguro de que las páginas aparecerán. Puede que lo haya dejado fuera. Hay tantas cosas que ver, distracciones felices todas ellas, y a veces las cosas se pierden. ¡Al final todo aparece, ja!'","'¿Has encontrado algunas de mis páginas, pero crees que el viento ha arrastrado más hacia el norte? ¿Puedes ir a comprobarlo, ${PLAYER}?'","Encuentra el manuscrito de Bingo en algún lugar cerca de la casa de Tom Bombadil","'He regañado a Caléndula antes, y nunca parece servir de nada. La chica siempre está yéndose en busca de aventuras. ¡Aventuras! ¡Más bien son trastadas y molestias, si me preguntas a mí!\
\
'Ha estado bien ver a mi primo Bingo, pero debo pedirle que se vaya tan pronto como pueda. O ha sido una mala influencia para Caléndula o ella lo ha sido para él, ¡pero de cualquier manera hay demasiado espíritu aventurero entre esos dos!\
\
'Los Boffins hemos sido muchas cosas, ¿pero héroes? ¡No que yo sepa!'","'¡Te veré de vuelta en casa de mi prima Prisca en Norburgo, ${PLAYER}! ¡No quiero estar aquí ni un instante más!'","Encuentra la parte del manuscrito que habla de la lección de natación de Bingo","Habla con Bingo en el exterior de la casa de Prisca Boffin, en Norburgo","Tom Bombadil está en el exterior de su casa en el Bosque Viejo durante el día, y dentro durante la noche.\
\
Bingo te ha pedido que recuperes su manuscrito de Tom Bombadil y averigües qué piensa de él tras leerlo.","'¿Tom ha perdido mi manuscrito? ¡Oh, qué fastidio! Sé que todavía no había mucho escrito, ¡pero aún así siento mucho su pérdida! ¡No seré capaz de recrear exactamente lo que escribí la primera vez! Quizá deba abandonar esta empresa. No soy escritor, ¡ni aventurero!'\
\
Intentas consolar al desanimado hobbit, y pronto Bingo parece menos abatido.\
\
'Quizás tengas razón, ${PLAYER}. Tom está casi siempre fuera de casa. Quizá lo dejó olvidado en algún lugar cercano. ¿Puedes buscar en los alrededores por si encuentras algunas páginas de mi manuscrito? ¡No quiero perder el registro de este viaje tan cerca de su comienzo!'"},
[11526]={"Pitch is used to waterproof boats and coat arrows so they will burn.","Collect vases from Sâd Torech (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Vases can be found in Sâd Torech.\
\
Aldbéort has asked you to collect pitch-filled vases from Sâd Torech.","'Very good. We are not making many boats these days, but the Orcs do not like when our arrows burn.'","<rgb=#FF0000>Completing Aiding the Eastemnet will cancel this quest</rgb>","'Let me know when you are ready to venture to Sâd Torech.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is an instanced public questing area.</rgb>","Collected vases from Sâd Torech (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Sâd Torech: Pitched Battle","Aldbéort is at Cliving.\
\
Aldbéort will be pleased to receive the pitch-filled vases.","Talk to Aldbéort","'The Orcs often come at night, marching through the farms and coming right up to the edge of town before we even know that they are out there. It has become a large problem, and we have lost many from surprise attacks.\
\
'We need pitch. With it, we can coat our arrows and set them ablaze, lighting the night sky and revealing our enemies. Sâd Torech, a former town of Gondor, has many vases filled with pitch. Bring some back for us.'"},
[11527]={"Drakelings and bats have settled in the remains of Sâd Torech.","Sâd Torech: Sinking Feeling","Defeated drakelings and bats in Sâd Torech (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Drakelings and bats can be found at Sâd Torech.\
\
Aldbéort asked you to clear some of the drakelings and bats from Sâd Torech.","'It will take time to clear them all out, but I am glad that we have begun.'","Defeat drakelings and bats in Sâd Torech (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I would like to be able to send the youths to Sâd Torech to collect the pitch-vases for us, but I cannot. The journey itself is easy and safe enough, but the town has been settled by drakelings, and while they are small, our young simply cannot withstand that threat.\
\
'If you can clear out some of the drakelings and bats, in time we may be able to reclaim the town, and our supply of pitch shall no longer be threatened.'","<rgb=#FF0000>Completing Aiding the Eastemnet will cancel this quest</rgb>","Aldbéort is at Cliving.\
\
Aldbéort will be pleased to hear the drakeling and bat population in Sâd Torech has been thinned.","Talk to Aldbéort","'Are you prepared to journey to Sâd Torech?'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is an instanced public questing area.</rgb>"},
[11528]={"Destroyed Sûhalar barricade (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Easterlings can be found across the River Forant in southern Talath Anor.\
\
You should defeat Sûhalar patrols and destroy Easterling barricades.","Defeat Sûhalar patrols (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Ingold can be found at the northern gate of the Rammas.\
\
You should speak with Ingold.","Sûhalar on the Forant","Speak with Ingold","'This is a fine start down the path to victory! There is much more to do though if we are to stand a chance in the days to come.'","Defeated Sûhalar patrol (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'This northern army consists of Orcs from Mordor and Sûhalar Easterlings. These strange, axe-wielding Easterlings are a new threat, the likes I have not seen before. If we are to hold the northern gate for the Rohirrim we will need to deal with these northern forces.\
\
'Venture into Talath Anor, the lands north of here and defeat patrols of these Easterling axe-men.\
\
It has also come to my attention that these Easterlings are trying to construct barricades along the Forant River. This should be dealt with as well.'","The discovery of a northern army and strange axe-wielding Easterlings concerns Ingold and threatens his ability to hold the North-gate.","Destroy Sûhalar barricades (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[11529]={"This man disagrees with Agelwyn, and wishes to defend Marton","Agelwyn is in the refugees' hiding spot north of Marton.\
\
You should speak with Agelwyn.","This man agrees with Agelwyn","Tell the refugees of Marton of Agelwyn's command (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'I support Agelwyn in this choice.\
\
'It pains me to leave Marton to the Orcs, but I am too old and stiff to fight. If I were a younger man, I might feel differently.'","This woman is relieved to go to Helm's Deep and avoid a skirmish with the invading Orcs","This woman respects Lady Agelwyn's position as acting Thane","This man does not seem to speak much, but he bows his assent. He has not left Agelwyn's side, and it seems that he is as loyal to her as he was to Gladsúnu.","'Five agree with me, and four do not. But that must not change my decision. I should count myself lucky that I have not angered everyone.'","'Helm's Deep?! Why, that is nonsense. Are we truly going to let the Orcs who took our town think that we are cowards who will simply roll over and flee?\
\
'I do not support this decision!'","This man does not respect Agelwyn's decision","'I will gladly follow my king to Helm's Deep. It would be an honour to fight for him there!'","'Thank heavens Agelwyn has made this decision! I am terrified of the Orcs that took over our town. I do not believe we can win against those fearsome foes.'","The people of Marton can be found in the refugees' hiding spot north of town.\
\
You should deliver Agelwyn's decree to the people of Marton.","'I cannot believe we would abandon the lands of our forefathers! We have inhabited Marton for hundreds of years. Are we to just leave it to the Orcs?\
\
'A vile decision! Do tell the lady that.'","This man agrees with Agelwyn, for he wishes to defend the King","Gladsúnu's loyal soldier is silent, but bows his assent","'Agelwyn refuses my counsel, does she? Well, now I know where the people stand in her eyes....\
\
'Perhaps her foolishness can still be amended.'","Speak with Agelwyn","'I respect Lady Agelwyn's decision. Thane Gladsúnu left her in charge, and I will follow her lead.\
\
'Gladsúnu is a wise young man, and would not give us a leader he did not trust.'","'I do not agree with that young lady on this decision. I should not be travelling so far in my old age.\
\
'It is foolish to ride across the plains when our home is right here.'","You believe that Agelwyn should take a firm stand and make a decision for her people, regardless of their feelings.","This woman resents that she has been commanded to abandon her home","This woman disagrees with the choice to go to Helm's Deep, which she deems is too far","'I believe that I should issue a strong command, for that is what my husband would have done. Gladsúnu was wise, and no one questioned him.\
\
'We should go to Helm's Deep, as Gladsúnu bade me. The King is there. There is no other way... I think. Is that right?'\
\
You assure Agelwyn that her decision is just, and you will inform the other refugees.","Tactic I: Strength in Leadership"},
[11530]={"This man wishes to retreat to Helm's Deep","This man wishes to go to Helm's Deep to defend the King","This woman respects Lady Agelwyn's position as acting Thane, and will follow her will","This man firmly believes in remaining at Marton, and is contemptuous towards Agelwyn for considering anything else","This man wishes to defend Marton","Agelwyn is in the refugees' hiding spot north of Marton.\
\
You should speak with Agelwyn.","'I believe we should go to Helm's Deep.\
\
'It pains me to leave Marton to the Orcs, but I am too old and stiff to fight. If I were a younger man, I might feel differently.'","'Whatever Agelwyn leans towards herself, I will follow. Thane Gladsúnu left her in charge, and I will follow her lead.\
\
'Gladsúnu is a wise young man, and would not give us a leader he did not trust.'","Ask the refugees of Marton to vote (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'Since I have so little experience in command, I would like to know what the other townsfolk think we should do. I know some must wish to fight and win back Marton, but surely others will not want to put themselves into harm's way.\
\
'I will let the majority decide. Do you think that is wise?'\
\
You assure Agelwyn that her decision is just, and you will ask the other refugees to weigh in on the matter.","Gladsúnu's loyal soldier is silent, but bows his loyalty to Agelwyn","This man does not seem to speak much, but he bows his assent. He has not left Agelwyn's side, and it seems that he is as loyal to her as he was to Gladsúnu.","Tactic II: The Will of the People","'I will gladly follow my king to Helm's Deep. It would be an honour to fight for him there!'","'I have already stated what must be done. Marton needs to be taken back.\
\
'The fact that she even considers any other option only demonstrates her weakness as a leader. This girl should not be playing at Thane as if the position was one of her dolls.'","'I cannot believe that Agelwyn would even consider abandoning the lands of our forefathers! We have inhabited Marton for hundreds of years. I vote not to leave it to the Orcs.\
\
'Tell the lady what I said.'","'It is clear that we must fight to win back Marton! We cannot let the Orcs who took our town think that we are cowards who will simply roll over and flee.'","You believe that Agelwyn should ask her people what they think, and let the majority of them decide the fate of Marton's refugees.","For myself, I should not be travelling so far in my old age. I believe we should attempt to remain in Marton.\
\
'It is foolish to ride across the plains when our home is right here.'","Speak with Agelwyn","'Helm's Deep!! Would that I could vote for two. I am terrified of the Orcs that took over our town. I do not believe we can win against those fearsome foes.'","This woman votes not to abandon Marton","The people of Marton can be found in the refugees' hiding spot north of town.\
\
You should ask the people of Marton what they think should be done: Retreat to Helm's Deep, or fight to with back the town.","This woman very much wishes to avoid a skirmish with the invading Orcs, voting for Helm's Deep","'This did not make anything easier! I had hoped the people would decide, but instead they have left me to break a tie.\
\
'Four definitively for Marton, and three for Helm's Deep...and I am four. I do not deny that I wish to go there as Gladsúnu counselled. And two more follow my decision.\
\
'Then it looks like we go to the stronghold of Helm's Deep, but many will not like it....'","This woman prefers to remain in Marton"},
[11531]={"This man wishes to retreat to Helm's Deep","This man wishes to go to Helm's Deep to defend the King","This woman respects Lady Agelwyn's position as acting Thane, and will follow her will","This man firmly believes in remaining at Marton, and is contemptuous towards Agelwyn for considering anything else","This man wishes to defend Marton","Agelwyn is in the refugees' hiding spot north of Marton.\
\
You should speak with Agelwyn.","Tell the refugees of Marton of Agelwyn's command (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'The decision must be mine, but I do not want to make a blind one. I wish to know what the others think. My heart leans towards Helm's Deep, but I truly don't know if it's prudent.\
\
'Do you think this is a bad idea, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You assure Agelwyn that her decision is just. You should ask the other refugees to say what they think, and report to Agelwyn on their concerns.","'I believe we should go to Helm's Deep.\
\
'It pains me to leave Marton to the Orcs, but I am too old and stiff to fight. If I were a younger man, I might feel differently.'","'If I weigh everyone's decisions, including the two that will follow where I wish, the majority do wish to go to Helm's Deep. That is in line with my own desire.\
\
'This was not as clear a choice as I had hoped. I fear I will displease many.'","'Whatever Agelwyn leans towards herself, I will follow. Thane Gladsúnu left her in charge, and I will follow her lead.\
\
'Gladsúnu is a wise young man, and would not give us a leader he did not trust.'","Tactic III: Wisdom of Counsel","You believe that Agelwyn should listen to everyone, but ultimately make her own decision.","Gladsúnu's loyal soldier is silent, but bows his loyalty to Agelwyn","This man does not seem to speak much, but he bows his assent. He has not left Agelwyn's side, and it seems that he is as loyal to her as he was to Gladsúnu.","'I will gladly follow my king to Helm's Deep. It would be an honour to fight for him there!'","'I have already stated what must be done. Marton needs to be taken back.\
\
'The fact that she even considers any other option only demonstrates her weakness as a leader. This girl should not be playing at Thane as if the position was one of her dolls.'","'I cannot believe that Agelwyn would even consider abandoning the lands of our forefathers! We have inhabited Marton for hundreds of years. I vote not to leave it to the Orcs.\
\
'Tell the lady what I said.'","'It is clear that we must fight to win back Marton! We cannot let the Orcs who took our town think that we are cowards who will simply roll over and flee.'","For myself, I should not be travelling so far in my old age. I believe we should attempt to remain in Marton.\
\
'It is foolish to ride across the plains when our home is right here.'","Speak with Agelwyn","'Helm's Deep!! Would that I could vote for two. I am terrified of the Orcs that took over our town. I do not believe we can win against those fearsome foes.'","This woman votes not to abandon Marton","This woman very much wishes to avoid a skirmish with the invading Orcs, voting for Helm's Deep","This woman prefers to remain in Marton","The people of Marton can be found in the refugees' hiding spot north of town.\
\
You should ask the people of Marton what they think Agelwyn should do next."},
[11532]={"'¿Thomas Cardoso te envió? Sí, sí, me aseguraré de que reciba su moneda. Tengo algo mucho más importante que tratar contigo.'","Tad Cortahoja se encuentra frente al Pabellón de Caza de Bree, al oeste de la Puerta Sur.\
\
Tad Cortahoja ha pedido que los aventureros de Bree vayan a hablar con él.","'Hola. Pareces justo el tipo de persona que Tad ha estado buscando. El joven Cortahoja lleva tiempo buscando aventureros por Bree y me pidió que los enviara con él cuando los viera.\
\
'Ve, visita a Tad Cortahoja. Debería estar al oeste de la Puerta Sur, aquí en Bree. Asegúrate de decirle que te envié yo; no me pagan si no van de mi parte.'","Tad Cortahoja ha pedido que los aventureros de Bree vayan a hablar con él.","La Petición de Tad"},
[11533]={"Tailor: Fur Blankets","Stitch fur blankets for the people of Wildermore (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'These are lovely, ${PLAYER}! I aspire to do such skilled tailoring myself, but I am afraid I am nowhere near your level of skill.\
\
'I will make sure that these are delivered to those who need them.'","<rgb=#FF0000>Completing Wildermore's Recovery will cancel this quest.</rgb>","A skilled tailor such as yourself can help the refugees of Wildermore by stitching warm blankets for them.","Hildelith is in Forlaw.\
\
You have stitched fur blankets, and should now deliver them to Hildelith.","Hildelith has given you a recipe for fur blankets.\
\
You should stitch fur blankets for the cold refugees at Forlaw.","Stitched fur blankets (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Are you a tailor as well as a hero, ${PLAYER}? That is good to hear, for many refugees in Forlaw shiver in this colder climate. It will take them a while to adjust; until then, they need blankets.\
\
'Have you any Riddermark hides that can be turned into warm blankets for the people?'","Deliver the fur blankets to Hildelith"},
[11534]={"Uruk-hai pillagers can be found along the edges of the road to the south-west of Entwade.\
\
Thane Edric has asked that you clear the road south of foes as his wife, Léoflad, continues to prepare her people to journey south to Aldburg.","Defeated Uruk-hai pillagers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Thane Edric can be found outside the Mead Hall of Entwade in Kingstead.\
\
You have defeated many Uruk-hai along the road south of Entwade and have secured safe passage for Léoflad and her people. You should return to Thane Edric.","Talk to Thane Edric","'You bear the telling marks of a skirmish, ${PLAYER}. I trust it is done then.\
\
'The Uruks have been fighting with great tenacity as of late, so I am glad that their riders along the road have been quelled.'","Tainted Lands, Tainted Legacy","Uruks have recently begun to attack and pillage travellers upon the southern road through Kingstead. Such attacks threaten the journey of Léoflad and the people of Entwade.","Defeat Uruk-hai pillagers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","DNT -- Players will not see","'You appear to be a hale ${CLASS}, traveller. As my wife makes ready to escort my people south to safety, I would ask something of you.\
\
'The road to the south will lead my people to Aldburg, but our foes lurk too near. The Uruks that stalk the fields of Kingstead have done much to harry my people and have been so bold as to attack Entwade itself several times in the past weeks. Now, I have heard talk that they ride along the road to the south and slay passers-by before claiming their goods.\
\
'My people and my wife cannot meet such a fate, ${PLAYER}. Ride against them and clear the road so that my people may pass unfettered when the time comes.'"},
[11535]={"Has robado la famosa receta de la Cerveza de Gunderic","'Psst. Por aquí. Sí, tú; ¿a quién más crees que le estaría hablando? Estás justo delante de mí, insensata criatura ${RACE}.\
\
'He tenido una idea... una visión, si se quiere. Es el sueño de la Asociación Cervecera. Suena maravilloso, ¿no? Una auténtica hermandad de enanos amantes de la cerveza, con nuestras mejores recetas. ¡El problema es que esos bribones de pies peludos, esos hobbits desvergonzados, se nos adelantaron!\
\
'Aquí es donde entras tú. ¿Conoces la iniciación de la Liga de las Posadas? Vamos a ponerle fin y ahogarla desde el comienzo para que no pueda crecer más. Debes robar las recetas de sus preciadas cervezas y ales. Sin recetas, no puede haber Liga de las Posadas.'","Jónar, un habitante siniestro y hosco de la Mansión de Thorin, se ha vuelto cada vez más amargado ante el creciente éxito de la Liga de las Posadas.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro de misiones cuando finalice el festival actual.</rgb>","Roba la receta de la Cerveza de los Helechos","'¡Esos pequeños demonios de pies peludos y caras lampiñas! ¡Los odio! ¡Odio a todos los hobbits! ¡Jamás imaginé que duplicarían esas recetas y las repartirían entre todos esos entrometidos ${CLASS} que quisieran una!\
\
'Pero he aprendido algo que jugará a favor de la Asociación Cervecera, la mayor liga de amantes de la cerveza de toda la Tierra Media: ahora sabemos que los hobbits no guardan sus secretos como lo hacemos los enanos, y eso será su perdición. ¡Ja!'","Jarra Contaminada","Lleva las recetas robadas a Jónar en la Mansión de Thorin","TBD","'¡Exijo esas recetas! ¡No se debe permitir que esa liga de hobbits perdure, no cuando cerveceros superiores están aquí ante ti!'","Roba la receta de la Cerveza de Gunderic","Las valiosísimas recetas de la Liga de las Posadas pueden encontrarse repartidas por toda la Comarca: en Cepeda, fuera de la Perca Dorada; en los Grandes Smials de Alforzaburgo; en la Oficina de la Guardia de Tejonera; y en El Cruce.\
\
El enano Jónar te ha pedido que robes las recetas de las ya célebres bebidas maestras de la Liga de las Posadas: la Cerveza de los Helechos, la Cerveza de Gunderic, el Porter de Perry y la Sidra de Nudoraíz.","Jónar te espera con impaciencia en la posada de la Mansión de Thorin.\
\
Deberías regresar y llevarle las recetas robadas, pues querrá oír todo lo sucedido durante tus encuentros con los miembros de la Liga de las Posadas.","Has robado la escurridiza receta de la Cerveza de los Helechos","Has robado la célebre receta de la Sidra de Nudoraíz","Roba la receta del Porter de Perry","Roba la receta de la Sidra de Nudoraíz","Has robado la codiciada receta del Porter de Perry"},
[11536]={"Enârshan has asked you to sabotage the supplies in Khûn Sagaz with the Idâmi concoction as well as take as many of their weapons as you can.","Tainted Stores","Weapons gathered in Khûn Sagaz (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Contaminate supplies in Khûn Sagaz (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You are back. Were you able to find success in Khûn Sagaz?'\
\
Enârshan smiles slightly as you give her the weapons you took and confirm that you used her concoction on the supplies.\
\
'Wonderful news. I believe we are nearing our goal.\
\
'You have done well.'","Gather weapons in Khûn Sagaz (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Supplies contaminated in Khûn Sagaz (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Return to Enârshan","'Ah, you are here. Good. Everything is now ready.'\
\
Enârshan hands you the concoction she crafted.\
\
'Take this concoction and pour it over their supplies within Khûn Sagaz. I also ask that you take any weapons you can from them.\
\
'This will give us the advantage we need to drive them away at last. My falls will soon be free with your help.'","Return to Enârshan in the Falls of Ilûritu and let her know you have used her concoction on the supplies and taken what weapons you could.","Enârshan has provided you with the Idâmi concoction to use on the supplies in Khûn Sagaz to weaken them. She also instructed you to take from them any weapons you find."},
[11537]={"'The watch-tower is evidently the first place the next wave of invaders means to take over. Elain will join you there to help secure our lands. If we can frighten away the Draig-lûth, I believe that we will remain safe from them for at least a generation.\
\
'Guto would have us wage a war of revenge that lasts a hundred years. I would give anything to teach him the error of judgement before I die. Wars are crueller than anything in this world.\
\
'Elain has more wisdom than Guto and is a strong warrior, but even strong warriors can be hurt. I beg you to keep her safe, ${PLAYER}... and keep yourself safe as well!'","'Ah, ${PLAYER}! We are like old friends now. I am glad that you have joined me, for it seems the Dragon-clan have arrived before us.\
\
'I fought many Draig-lûth off the path, but I dare not go nearer to the watch-tower. They will surely see us if we venture into the stone circle, and our hides will be sprinkled with a rain of arrows from the sky.'","Elain awaits you at the watch-tower in the centre of Trum Dreng, long held by the Stag-clan. The watch-tower has likely been captured by the Dragon-clan invaders.","Find Elain at the watch-tower","'Elain is a good girl, but I worry for her so. She is strong for her size and wise for her age, but even those who are blessed with such gifts can come into harm's way. Please, ${PLAYER}, keep her safe.'","Take Back the Watch-tower","Elain awaits you at the watch-tower in Trum Dreng, on a hill to the east of Lhan Tarren.\
\
You should join Elain at the watch-tower and see what can be done about the Dragon-clan invaders there."},
[11538]={"Join Golasgil and the men in toasting to those who fell on the Pelennor.","'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. The men and ale are gathered. Here goes nothing.'","Gathered soldiers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Golasgil","Join Golasgil in singing Authlin's Song to lift the hearts of the gathered men.","Gather soldiers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Golasgil can be found in the Camp of the Host, on the northern edge of North Ithilien.\
\
The celebration has gone off without a hitch. Now you should talk to Golasgil.","Collect kegs of ale (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Take Heart, Men of Gondor","'Lord Elessar has asked me to do something for the men? I will do my best, if my king wishes it. This would have been a task better suited to someone like Forlong, but alas, it falls to me.\
\
'He is not mistaken. Gondor has lost much already, but we all know that if we do not act now, we will lose everything. What would Forlong have done?\
\
'I have an idea. Gather the men from around camp, and some kegs of ale. Then, meet me back here. We will celebrate one last time before we march bravely into the Enemy's maw.'","Golasgil can be found in the Camp of the Host, on the northern edge of North Ithilien.\
\
You should speak with Golasgil and tell him the kegs and soldiers have been gathered.","<rgb=#FF00FF>Toast</rgb> with Golasgil","Golasgil can be found in the Camp of the Host, on the northern edge of North Ithilien.\
\
Lord Aragorn has asked you to talk to Golasgil.","'Well, my spirits are certainly lifted! We will march to our destiny with a song in our hearts. For Gondor and for all the Free Peoples. I think Forlong would not be ashamed of us, ${PLAYER}.'","'${PLAYER}, while those of faint hearts have departed, I feel we must do something for the men who remain. They have lost so much already, and this may be our last true chance to bolster their spirits before we move into the Enemy's territory.\
\
'I would have you speak with Lord Golasgil. With so few Lords of Gondor left, I will need him to bear more of the burden of leadership. I know he will show a brave face in front of his men if I ask it of him.'","Collected kegs of ale (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","<rgb=#FF00FF>Cheer</rgb> at Golasgil","<rgb=#FF00FF>Sing</rgb> with Golasgil","Aragorn wishes to do something to lift the spirits of the remaining soldiers.","You can find soldiers and kegs in the Camp of the Host, on the northern edge of North Ithilien.\
\
Golasgil has asked you to gather soldiers and kegs of ale."},
[11539]={"Defeated Kala-gijak look-outs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Excellent. Now when we attack, they won't see it coming. Everything is going according to plan.'","Faeron can be found outside Kala-gijak.\
\
You should talk to Faeron.","Kala-gijak has archer towers all around the perimeter where look-outs search for intruders. You need to find a way to remove these look-outs before your Drúadan friends are spotted.","Talk to Faeron","Kala-gijak look-outs can be found in the archer towers in Kala-gijak.\
\
You should defeat Kala-gijak look-outs.","Defeat Kala-gijak look-outs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Do you see those archer towers around Kala-gijak's perimeter? There is a look-out posted in each one. I need you to climb up and prevent those Uruks from signaling the alarm. Otherwise, our whole plan may fail.'","Take Out the Look-outs"},
[11540]={"Talk to Lanbert at the Cuthstan-camp","'How does one lead a company of soldiers when he cannot keep them armed? We have not enough arms to go around, yet still my requests to Stangard for new supplies are denied! I fear we must take this matter upon ourselves.\
\
'My scouts report that many of the Orcs in this region are carrying blades which would be suitable for our use. I would ask you to collect swords from fallen Orcs and return them to me here. Ensuring we are well-equipped is of the utmost importance.'","Collect weapons from defeated Orcs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Ah yes, these are suitable blades. Strong and well-made are the weapons you have brought before me. Are you certain these came from those miserable savages?\
\
'Well, no matter. You have both weakened the Orcs and strengthened our camp, in a single bold act. I am in your debt.'","'Now is not the time to be particular! Gather any working swords you can from the Orcs and bring them back to me.'","Collected weapons from defeated Orcs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The tribe of Orc vandals is south-west of the Cuthstan.\
\
Lanbert has asked you to search defeated Orcs for suitable weapons and to return them to him at his camp.","The men at the Cuthstan-camp are short on supplies, and the camp's leader has turned to scavenging weapons from fallen Orcs.","Lanbert is at the Rohirrim-camp at the base of the Cuthstan.\
\
Lanbert is awaiting your return with suitable weapons taken from the Orcs.","Taking Arms"},
[11541]={"Tolwin can be found in the hall of Crithost.\
\
You should speak with Tolwin.","Taking Back the Land","Orcs can be found with Eryn Cordovath.\
\
You should defeat Orcs in the orchard.","Defeat Orcs in Eryn Cordovath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Travel to Eryn Cordovath and assess the situation","'The look-out said the band of Orcs were at least a dozen strong. If we do not get to the orchard quickly, I fear our beautiful trees will be destroyed.\
\
'Please go to Eryn Cordovath at once and stop this band of Orcs before the orchard is no more!'","Eryn Cordovath is located north-west of Crithost.\
\
Travel to Eryn Cordovath and assess the situation.","'It saddens me that much of the orchard burns. I've spent many days playing in Eryn Cordovath. Hopefully, we will be able to rebuild from what is left of the orchard back into something as wonderful as it was before the invasion upon these lands.'","The Orkish patrol has already made it to the orchard and must be dealt with","Has derrotado orcos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","A look-out has spotted a band of Orcs headed for Eryn Cordovath, a nearby orchard that is in the process of being evacuated. Tolwin wishes for you to ride out there and assist the farmers.","Talk to Tolwin"},
[11542]={"'You have brought peace, not only to Sen Chatâk, but to countless peoples throughout Kighân.\
\
'I hope that these goblins move on from our lands, but even if they do not, they are disorganized and leaderless. They will be easy prey for our warriors.'","Go to Glúkroz and destroy goblin weapon racks and defeat Lugadúr, chieftain to the goblins. Glúkroz can be found north-east of Sen Chatâk.","Return to Ahâto in Sen Chatâk","Destroyed goblin weapon racks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat Lugadúr in Glúkroz","Destroy goblin weapon racks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'There is one goblin who leads the rest. I believe they call this one Lugadúr. He is the worst, by far.\
\
'Even if you destroy their weapons of war and defeat many of them, this Lugadúr will still raid our village. He has no fear, and a powerful lust for blood. I have seen Men and goblins like him before. He wants for nothing but destruction.\
\
'Defeat him, and we may yet see peace. The remaining goblins will scatter without their leader to guide them. May they scatter far from Kighân. Will you move to defeat him?'","Ahâto, a local hunter in Sen Chatâk, has asked you to hunt down Lugadúr, goblin chieftain to the marauding goblins of Glúkroz.","Taking Down Lugadúr","Return to Ahâto in Sen Chatâk to report on Lugadúr's demise."},
[11544]={"Find Tomos in the wild","Taking Matters Into Their Own Hands","'Please help him and bring him back to me, ${PLAYER}. Tomos was a great warrior when he was a young man, but those years are behind us now. We should do as the White Hand commands, for they hold the power now....'","'Hail, ${PLAYER}! Look... the Draig-lûth! I knew that they had settled nearby. They can smell the weakness of Galtrev.\
\
'I know I risk all to come here, but someone must deal with this menace. The White Hand does nothing but force us to labour for a war that does not help us.'","'${PLAYER}, you must help me! It is my husband Tomos... he is a stubborn old warrior, and he has gone to fight the Dragon-clan alone.\
\
'He says that the White Hand does not do enough to protect Galtrev, and so he must do so himself... but he is missing his work while he is gone. They will surely kill him upon his return!'","An elderly warrior of Galtrev, infuriated by the unwillingness of Isengard's guards to protect Pren Gwydh from the violence of the Dragon-clan, has decided to take matters into his own hands.","Tomos has escaped his forced labour to look into doing something about the Dragon-clan menace in Pren Gwydh.\
\
You should seek out Tomos and help him so that he can return before the White Hand Overseers notice that he is gone."},
[11546]={"While aiding the people of Sardol, you have come across fishing nets in the river Blackroot. Because Malthellam has urged the people to remain in their villages and their hunters have largely gone missing, it is likely that their food supply will begin to dwindle the longer the conflict continues in Gondor.\
\
You should gather fish to add to their supply in Sardol.","Fish can be found in nets in the Blackroot outside Sardol in south-western Blackroot Vale.\
\
You have discovered fishing nets in the river Blackroot and should gather fish to aid the people of Sardol.","Taking What Remains","Completado","You have recovered many fish from the nets along the river Blackroot.","Gathered fish from nets in the river Blackroot (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","DNT -- will not be seen","Gather fish from nets in the river Blackroot (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have recovered as many fish as you are able to bear back to Sardol. While the people who dwell there still have a supply of food, it will certainly dwindle the longer the Dead and Orcs plague the vale.\
\
You have done well to secure the health of Sardol for days to come.","With the hunters of Sardol missing, fish from the river Blackroot may be the only choice left for their survival if the danger in the vale continues to escalate."},
[11547]={"Transmitir la información a Calargyl","Maeriel necesita saber lo que su compañero montaraz sabe de los jabalíes enfermos y los huargos agresivos.","Habla con Calargyl","'Has demostrado ser más fiable que mi hermano, así que me pregunto si puedo encomendarte otra tarea. Debía encontrar a mi compañero montaraz, Calargyl, en Amon Firn, pero no quiero dehar solo a Merruth.\
\
¿Podrías contarle a Calargyl lo que hemos visto aquí? Los jabalíes enfermos y la presencia de huargos agresivos es preocupante. La oscuridad se cierne sobre Cardolan. Seguro.","'¡Saludos! Mi nombre es Calargyl. ¿Así que Maeriel está arreglando el desastre de su hermano? No me sorprende, pero el resto de noticias que me cuentas es bastante preocupante. He visto cosas extrañas con mis propios ojos.'","Maeriel te ha pedido que hables con su compañero montaraz, Calargyl, sobre lo que habéis visto y hecho en la Pradera de Juncos.\
\
Calargyl está cerca de Amon Firn, en el noreste de Cardolan."},
[11548]={"Go to the Rangers' camp","'Were it not for you, I would be dead right now, or worse! I could never thank you enough for stopping those men.\
\
'I knew my journey would be perilous, but I did not think I would be imperilled so often! If you wish to visit your friend's camp, I am happy to go with you. Who knows what would befall me if I did not!'","Khagâmi is tired from her travels west through An Shêru, and is ready to settle in for the night.","As you and Khagâmi talked at the camp-fire, you were attacked by a group of bandits. You were able to defend yourself with unexpected help from Faeron, Ranger of the Grey Company. You should talk to Khagâmi about the evening's adventure.","'Shall we build a camp-fire and make ourselves comfortable? It would be nice to get to know one another over a meal, would it not?'","Faeron invited you to his camp atop the nearby hill, and there you found his companion, Rhadrog. You should talk to him.","Talk to Rhadrog","Complete Instance: Taking a Rest","Khagâmi, who wanted a travelling companion in An Shêru, would like to set up camp and rest here for the night.","Talk to Khagâmi","'${PLAYER}! I did not expect to see you again so soon! What brings you to these parts?'\
\
You introduce Rhadrog and Khagâmi to each other and tell him of her errand.\
\
'I am sorry to say that I know little of these lands and cannot be of more help in your search for these dwarves of which you speak. Faeron and I have only just arrived here ourselves. We wanted to scout the areas to the west to see if the blight has spread to other areas. Thankfully, we have yet to see any such disease in this highland.'","'I do not know about you, but I am ready to get off my feet. Let us set up a camp here and get settled for the evening.'","Taking a Rest","You see a familiar face","Instance: Taking a Rest completed","After defending your encampment with unexpected help from Faeron, the Ranger invited you to his camp atop the nearby hill."},
[11549]={"'Ah, ${PLAYER}. I was rendered unconscious during the battle, but apparently the Dunlendings thought me dead. When they had removed themselves from the Mustering Tree, your Ranger friend found me and brought me back here.\
\
I will live, but others are lost forever but in song. Our lost companions will be missed, but I believe our actions will hinder the war-efforts of the Dunlendings...though to what degree, I cannot yet say.'","Taking a Stand","You found all of Léofward's scouts and reported back to him. Now Léofward prepares to act upon your discoveries.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This instance can only be run solo.</rgb>","Léofward is at the Rohirrim scout-camp in the Gravenwood.\
\
You should let Léofward know when you are ready to depart for the Mustering Tree.","Accompany Léofward to the Mustering Tree","Léofward is at the Rohirrim scout-camp in the Gravenwood.\
\
You should return to Léofward to discuss the battle at the Mustering Tree.","'I am distressed, ${PLAYER}. I fear that Cuthric's insolent goading of the Ox-clan captain has compromised our mission. More than that, both companies now converge upon the Mustering Tree, and I fear that once they have combined their strength, they will overrun our camp, and Théodred will have to fall back.\
\
'I will join Thurbald, Elfrith, and Cuthric and make a stand against the foe...will you join me, ${PLAYER}? At the least, we will have an end worthy of rememberance.\
\
'Let me know what you decide, my friend, but I must know soon.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This instance can only be run solo.</rgb>","Talk to Léofward at the Rohirrim scout-camp","'It is decided then! Let us be off and let the Dunlendings beware!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This instance can only be run solo.</rgb>"},
[11550]={"'Edric must be told what has happened here, and not a moment too soon.\
\
'Poor Léoflad, I have known her since she was but a girl.... She was trained well in the art of sword-play, and I grieve that she did not remain at the Wade to aid us. And now... I fear for Edric, truly I do. Such a loss would break the strongest man. Were there only more time to mourn....\
\
'I will prepare dear Léoflad for travel, and I shall bear her to the Wade with haste. Prepare a steed, ${PLAYER}, and leave the rest to me.'","Agelman can be found at your side or can be rallied by sounding your horn.\
\
You have readied the horse, and should now speak to Agelman before sending him back to Entwade.","The horses can be found near the farmhouse at Pendlac's Farm in south-eastern Kingstead.\
\
Agelman has asked that you ready a horse for him as he prepares Léoflad's body for travel back to Entwade.","Talk to Agelman","Readied the horse at Pendlac's Farm","'Well done, ${PLAYER}. Now then, allow me to ready Léoflad for her final journey.\
\
'Such a brave Woman....'","Ready the horse at Pendlac's Farm","'Have you readied the horse?'","Agelman hopes to return Léoflad to Edric's side and persuade the Thane not to abandon his charge in the wake of such a tragedy.","Taking the Blame"},
[11551]={"Taking the Fight To Them","'You are more effective than you appear.\
\
'Thank you. You may consider me a friend. Have I anything you should need of in Zajâna, do not hesitate to ask.'","'I believe Doorward Azagâya is our best bet as an ally. We need to prove our worth to her, and that we mean her no harm.\
\
'Go to her and see if she has a task that needs doing. The Doorwards said we need to lead with actions, well then, let our actions show our pure intentions.\
\
'Seek out Doorward Azagâya, ${PLAYER}, and do what she asks of you. I believe she will then tell us what we need to know about Bârshud.'","Return and report your success to Azagâya outside of the Shorakhúna in Zajâna.","Defeated Ordâkhai forces in Zajâna (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Report back to Mizâdi outside the Shorakhúna in Zajâna","Defeat Ordâkhai forces in Zajâna near Lajór (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Azagâya wishes for you to prove your friendliness to Zajâna by defeating Ordâkhai in Zajâna near the Hall of Lajór.","Speak with Doorward Azagâya outside of the Shorakhúna in Zajâna.","'I knew it! We just had to show our good intentions. All right, now we see if she is willing to tell us more information about Bârshud and his contacts in Zajâna.'","'If you want to prove your usefulness, I will not deny you that chance.\
\
'We have pushed the Ordâkhai back, but they are still a thorn in the side of Zajâna. They are barricaded in the Hall of Lajór and its immediate surrounds.\
\
'You and Mizâdi claim to be friends of Zajâna. Friends do each other favours. Take out a number of the Ordâkhai near the Hall, and I will be more friendly to you both.'","Defeat Ordâkhai forces near the Hall of Lajór in Zajâna. The Hall of Lajór is located in the eastern end of Zajâna.","Report back to Mizâdi outside the Shorakhúna in Zajâna.","Speak with Azagâya outside of the Shorakhúna in Zajâna"},
[11553]={"The Ornendil Bridge is located in Northern Osgiliath over the Anduin River.\
\
You should defeat enemy guards on the Ornendil Bridge.","'The enemy is on the Ornendil Bridge! I want to send you in to defeat the guards on the bridge so that we can recapture this key defensive point.\
\
'Taking hold of the Ornendil Bridge is important to the safety of our stronghold at the Palace of Eldacar. May hope be by your side.'","Taking the Ornendil Bridge","Defeat enemy guards on the Ornendil Bridge (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You have done much for the Gondorian army. We will take back this city!'","Edenos has tasked you with taking back the Ornendil Bridge in Northern Osgiliath by defeating enemy guards.","Edenos is at the Palace of Eldacar.\
\
You should speak to Edenos.","Defeated enemy guard (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Speak with Edenos"},
[11554]={"'Por favor, muestra el somnífero al Capitán Pasolargo. Entonces sabrá que no fallé en mis deberes.\
\
'¡Hemos sido saboteados!'","El Capitán Pasolargo se puede encontrar en Puente de Caballetes.\
\
Talbot Hinton te pidió que le mostraras al Capitán Pasolargo la extraña poción elaborada por los Orcos cerca de Nan Wathren.","Regresa con el Capitán Pasolargo","Talbot Hinton está en Puente de Caballetes.\
\
Deberías hablar con Talbot Hinton.","Has liberado al guardia inocente de su injusta prisión","'Humph, bueno entonces. Me alegra que esa debacle haya terminado. Quizás ahora podamos centrarnos en asuntos más urgentes....'","El Capitán Pasolargo se puede encontrar en Puente de Caballetes.\
\
Deberías hablar una vez más con el Capitán Pasolargo.","'No puedo agradecerte lo suficiente por tu ayuda, buen ! No sé si alguna vez te han metido en la picota... pero puedo decirte que no es una experiencia cómoda.\
\
'Creo que el Capitán Pasolargo estaba listo para ahorcarme por lo que pasó. Probablemente me has salvado la vida, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}.'","Muestra el somnífero elaborado por los Orcos al Capitán Pasolargo","Libera a Talbot Hinton de la picota","Talbot Hinton está en la picota en Puente de Caballetes.\
\
Deberías liberar a Talbot Hinton de sus ataduras, pues su inocencia está probada.","Talbot te ha pedido que le muestres el somnífero que encontraste al Capitán Pasolargo.","Habla con Talbot Hinton","El Capitán Pasolargo escucha tu explicación y toma una profunda inhalación del frasco de la poción.\
\
'¿Los Orcos elaboraron esto, ¿verdad? No es bueno para nosotros. Parece que han comenzado a usar el sabotaje cuando sus incursiones han sido frustradas por nuestras defensas en Los Caballetes.\
\
'Supongo que Talbot puede ser liberado de sus ataduras. Pero los guardias deben estar alerta ante cualquier viajero sospechoso a partir de este momento. Es un día triste para Puente de Caballetes....'","Talbot redimido"},
[11555]={"Defeated Ghâsh-hai (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Akhrûn, a former slave, has just escaped from the prison fortress of Naerband and may reluctantly seek aid in escaping further south to Nurn.","Talk to Akhrûn","The woman seems apprehensive about speaking to you.\
\
'You are not from here, I can see. I am Akhrûn. I have prayed for freedom each day. Now it is here but not the freedom of my dreams.\
\
'My freedom led me and my brethren to flee from our slavers in Udûn. We felt that freedom for the first time when the tower fell and fires spilled from out of the mountain.\
\
'I wished to return to my family in Nurn, but we were enslaved again by those who dwell in Naerband. I resisted so they threw me into the prison. The rest are still being held outside the fortress.\
\
'Now I do not know what to do.'","It seems Akhrûn isn't accustomed to talking for extended periods of time. She catches her breath and continues.\
\
'Naerband is a prison that no one leaves. We were meant to be rotting in cells, sometimes tortured or worse. \
\
'I alone escaped. I found a loose brick in my cell. Behind the brick were some metal shavings that I was able to use to pick the lock to my cell. From there, I found an old forgotten passage that led to the outside.\
\
'I want to rescue the rest of my fellow Nurnhoth from Naerband, but I cannot do it alone. Will you help us retain our newly found freedom?'\
\
You agree to assist Akhrûn.\
\
'I am thankful for your help. First we will need to defeat many of these Orcs of fire who patrol from here to Naerband.'","Akhrûn can be found just outside of Orodir, next to Naerband.\
\
You should speak with Akhrûn.","Ghâsh-hai patrollers can be found in Talath Úrui near Naerband.\
\
You should defeat Ghâsh-hai who patrol the path to Naerband.","Tales From Naerband","As Akhrûn pauses, your gaze catches the citadel of Naerband looming above you","Akhrûn can be found near Naerband in Talath Úrui.\
\
You should speak with Akhrûn.","Defeat Ghâsh-hai patrollers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Speak with Akhrûn","'Good, we have made it to the bridge to Orodir. It is here where they keep prisoners before sending them to die in Naerband.'"},
[11556]={"You have listened to many stories from the soldiers in the Swan-knight's Keep. You should bring these stories to Fingaer who is waiting for you in Harper's Court.","'Wel- AACHOO! -come back. Do you have tales for me to write about?'\
\
You pass along the stories you heard from the swan-knights. The bard's face grows pensive as you speak.\
\
'It seems that along with glory, there is also much darkness in war. Too often our songs sing only of the honour to be won, the renown one might gain. You have given me much to think about, ${PLAYER}. I shall endeavour to write a song that encapsulates both the glory and the horrors of war, lest we are urged to go too soon to battle when other ways might suffice.\
\
'Do not get me wrong, for our knights were fighting for the very world itself. But it is good to know of, and to share, both sides of this coin. You have my thanks for bringing me these tales.'","'Tales of battle for a bard? Songs cannot but hope to encapsulate the glory, the terror, the rush of steel upon steel and the fear of the flesh in the presence of it all. There were Orcs and feral Men, flashes of blood and metal and fur, fighting by tooth and fang and claw. It was a thing I shall never forget... and from which my dreams will never be safe.'","Fingaer has asked you to speak with soldiers in the Keep of the Swan-knights.\
\
The Keep of the Swan-knights is in Dol Amroth.","A bard of Harper's Court would like to compose songs about the Battles in which the city's swan-knights partook.","'You wish to know of the battlefield? I have much to say, of course! Why, I myself was responsible for bringing down six Orcs! One after the other, they fell at my hand!\
\
'I was even lucky enough to find myself back to back with Prince Imrahil at one point! We were set upon by a pack of vicious warriors, but they had nothing on my lord! You should have seen the way he swung his sword! Like it weighs nothing at all! His foes fell in great numbers before him - piled around us in droves!\
\
'Glad am I that I was able to serve and save these lands, my Prince, and our King.'","'Stories of the battlefield, you say?'\
\
She is quiet for some time.\
\
'It was important. We did not really have a choice, did we? It was go to war or die, or go to war and die, as many of my friends, my family did. But we could not just wait for them to take our country and our lands, to kill and slaughter as they washed over us like a dark wave. It was important that I went, that we went. I just wish more of us had come back. But it was important.'","Talk to Celudir","'The war? For a bard? I... I do not really remember it, truly. I think I do not want to. It comes in flashes to me in dreams - the noise of it. There is always a lot of noise. My captain yelling, the snarls of the Enemy, the sounds of metal on metal, or worse, on skin. The cries of the wounded, the horns propelling us forward - beacons of hope when it seemed all was lost.\
\
'I do not wish to remember, but I fear I will never forget. I am just glad that we have won. My only hope is that none may ever need to experience such things again. Perhaps, because I and others met that bloody host on the field, our children will know peace. Perhaps none other will again have to carry these memories.'","Talk to Ríaneth","Talk to Gloril","Tales of Battle and Woe","Talk to Nennion","Return to Fingaer","'Well met. You seek stories of the battlefield? I wish I could tell you I was a hero and did great deeds, but in truth, I was sick with fever and never made it out of camp. You will not find tales of glory from me, I am afraid.'","Talk to Brithben","'Well met! I am ...achooo! Oh, pardon me. Do pardon me. I am not ill, merely suffering from having walked here by way of the stables. You see, horses make me incredibly ill, and Dol Amroth has them stuffed into every nook and cranny.'\
\
The bard's words are interrupted by a procession of sneezes. He blows his nose noisily and smiles at you with watery eyes.\
\
'Ahem. I am Fingaer, minstrel extraordinaire, and it is my calling to write about the great and glorious battles in which our brave swan-knights partook. ACHHOO! However, it is also my curse not to be able to get close enough to them without setting myself sneezing for days. Say, if you were to make your way to the Keep of the Swan-knights and listen to their tales for me, I would reward you for your time. What do you s...s…ssssSACHOO… say?'"},
[11557]={"'What know you of the battle on the fields of Gondor?'\
\
You tell Daugha-tûm of deeds great and small on the Pelennor Fields. You speak of the death of Théoden King, the triumph of your allies against the Witch-king of Angmar, and of the sacrifices of great warriors before the Enemy's forces.\
\
'The Rangers spoke of a wraith garbed all in red, who thought himself protected from weapons of war, yet he fled the field in fear. How can one who need not fear death be cowed before the armies of Gondor? They cannot be so mighty!\
\
'If the Dark Lord has such servants in his command, how lowly must we be in his sight?\
\
'I hunger for battle with the Men of Gondor, and yet, this is an ill-fated path for my people. We shall be used to the last, and what glory shall we have when all of us are gone?\
\
'This battle must be ended, ${PLAYER}. It must... if ever we are to return home in peace.'","Jubuya can be found at Aelin Veren in central North Ithilien.\
\
You have spoken to the other prisoners and should now speak to Jubuya once more.","Talk to Jubuya","Jubuya, a sorcerer of Harad, has offered to tell the Rangers of his homeland and culture in exchange for leniency.","Talk to Daugha-tûm","Tales of Harad","'You know of the great battle? Tell me what happened - I beg you. What of the Men of Harad?\
\
You tell Thai-chât of the Black Serpent's doom at the hands of Théoden King and of the three Mûmakil who fell in their assault against the walls of Minas Tirith.\
\
'So much death... if only we had abandoned the Dark Lord long ago. Cruel is a master who sits behind black mountains and steep tower-walls, feeling nothing as his soldiers are slaughtered.\
\
'I no longer wish to be a part of this war... I wish only to return to Harad.\
\
'I have heard all I can bear. Leave me, ${RACE}!'","The Haradrim prisoners can be found at Aelin Veren in central North Ithilien.\
\
After questioning Jubuya, he has asked you to speak to his fellows about their lives in Harad.","'I have waited patiently for you to tell them of the battle, and now I ask that you tell me what you told them.'\
\
You tell Jubuya of the battle on the Pelennor Fields. You tell him of the shattering of the gates of Minas Tirith and of Grond. You tell him of the Witch-king of Angmar and of Gothmog's flight. You tell him of the Black Serpent's death, and of Théoden King who fell soon after. He listens attentively, and bares a sad smile when your tale comes to an end.\
\
'So my King and his sons are slain, then. They would not have wished for death to find them any other way, ${RACE}.\
\
'Regardless of this war's outcome, much will change in my homeland. The lands of Harad are unforgiving, but beautiful. If ever there is peace between our peoples, or if you remain such a bold adventurer, I believe you would feel at home in the wilds of Harad and among the warm winds of our deserts and jungles.\
\
'If there were the time, I would tell you more of it, but I can sense these Rangers no longer appreciate our conversation.'","Talk to Thai-chât","'I shall answer your questions, ${RACE}.\
\
'In truth, I know little of our purpose here... only that our war-master bade us surrender to these forest-men. You call them Rangers, do you not? A strange name, I think.\
\
'We had long been stationed in the lands of Dagorlad, but travelled southward to reach the battle on the fields. Many of our number were slain at Cirith Negen by the Rangers, and soon we were few. I learned of Gondor's victory from the Rangers, but know little else of the battle.\
\
'If this is our fate, I wish only to learn more of that great battle and then return home with my brethren. I would ask to hear more of the battle, but first, you should speak to my brethren of it... they are eager to hear of it.'"},
[11558]={"Bands of soldiers, Rangers, and warriors can be found throughout Haerondir.\
\
Elladan has asked you to gather the soldiers of the Host of the West stationed in Haerondir in the hope that he and his brother might ease their worries through the telling of an old victory over the Enemy.","Talk to Elladan at Haerondir","Gather bands of Men from the Host of the West (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Elladan can be found on the eastern ramparts of Haerondir.\
\
You have gathered many soldiers, rangers, and warriors and should now return to Elladan and Elrohir.","'You have done well, my friend! I see many have come to hear our father's tales, and we shall soon begin.\
\
'Let us hope it can bring some comfort to these men before we make for the Black Gate!'","Tales of Hope and Glory","After seeing the weight of the burden resting on the soldiers in the Host of the West, Elladan and Elrohir seek to inspire hope by telling them a tale of victory over the Enemy.","'${PLAYER}, my father's tales can do much to inspire hope and awe. Elrohir and I have heard them many times, and they are known to us now perhaps even more clearly than to our father after these long years.\
\
'His tales are full of both glory and despair, but certain moments carry with them no sadness even in the face of loss. He told us many tales of the battles during the Last Alliance, and while no moment can match the joyous defeat of the Enemy at the end of the Second Age, there are others that might inspire those in times such as these.\
\
'My mind is drawn to father's tales of the Battle of Dagorlad. It was a great and terrible battle that raged for many long years, and even after victory was won many more passed before the Ring was cut from the Dark Lord's finger. Even still, it was a victory that marked a turning point in what to many seemed a hopeless war against Sauron. Men, dwarves, Elves, and even the High Elves stood fast against the Enemy's forces and though many were lost in the fighting, they pushed forth and threw down the Black Gate.\
\
'It is a tale of victory against great odds, and it seems we march to a battle that shall be much the same. Brother, can you think of a greater tale to tell these men?'\
\
Elrohir shakes his head and seems pleased with Elladan's choice.\
\
'Gather the men of Haerondir, my friend, and let them hear of glory from us!'"},
[11559]={"'You have spoken with some people in the camps? Good. But before you judge the truth, I would ask you to witness the dangers we face out here. Every night we hear the howling of wolves, and betimes they grow bold and attack.\
\
'We fend them off with fire and bow as we may, but always we see the form of a great, grizzled pack leader beyond our reach. Tungváka we have begun calling him. Defeat him, and the wolves would surely lose their boldness, and keep away from our tents.\
\
'I think you will find Tungváka among his pack, down in the ravine east of here, among the trees.'","Enkárvo has encouraged you to talk to the Easterling refugees so you can judge the truth for yourself.","'When first we arrived in this vale, some number of us ventured down to the river's edge, so we might wash the mud from our cloaks and fill our water-gourds.\
\
'There, kneeling by the cool waters did we look up and behold the high tower of Dale, its walls and bridges and houses huddled like a herd of sheep.\
\
'But no gates or doors could we see from our place on the river, as if Dale had turned its back. Little did I dream that day how true this thought might be!'","Lobos derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat Tungváka","'There is a name whispered in fear among our tents: Athálrik. Have you heard this name? He and his men come among us, chests puffed out. They shove those who have not offended. They take what is not theirs. They accuse us of things we never imagined.\
\
'And suppose we struck back? We are not so helpless against a handful of men, armed though they be. If we struck back, would the Men of Dale believe we did so in defence? No, no. That is not the way.'","Defeated Tungváka","Talked to Easterling refugee (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","You should return to Enkárvo in the Dorwinion refugee camp, in the hills east of Dale.","Derrotar lobos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'We Chayasír dwelt in this valley once, many lives of Women and Men ago. So it is sung by our Sangemêkh, our Song-Mother, of how before we wandered we settled around the Long Lake.\
\
'How long have these Dale-folk lived here? If they continue to prove unworthy of this fair and bounteous land, perhaps it is they who should wander and the Chayasír should take it back!'","'Why have we fled so far from our homes in Rhûn? Have you not heard of the great devastation that happened there? Some say it was a blazing fire that rose up out of the earth, consuming all. Others, a darkness coming down from the sky, a thousand, thousand night-black red-eyed crows.\
\
'I did not see it with my own eyes, I confess. They say none who did escaped with their lives. But when peoples, not just of Dorwinion, but beyond came fleeing in droves past our homes, we fled, too.\
\
'Had you seen the terror in their eyes, you would have done the same!'","'The camps of the Chayasír and of Dorwinion are not far from each other. You should go and talk with the people of both, and maybe you can judge for yourself.'","'Many carts full of goods have I known from Dale, though until we fled I lived all my life in far Dorwinion.\
\
'Many a merchant of Dale have I known, fair of speech and manner, come down the long roads to trade with us.\
\
'So tell me now, if you can, how they have forgotten us now that we are at their doors? How they have forgotten their fair speech and the hospitality with which we treated them?\
\
'Tell me, when they rise in the morning, how can they look their children in the eyes?'","Tales of the Travelled","'Some among us may complain of their lot - but is that not always so? So we do not lay about in a palace upon cushions of silk! Many leagues we walked, dogged by hunger, harried by sickness, robbed and beaten. And always the terror of what devastation lay behind us, never knowing whether it followed us, and how fast.\
\
'Here we have found food and rest for our weary feet. We have come so far. Surely we can overcome the obstacles before us.'","'Look for the wolf ancient Tungváka and his pack in the low ravine south and east of here. They are the wolves who have grown bold enough to try and attack us.'","'Tungváka is defeated? You have done a great good. But here is Komúsi. Your face tells me the tidings are not happy.\
\
'What has happened?'","'We are Chayasír, and so we wander. But never so long, so ceaselessly and wearyingly have we wandered. I have seen such wonders as I never imagined!\
\
'From the ruin we fled and came over high mountains. We were very near the tops when they shook, shook mightily. We fell to our feet, all of us, and watched amazed as the snows flowed cascading like thundering rivers down onto the foothills below.\
\
'Then we came to the sea, the waters roiling and the sands lined with a great wreckage of ships. There was fire among them, and whether they came from strife among men, or great storms, or some other cause, I cannot say.\
\
'We did not tarry. We went on.\
\
'Over green lowlands we travelled, and then up into high dry-lands, swept cold by wind. There the earth had been opened up as if from a wound, and we could not see into the depths.\
\
'Armies we saw, gleaming and orderly, as if going off to war. Then we saw other soldiers, wounded and dirtied, wandering as if lost. Sometimes they robbed us, or beat us. Other times, they went on by.\
\
'At long last we have come here. Our Sangemêkh says this is a homecoming and that we will stay here, at least for now. And so we rest, and mourn all we have lost, and think in wonder over all that we have seen.'","Return to Enkárvo","'Have you heard the tale of the War in Mordor? Let me tell you, for I have heard all about it. The armies of Gondor blew their horns and the gates crumbled before the blasts. Then the Red King vied in battle, one on one, with the White Sage. At their blows, the earth trembled! When the Red King struck, the sky darkened. When the White Sage landed a blow, the mountain burst into flame.\
\
'Though he took a grievous wound, the White Sage prevailed and claimed the Red King's crown. All the Orcs of Mordor perished on the spot and a thousand thousand birds descended from the skies to pick at their bones.\
\
'That is what I heard, and I swear that it is true!'","Talk to Easterling refugees (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","The wolves can be found south and east of the refugee camp hills.\
\
You should find and defeat wolf pack leader Tungváka, and a number of his pack, to stop them from being bold enough to attack the Easterling refugees.","'When you haggle over the cost of goods in the market, neither haggler is fully to be believed. This we know. And yet, there is a true and fair worth to the goods, and when the haggling is done, it is hopefully found. But how do you know that truth? You hear both sides.\
\
'Why do you not go among my people and among the Chayasír, and hear our sides of the story? The two camps are close, and when you are done, maybe you can judge the truth for yourself.'","You should talk to refugees of Dorwinion and the Chayasír in their camps in the hills to the east of Dale."},
[11560]={"Talons at the Talan","Prepare to defend Talan Revail","The crebain have been driven off","Cúvroval is at Talan Revail.\
\
You should speak with Cúvroval regarding the craban-attack on Talan Revail.","'Alas, it has been long since I laid eyes upon the Great Eagles of the Misty Mountains, whose ancestors served the Elder King in ages past.\
\
Lo, what is that? Do you see that black cloud approaching? Ai-oi! It is a flock of crebain from the west descending upon us.\
\
'Please lend me your aid in driving them off!'","Talk to Cúvroval at Talan Revail","'Excellent work, my friend! You are welcome to stand at my shoulder any day.'","'The crebain are descending even now! Stand by my side, and we shall drive them off!'","Cúvroval is at Talan Revail.\
\
A flock of crebain is descending upon Talan Revail from the West. Cúvroval has asked you to help defend the talan and drive the crows off!","Cúvroval wants you to help her defend flet against an incursion of angry crows."},
[11562]={"Se pueden encontrar enredaderas amargas, hierba fétida y brotes de tejo silvestre en el norte del Bosque Salvaje.\
\
Mantoespino te ha pedido que te encargues de algunos problemas botánicos en el bosque.","Apaciguamiento del Bosque Salvaje","Un Ent furioso bloquea el paso al Bosque Salvaje, pero se le podría convencer, con algo de persuasión, para que deje entrar en el bosque a los habitantes de Puente de Caballetes.","Enredaderas amargas destruidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Destruye los brotes de tejo silvestre (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Juuum, jum. ¿Has conseguido arrancar solo las plantas y árboles que te indiqué? Parece que tienes buen ojo, ${PLAYERNAME:pequeño[m]|pequeña[f]}. Enseñaré a tu gente qué pueden retirar sin dañar el bosque'.","'Los Elfos me llaman Egfinnel, aunque en la lengua de los Hombres soy Mantoespino. Poco he viajado por este bosque, pero mucho he visto que me inquieta.\
\
'El Bosque Salvaje se ha vuelto demasiado salvaje. Plantas y árboles que no deberían estar en esta zona dificultan el crecimiento de los que sí deberían, juuum. Limpia las enredaderas amargas, la hierba fétida y los brotes de tejo silvestre, y pensaré en dejar pasar a la gente del pueblo'.","Habla con Mantoespino","Mantoespino se encuentra en la parte central del Bosque Salvaje.\
\
Deberías ir a hablar con Mantoespino.","Brotes de tejo silvestre destruidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'El Bosque Salvaje ha estado abandonado durante demasiado tiempo'.","Destruye las enredaderas amargas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Hierba fétida destruida (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Destruye la hierba fétida (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[11564]={"Acompaña a Bersi fuera de la guarida de las arañas, defendiéndolo de ellas.","Habla con Bersi","Atrapado en la telaraña","'¡Por favor, ayúdame a escapar de estas horribles arañas! Estaba recogiendo hierbas y no me di cuenta de que me estaban acechando. ¡He estado atrapado aquí durante días!'","Has encontrado a Bersi de Gondamon, que fue a recoger hierbas cerca de una guarida de arañas y se encontró atrapado.","Has rescatado a Bersi"},
[11565]={"'Tengo un asunto de gran pesar, ${PLAYER}. Muchos de nuestros más valientes compañeros han caído en la lucha contra los orcos que descienden por los pasos desde el Norte, y deseamos honrar sus hazañas, tanto por ellos como por el ánimo de quienes inevitablemente deberán alzar su estandarte y marchar a morir en su lugar.\
\
'Tu habilidad es tal que quiero pedirte que tejas un tapiz que relate los hechos de nuestros héroes, para ejemplificar la vida y la muerte de quienes luchan bajo la enseña de Esteldín, de modo que sean recordados en épocas más pacíficas por venir.'","'Tantos han caído, y sus historias y canciones solo son conocidas por unos pocos. ¿Tendrías el corazón para tejer otro tapiz que conserve sus vidas y hazañas para quienes vengan después?'","Tapiz de las Hazañas — Introducción","Techeron está en Esteldín, en las Quebradas del Norte.\
\
Techeron te ha pedido que tejas un tapiz que relate las hazañas de los caídos, para alentar a quienes aún permanecen.","Teje un Tapiz de las Hazañas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Entrega el Tapiz de las Hazañas a Techeron en Esteldín","Muchos de los Montaraces de Esteldín han caído en la guerra contra Angmar, y el ánimo de quienes quedan se ve amenazado.","'Este tapiz, finamente tejido y glorioso en sus relatos de valor, servirá muy bien a nuestros propósitos. ¡Quién pudiera algún día estar junto a aquellos espíritus valientes cuyas historias aquí se narran!\
\
'Te doy las gracias, ${PLAYER}. Tu habilidad en estas labores no tiene igual, y los Montaraces de Esteldín te quedan en deuda.'"},
[11567]={"Derrota Maestros de Combate Tarkrîp (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Aventurarse en lo profundo de Nan Wathren te ha revelado razas incluso más fuertes de orcos Tarkrîp.","Derrota Tarkrîp enfurecidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Aventurarse en lo profundo de Nan Wathren te ha revelado razas incluso más fuertes de orcos Tarkrîp.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Se recomienda una Comunidad.</rgb>","Orcos Tarkrîp fortalecidos","Has derrotado a Tiradores de Élite Tarkrîp (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los Tarkrîp enfurecidos, Tiradores de Élite Tarkrîp y Maestros de Combate Tarkrîp se encuentran en el centro de Nan Wathren.\
\
Debes derrotar varios de estos violentos orcos en Nan Wathren.","Has respondido al desafío de los luchadores Tarkrîp en el centro de Nan Wathren, venciendo a estos terribles enemigos.","Has derrotado a los Tarkrîp enfurecidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota a Tiradores de Élite Tarkrîp (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Completado","Maestros de Combate Tarkrîp derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[11568]={"'We can count ourselves lucky that most of the Corsairs in Tarlang's Crown do not seem to be any different than the others on the coast.\
\
'They still go far out of their way to secure more ale, and they keep much of it nearby even in times of war. If you were to destroy their stores, I am certain they would descend into chaos and begin to fight amongst themselves.\
\
'Be wary of how simple this may sound, ${PLAYER}, for the Corsairs are not ones to leave their barrels unguarded.'","Barrels of ale can be found throughout Tarlang's Crown, especially near Corsair tents.\
\
Elaglar has asked you to destroy barrels of ale in Tarlang's Crown in hopes that it will throw the Corsairs into disarray.","Elaglar can be found in Dol Amroth.\
\
You have destroyed many barrels of Corsair ale, and should report your success to Elaglar.","Destroyed barrels of ale in Tarlang's Crown (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","DNT -- will not be seen","Destroy barrels of ale in Tarlang's Crown (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Elaglar","Tarlang's Crown - A Dangerous Thirst","'I am certain it will be a long time before we can deprive them of all of their ale, but this ought to rile them up for some time.\
\
'I would much rather they fight amongst themselves over what little remains than take the fight to us!'","The Corsairs of Umbar have stocked Tarlang's Crown with ale that could easily be turned against them."},
[11569]={"In the wake of numerous thefts in Blackroot Vale, many supplies have been ferried downriver into Tarlang's Crown.","Tarlang's Crown - Carried Downriver","'Thank you for bringing these to me, ${PLAYER}. I shall see them returned to Blackroot Vale at once.\
\
'If the Corsairs seek to steal more for their needs, I will know to call on you again.'","Elaglar can be found in Dol Amroth.\
\
You have retrieved many stolen barrels from Tarlang's Crown and should deliver them to Elaglar.","'Based on what we have learned of the Corsair presence in Blackroot Vale and Belfalas, they seem to enjoy ferrying their supplies downriver. You mentioned that in Blackroot Vale, they sneakily stole goods away and sent them down the Blackroot.\
\
'The time has come for us to reclaim what was stolen, ${PLAYER}. Travel to Tarlang's Crown and recover the barrels taken from Blackroot Vale by the Enemy.\
\
'Be prepared to move carefully or gather your allies before you depart, ${PLAYER}.'","Recover stolen barrels from Tarlang's Crown (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Barrels can be found throughout Tarlang's Crown and the river Blackroot.\
\
Elaglar has asked you to recover barrels stolen from Blackroot Vale in Tarlang's Crown.","DNT -- will not be seen","Deliver the stolen barrels to Elaglar"},
[11570]={"Corsairs can be found throughout Tarlang's Crown.\
\
Elaglar has asked you to thin the numbers of the Corsair forces in Tarlang's Crown.","Elaglar can be found in Dol Amroth.\
\
You have slain many Corsairs and should now report to Elaglar.","Defeated Corsairs in Tarlang's Crown (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Corsairs of Umbar work in service of The Scourge and his ally, Azruthor, in Tarlang's Crown and present a constant threat to the people of Gondor.","Defeat Corsairs in Tarlang's Crown (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'We have heard that The Scourge has sent Corsair forces into Tarlang's Crown. While we are still unsure of their purpose there, I do not wish to wait to find out.\
\
'Travel to Tarlang's Crown and defeat the Corsairs there. However, I would not go alone if I were you... you would do well to gather your allies before setting off!'","DNT -- will not be seen","Talk to Elaglar","'Their numbers may recover in time, but you have dealt them a harsh blow this day!'","Tarlang's Crown - Servants of the Heirs"},
[11571]={"Defeated darkwater in Tarlang's Crown (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The Enemy is bold to summon our own rivers into battle against us, ${PLAYER}. Thank you for quieting the waters of the Blackroot once more.'","'My scouts have told me that vile things have been seen in Tarlang's Crown. The water of the Blackroot itself has risen against us and serves only to strengthen the already considerable forces there.\
\
'If the water can be returned to the river, perhaps we can then mount a more successful assault on The Scourge's forces.'","Swelling from the waters of the Blackroot, darkwaters now wander Tarlang's Crown in service of the Heirs of Castamir.","DNT -- will not be seen","Darkwater can be found in and along the river Blackroot throughout Tarlang's Crown.\
\
Elaglar has asked you to venture to Tarlang's Crown and defeat the darkwater under the thrall of the Heirs of Castamir.","Defeat darkwater in Tarlang's Crown (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Elaglar","Tarlang's Crown - Waters of the Blackroot","Elaglar can be found in Dol Amroth.\
\
You have defeated darkwater lurking in Tarlang's Crown and should report to Elaglar."},
[11572]={"Tarea: Fichas de Heroísmo","Reúne Fichas de Heroísmo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lleva Fichas de Heroísmo al viajero curtido","Fichas de Heroísmo reunidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","El viajero curtido te ha llevado a una vía peligrosa a través de la Tierra Media. Representa a una facción de montaraces que guían a quienes desean recorrer las Vías del Valor.\
\
A medida que luches contra enemigos por los campos y montañas de la Tierra Media, es posible que encuentres alguna que otra Ficha de Heroísmo tras tus victorias.\
\
El viajero curtido se ha ofrecido a recibir estas Fichas de Heroísmo a cambio de mejorar tu reputación en las Vías del Valor.","'Veo que has regresado con las Fichas de Heroísmo que te pedí.'","Reúne Fichas de Heroísmo en tus batallas por toda la Tierra Media.","'Tráeme Fichas de Heroísmo de tus batallas por los parajes de la Tierra Media y me encargaré de que recibas una recompensa acorde.'"},
[11573]={"Reúne Fichas de Heroísmo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lleva Fichas de Heroísmo al viajero curtido","Fichas de Heroísmo reunidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","El viajero curtido te ha llevado a una vía peligrosa a través de la Tierra Media. Representa a una facción de montaraces que guían a quienes desean recorrer las Vías del Valor.\
