[11818]={"Dufrig is in the brenin's hall in Lhanuch.\
\
You should speak with Dufrig to enter the brenin's hall and observe the deliberations of the Council of Brehur.","'You must earn the trust of the brehur, if you wish to secure the safety of your friends.'","The brehur of Lhanuch are in the brenin's hall in Lhanuch.\
\
Dufrig has told you to earn the favour of the brehur of Lhanuch before Glynn Brenin's council comes to a decision on whether to bow to the demands of Isengard.","'Your presence here is no mystery to me, Duvodiad. Our village is caught between powers. On one hand, we have the emissaries of Saruman the White, who demand our fealty in battles to come, while the Duvodiad of the North once again tresspass unwanted upon our lands.\
\
'Glynn Brenin will soon hold council to decide our course. We have no love for the Men of the North, but we are not blind...we see what is happening to our brethren in Dunland. They will serve Isengard as pawns in the war to come, and many will never see their homes again. Yet if we refuse, we may come to blows with our own kinsmen, or the savage half-orcs who serve under the banner of the White Hand. I cannot say which would be worse.\
\
'Know that Glynn Brenin's mind is not yet resolved in this matter, Duvodiad. Prove your worth to the brehur, and he may yet find the will to reject the entreaties of Isengard. Otherwise, I suspect that your wandering friends will soon be hunted down by Saruman's armies, and our Men-folk shall march to war in the South, to what fate, I know not.'","Complete 'Signs Among the Ashes'","Convince Glynn Brenin to reject the emissary's demands","The chieftains of Nan Laeglin will soon hold a council under Glynn Brenin to decide how to treat with the emissaries of Isengard and the passage of the Grey Company through Enedwaith.","Complete 'A Weapon of Old'","'The Council of Brehur has begun its deliberations...do you wish to watch them?'","The Brenin's Council","Complete 'The Half-orcs'","Complete 'Where There is Smoke....'"},
[11819]={"Examina el quinto puente","Examina el segundo puente","'¡Has regresado! ¿Qué has encontrado?'","Este puente está en buen estado","Las tablas de este puente están desgastadas por el tiempo","Examina el cuarto puente","¡Las tablas de este puente se ven bien!","Examina el sexto puente","Durante generaciones, la familia Gochelgar ha estado encargada del cuidado de los puentes de Glyn Helyg.","Esta tabla está podrida y necesita ser reemplazada","Examina el primer puente","¡Este puente sería una gran trampa! Debería repararse primero","Informa de vuelta a Ponta","'¡Saludos! Soy Ponta Gochelgar. Durante generaciones, mi familia ha estado a cargo del mantenimiento de los puentes de Glyn Helyg. Es un trabajo muy importante, pues una tabla de puente podrida podría desmoronarse bajo el peso de un pie o una pezuña.\
\
'Es cerca de esta época del año cuando necesito hacer una inspección completa de cada puente, pero he estado sintiéndome bastante mal estos últimos días. Si estás dispuesto a subir y bajar por ahí, podría compensarte por el trabajo si me ayudas.\
\
'¡Maravilloso! Lo primero que debemos hacer es examinar los puentes para asegurarnos de que las cuerdas, las tablas y los puntos de anclaje estén en perfectas condiciones.'","Ponta Gochelgar te ha pedido que examines los puentes de Glyn Helyg en busca de signos de podredumbre y desgaste.\
\
Los puentes cruzan los tramos entre los acantilados de Glyn Helyg.","Deberías informar a Ponta sobre el estado de los puentes\
\
Ponta Gochelgar está en Glyn Helyg","Examina el tercer puente","Los Puentes de Glyn Helyg","Las tablas están firmes y seguras"},
[11820]={"Speak with Katâl outside the caves of Hurum Kâna. Hurum Kâna can be found in Kighân to the north of Zajâna, just off the Great Road.","Speak with Katâl outside Hurum Kâna","'Yes, I know of this Bârlat. Quickly, quickly, off the road and I would have words with you.'","The Brigand King","'There is a brigand on the Great Road, one self-styled brigand king, that I would have words with you about.\
\
'He calls himself Bârlat the bold, 'Brigand King of Hurum Kâna'. He has claimed the areas south and west of Zajâna as his 'kingdom'. He has been harassing and attacking travellers on the road for supposed taxes. This obviously cannot be allowed to continue. He is little more than an organized ruffian, despite his delusions of grandeur.\
\
'There is a merchant who frequently travels through that area, Katâl, who has asked for our aid in defeating this Bârlat and bringing peace to the Great Road. \
\
'Will you meet with Katâl?'","Doorward Azagâya has requested your aid in defeating a self-styled brigand king, Barlat the Bold. He makes his home in the caves of Hurum Kâna."},
[11821]={"Discover the camp of Thama Aklam","Thama Aklam has become home to a number of brigands, many of whom are bored and hope for a fight worthy of their skills.\
\
Defeat brigands in Thama Aklam.","Approach the camp at Thama Aklam to determine possible goings on.","Defeat brigand leaders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","As you approach the brigand camp, you begin to hear rumblings of frustration and discontentment.\
\
'It's been days since we had a good scrap,' you hear one complain.\
\
Perhaps you could satiate their boredom with a light scuffle or twelve.","Thama Aklam has become home to a number of brigands.","Defeated brigand leaders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated brigands in Thama Aklam (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have defeated many brigands in Thama Aklam.","You have tussled with many bandits. Perhaps they will be less inclined to start trouble along the road.","Defeat brigands in Thama Aklam (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Completado","The Brigands of Thama Aklam"},
[11822]={"The brigands of Eastmund's Lair in the northern Wold are of a hostile nature, and pose a threat to the upstanding folk of Langhold.\
\
You should defeat many brigands in an effort to drive them out.","Brigands have returned to the Wold after having been recently driven across the Great River.","Tell Dala of the brigand encampment that has emerged to the south-west","Find the small band of brigands who robbed the farmer","Defeat brigands at Eastmund's Lair (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The farmer indicated that the brigands may have wandered south-west from his farm after robbing him.\
\
You should find the small band of brigands who robbed the farmer at dawn.","The brigands in the northern Wold seems overly confident despite their recent banishment by Utred and the Riders of Langhold.","This outpost is much more worrisome than a mere band of robbers....","'A huge encampment of brigands, you say? This was no ordinary night raid, then....\
\
'Thank you for taking such a great risk in venturing into the fray, ${PLAYER}. I am sorry I chided you earlier and made light your courage. I think we must tell Thane Utred of this threat at once.'","Dala can be found at the north gate of Langhold.\
\
You should return to Dala.","Defeated a brigand (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Brigands of the Wold"},
[11823]={"'¿Por qué vienes a este lugar?'","Othran se encuentra en Tyrn Lhuig, el campamento de cazadores en la esquina suroeste de Malenhad, al este de Fasach-larran.\
\
Taraghlan te ha pedido que lleves las provisiones a su pariente Othran en el campamento de cazadores de Malenhad.","'¿Traes provisiones de parte de Taraghlan? Eso es bueno, porque las nuestras se estaban acabando. Tyrn Lhuig tiene algunos de los mejores cazadores de los Trev Gallorg, pero ningún hombre puede cazar sin provisiones.'","Taraghlan te habló de un campamento de cazadores llamado Tyrn Lhuig, que se encuentra en el extremo suroeste del gran pantano de Malenhad.","Lleva las provisiones a Othran","Los pantanos de azufre","'¡Ya has hecho grandes cosas por los Trev Gallorg, ${PLAYER}, y sé que harás aún más! Nuestros parientes lejanos aún no han tenido el beneficio de tu amistad, y me entristece por ellos.\
\
'Persiguen a sus presas en el gran pantano de Malenhad, al este de Fasach-larran. Es un lugar peligroso, sombreado por nubes venenosas y húmedo con agua sucia, hogar de extrañas bestias. Nuestros cazadores nos traen mucha comida y otras cosas de valor de Malenhad, pero necesitamos enviarles suministros para que puedan hacer su trabajo.\
\
'Lleva estos bienes a Othran en Tyrn Lhuig, el campamento de caza en la esquina suroeste del pantano. Encontrarás desafíos de caza allí para ti, si estás ${PLAYER:preparado[m]|preparada[f]}.'","'Lleva esas provisiones a Othran en Tyrn Lhuig, el campamento de caza en la esquina suroeste de Malenhad. Los cazadores las necesitarán.\
\
'El gran pantano de Malenhad se encuentra al este de Fasach-larran. No tendrás dificultad para encontrarlo si sigues tu olfato.'"},
[11824]={"Thane Torferth is in the Mead Hall of Stoke.\
\
You should speak with Thane Torferth regarding Ordlac and his treachery.","Thane Torferth is at Tordag's encampment near Torsbury.\
\
You should speak with Thane Torferth when you are ready to march upon Stoke.","Talk to Torferth to march upon Stoke","'I am proud to fight alongside you once more...Forth the Toringas!'","'I am grateful for your aid, ${PLAYER}. If you had not accompanied me, I fear that Reeve Fríthbert and his sister would have perished at Ordlac's hand. This is a terrible time, however, for Fríthbert is not yet old enough to lead the people of the Broadacres....'","'We must ride at once, ${PLAYER}, for there is little time to lose. The lives of many are at stake, not the least of which are Lúfa's and the Reeve's children's. We must take Stoke from the traitor and bring him ruin!\
\
'There is no time to spare, my friend...will you ride with the Toringas once more?'","The Broadacres Betrayed","Stoke has been freed and Reeve Fríthild's children saved from Ordlac","Talk to Torferth","At Lúfa's behest, you brought Thane Ordlac's token to Thane Torferth at Torsbury. He received it with great wrath."},
[11825]={"Benches are scattered about the park","Empty, crumbling benches line the paths of the Danakh-khêj park.","The fountains of Danakh-khêj still flow!","Danakh-khêj is in northern Clovengap.\
\
You should explore Danakh-khêj park.","Return to Gerja","Search for the park","The Broken Benches of Danakh-khêj","'So the fountains still flow? Ah, my mind wanders to what it must have been like. Dwarves of all ages, relaxing and enjoying the day, chatting together on the benches, the fountains splashing merrily. We shall return it to its glory, my friend.'","You found Danakh-khêj park!","Gerja Defthand is in north-east Clovengap.\
\
You should let Gerja Defthand know what you found in the park.","Danakh-khêj is in northern Clovengap.\
\
You should search for the ruins of the Danakh-khêj park.","Explore the park","'Have you found more locations?'","This dwarf-made memorial stone is weathered but has stood strong against time and the elements. The runes read, 'Rest well, Azagh Gamz, my fierce warrior.'\
\
Beneath the runes is a small, carved, paw-print.","'You found the vineyards! I can see them from here, now that you point out the direction. Oh how I wish I could be down among those arches!\
\
'I hear you did much to help clear them of sabre-tooth cats! Thank you, thank you ever so much!\
\
'The next location to find is Danakh-khêj. One of my ancient texts contains part of a song about meeting a beloved in a lush sward of grass under the mountain, the two gazing at the stars together. Should you find an enormous fountain, you shall know you are in the right place.'"},
[11826]={"You hear Fastred's voice echo down from the second floor","The Broken Family","'My son...my only son, taken from me under my nose! Elflád claims she had left for but a moment and upon her return Folcred was gone...\
\
'Fool guards! CAN I TRUST NO ONE?\
\
'He will not be hidden from me, and when I discover who has taken him, I will make them regret the moment they stepped into Rohan.\
\
'I have no desire to speak with you...get out of my sight!'","Upon your return to Snowbourn, you learned that Fastred discovered that his son has been taken by an unknown force. Meanwhile, you now know that Walstow faces a full-scale assault.","'This bodes ill for us, ${PLAYER}. Fastred is not himself, and our enemies beat at our door. We must aid Walstow before it is too late!'","'The tidings you bring are most... ill-timed. ${PLAYER}, Fastred's son has been taken.\
\
'We know not by whom, as Sigeric still sits in the prison, but Fastred is consumed with rage like I have never seen him.\
\
'To come between a father and son...that is truly unwise. I would not try to speak with him, but if you insist, I will not stop you.'","Talk to Fastred","Find Fastred in his home","Fastred can be found inside his home in Snowbourn.\
\
While this is not the best moment to intrude upon his time, you must warn Fastred of the coming danger.","Talk to Gísling","Gísling can be found in central Snowbourn.\
\
Since Fastred will not hear you, you should speak with Gísling.","Fastred is inside his home in Snowbourn.\
\
Despite Cynelac's warnings, you should warn Fastred of the impending attack on Walstow."},
[11827]={"Shalgoth fled to Gorthad Nûr.\
\
You should follow Shalgoth.","Defeat Broglok, overseer of Dáru Lagúrz","The Broken Houses","The broken houses of Dáru Lagúrz have been taken by the kergrim","Kergrim can be found in Rath Dúath.\
\
You should defeat kergrim in Rath Dúath and seek out Dáru Lagúrz.","Follow the path to Gorthad Nûr","As Broglok falls, his leader watches from the path to the north","Talk to Thurindol outside Gorthad Nûr","'The kergrim must congregate somewhere in the Morgul Vale. But where?\
\
'Hmmm... what if they gather at the old Gondorian burial houses that our scouts spotted when we entered the valley? I shiver at the thought of those beasts feeding on the dead, but there are likely to be many good men laid to rest in those old crypts, and the kergrim will not respect their sanctity as we would! You should head towards the charnel houses and defeat any kergrim you find on the way. I will join you when I can.'","Broglok can be found in Dáru Lagúrz.\
\
You should defeat Broglok.","The Kergrim of the Morgul Vale have taken control of the old burial houses Gondor had once constructed for Minas Ithil.","Defeated kergrim (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Seek out Dáru Lagúrz","These barrows are much older than those of Dáru Lagúrz","Derrota a los kergrim (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Stay low, my friend. I saw that fiend you chased. Shalgoth entered the tomb ahead.'","Thurindol can be found outside Gorthad Nûr.\
\
You should talk to Thurindol."},
[11828]={"The Broods of Lhingris","Collected phials of crawler ichor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect phials of spider ichor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'My friend, I have a peculiar task to ask of you....\
\
'If you would humour me, I would ask that you collect phials of ichor from the many creatures of Lhingris. Spiders, gredbyg, crawlers, and even the carrion-flies are all of interest to me.\
\
'I have grown more unsettled the deeper we pass into these lands, and I wish to examine the ichor of its creatures more closely.\
\
'Return to me when you have gathered as much as you can bear!'","'Ah, that will do. Thank you, my friend.'\
\
Legolas begins to inspect each phial of ichor you recovered and does so for some time. All of a sudden, a wave of horror washes over his face.\
\
'${PLAYER}... this... this cannot be!\
\
'Each phial of ichor you have collected is of the same source... they are all of Shelob's brood! Every single spider and every single insect in Lhingris is another of her twisted children!\
\
'Lhingris itself writhes with her essence!'","Collect phials of carrion-fly ichor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Ichor can be harvested from various creatures in Lhingris.\
\
Legolas has asked you to gather ichor from the many insects and spiders of Lhingris.","Collect phials of crawler ichor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Deliver the phials of ichor to Legolas near Dath Nethryn","Collected phials of spider ichor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Legolas can be found beside the road above the swamps of Dath Nethryn.\
\
You have gathered a great deal of ichor from the creatures of Lhingris and should now return to Legolas.","After exploring much of Lhingris, Legolas has become unnerved by similarities he has noticed in the many creatures and insects of the Ephel Dúath.","Collected phials of carrion-fly ichor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected phials of grodbog ichor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect phials of grodbog ichor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[11829]={"Defeat Guldur Brutes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated Guldur Brutes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Brutes of Sammath Gûl","Sammath Gûl, a tower deep within Dol Guldur, is in the Eastern reaches of southern Mirkwood.\
\
Naerdolen has asked you to enter Sammath Gûl and defeat many Guldur Brutes.","Naerdolen has asked you to go into Sammath Gûl and destroy the protective Black Uruks that attempt to stop all intruders."},
[11830]={"'${PLAYER}, I believe word of Gazathrug's death has reached the hobgoblins in the Pit of Stonejaws. They demonstrate a renewed resolve and send their brutes to test us at the Steepset. The hobgoblins even construct vile wards to denote their expansion into Máttugard.\
\
'We must defeat these hobgoblin brutes and destroy their wards at once. If we are not swift, then the hobgoblins will believe us to be weak, and move to crush us!'","Hobgoblin brutes have ventured out from the Pit of Stonejaws and into Máttugard.","Destroy hobgoblin wards (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Voina","Destroyed hobgoblin wards (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Voina can be found at Zidir-nesad, the Steepset, in Máttugard.\
\
You should talk to Voina.","Defeat hobgoblin brutes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Brutes of Stonejaws","Hobgoblin brutes and hobgoblin wards can be found in western Máttugard.\
\
You should defeat hobgoblin brutes and destroy their wards.","'You have done well, but we cannot celebrate our victory just yet. I have received some new information from a scout: it concerns the Angmarim.'","Defeated hobgoblin brutes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[11831]={"'Ah, so Éowyn believes it enough aid to send you here...how thoughtful of her.\
\
'As the warriors and my husband are away, if you wish to be put to work, I have no shortage of it for you.'","Éowyn seeks to ready her people to travel south to Dunharrow, but the path through the Harrowdale must be prepared before their travels can begin.","'When we are prepared, the path my people must take to Dunharrow is through the Harrowdale. I have sent several of my men through the valley already, and they work even now to ensure that a suitable camp is prepared for those who travel to Dunharrow.\
\
'Ellen Fremedon holds Underharrow along our path, and I have already sent word to ready supplies and beds for our passing. She is not fond of me, of this I am sure, but I cannot help but make demands in such dire times.\
\
'If you would aid her, perhaps that will assuage some of her frustration and allow us to depart sooner.'","The Burdens of Underharrow","DNT -- Will not be seen","Talk to Ellen Fremedon in Underharrow","Ellen Fremedon can be found outside the Mead Hall of Underharrow in the Harrowdale.\
\
Éowyn has asked that you aid Ellen Fremedon in preparing for the people of Kingstead as they journey to Dunharrow."},
[11832]={"Recover buried coins (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Return to Húrwen","'Are you going down to my farm, Elbery? I am Húrwen, and yes, it is mine, but alas it's completely overrun with goblins. I came back to see if they'd moved on, but the wretched things are still there. I wonder if you could help me. When word came that goblins were sighted in the area, my father... well, you see, he's got a troubled mind and I'm afraid he took all the money in our coffers and buried it about the property in an effort to \\qkeep it safe.\\q\
\
'I know I'm taking a big risk here, asking a stranger to recover it for me, but you're my only hope of getting back my coin before the goblins start wondering what's under the freshly dug earth.\
\
'Please, bring me back any coin you find, and I'll give you a share of it in return.'","Recovered buried coins (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","From a hill overlooking a large farm, a woman waits for help recovering her stolen coin.","'You actually did it! I saw you taking on those wretches too. I had a good feeling about you - glad am I that I trusted my gut! Give them here then, and I shall be sure to keep them away from my dear addled Father.'","The Buried Treasure of Elbery","Húrwen has asked you to search for sacks of coin that her father secreted about her farm.\
\
Elbery Farm is located in north-western Pinnath Gelin.","You have recovered multiple sacks of coins from Elbery Farm.\
\
You should bring the sacks of coin to Húrwen, who is waiting on the road west of Elbery, in Pinnath Gelin."},
[11833]={"The Buried Truth","'I do not wish to be here. I am bound by my captor and cannot leave until freed.\
\
'My captor hides away inside a crypt in the middle of Lake Isingmere, south of here. Go seek him out and defeat him, so that I may finally leave this place.\
\
'In order to call him forth, you'll need to open my casket, which is deep within the crypt.'","Defeat the captor Daegul located deep within the crypt","The captor Daegul has been defeated.","Locate the crypt in the middle of Lake Isingmere","The captor Daegul is not pleased that it has been disturbed.","Open the wailing Daegul's casket deep within the crypt","The wailing Daegul is bound to this location and cannot leave until it is freed by defeating its captor located within an island crypt.","Now that the captor Daegul has been defeated, the wailing Daegul will no longer be bound to the lighthouse.","'Thank you for freeing me. I am no longer bound to this place, therefore I will not be a nuisance to anyone. Best of luck along your journey.'","Speak with the wailing Daegul","You have located the crypt on Lake Isingmere.","Enter the crypt and look for the the wailing Daegul's casket located deep within.","You have opened the casket of the wailing Daegul. The captor appears to find out who is disturbing its rest.","Head to the island in the middle of Lake Isingmere and find the crypt located there."},
[11834]={"'¿Has visto a las criaturas llamadas salamandras? Parecen un tipo de sierpe, pero al mismo tiempo es como si fueran un tipo de criatura totalmente diferente. No las había visto en Evendim hasta hace poco, cuando Tyl Ruinen, la isla del lado oeste del lago, se infestó con estas criaturas. De noche, la isla parece estar ardiendo por las llamas que provocan estas extrañas bestias.\
\
'También se ha visto un buen número de salamandras en Barandalf, al sureste de Tinnudir... ¿podría ser que están extendiéndose? Aventúrate a Tyl Ruinen, si así lo deseas, y descubre el origen de esta plata de salamandras.\
\
'Hay unas ruinas en el centro de la isla llamadas Tollobel. Quizá allí haya alguna pista del origen de las salamadras.'","'¿Salamandras? ¿Por qué me preguntas sobre salamandras? ¡A mí, de entre todo el mundo! ¿Por qué debería un pobre sabio errante como Hunfredo Rebuscón saber algo de ellas? De hecho, ni sé qué es una salamandra. Nunca he oído hablar de ellas.\
\
'¡Ja! Te había engañado, ¿eh? Pensabas que todo era culpa de Hunfredo Rebuscón, ¿no? ¿No? Pero ahora ya lo sabes, yo no sé nada. Nada de nada. Al menos, nada sobre las salamandras.\
\
'Espera un momento. Esto no tiene sentido. ¿Quién diría algo así? Hunfredo Rebuscón es un gran sabio, ¿sabes? ¡Sé dónde está todo el conocimiento! Así que algo debo saber sobre salamandras. Pero, ¿qué? Esa es la pregunta. Una buena pregunta.'","Investiga Tyl Ruinen","'¡Hay salamandras en Tyl Ruinen, ${PLAYER}, y debemos averiguar por qué! Tyl Ruinen está en la orilla oeste del lago... ¡un largo trecho nadando desde aquí!\
\
'Hay unas ruinas llamadas Tollobel en el centro de Tyl Ruinen. Ahí es donde deberías comenzar a buscar.'","Multitud de extrañas criaturas han empezado a aparecer en Evendim, entre las que destacan las temibles salamandras.","La isla ardiente","'¡Por favor, vuelve a Tyl Ruinen para resolver el misterio de las salamandras!'","La isla de Tyl Ruinen en el lado oeste del lago, enfrente de Tinnudir, está infestada de salamandras.\
\
Calatherdir te ha pedido que viajes hasta Tyl Ruinen y a las ruinas de Tollobel para investigar el origen de las salamandras."},
[11835]={"Return to Candúr with the obsidian ore.","Gather obsidian ore (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Burning Mountain: Black Fire","Gathered obsidian ore (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I thank you. We should be able to trade this precious ore for more suitable building materials.'","Gather obsidian ore","Mineral riches await those who brave the perilous cliff road circling Mount Doom.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Warning: This quest requires The Burning Mountain: Blood Wings to be underway. If that quest has been completed or failed, you will be unable to exit and re-enter this instance in order to complete this quest.</rgb>","Gather obsidian ore.","Bring the obsidian ore to Candúr"},
[11836]={"The Burning Mountain: Blood Wings","You ran out of time...","Defeat The Blood-blade.","Talk to Candúr","You should return to Candúr and apprise him of your efforts.","'Atop the perilous peak of Mount Doom is a neglected road. There may be mineral riches to be had on this path, though the journey there is not an easy one. If we are to construct a new watch over this realm, we will need the hardened minerals of the mountain. Are you willing to take on this task?'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Warning: This quest has a one hour time limit. The timer will begin upon accepting the quest. This quest can be completed with one or two adventurers.</rgb>","'Careful now on your journeys.'","'You have slain a high ranking lieutenant of Seregost? I praise you for your valiant efforts.'","Defeat The Blood-blade","Defeated The Blood-blade","Mineral riches await those who brave the perilous cliff road circling Mount Doom.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Warning: This quest has a one hour time limit. The timer will begin upon accepting the quest.</rgb>"},
[11837]={"'You have done well, friend. Your efforts will be duly noted!'","Defeated Merrevail (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You should return to Candúr and inform him of your deeds on Mount Doom.","Defeat Merrevail on Mount Doom (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat Merrevail on Mount Doom","Talk to Candúr","Defeat Merrevail on Mount Doom.","Mineral riches await those who brave the perilous cliff road circling Mount Doom.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Warning: This quest requires The Burning Mountain: Blood Wings to be underway. If that quest has been completed or failed, you will be unable to exit and re-enter this instance in order to complete this quest.</rgb>","The Burning Mountain: Red Skies"},
[11838]={"Talk to Ingold","Habla con Gimli","Few have braved beyond the borders of Udûn","Travel to the Ruins of Díngarth in Dor Amarth","Gimli and Ingold can be found at the Ruins of Díngarth in Dor Amarth.\
\
When you have completed all you wish to do in Udûn you should speak to Gimli and Ingold.","The Ruins of Díngarth is located near Udûn in Dor Amarth.\
\
You should travel to the Ruins of Díngarth.","'We have managed to push through Udûn with only a small resistance. Now the task before us is to see what remains of Sauron's citadel, Barad-dûr. I am glad you are with us.'","'You have been a great help, in the wake of Lachír's folly. You have helped lead us to conquer what resistance and pitfalls we have encountered here in Mordor.\
\
'Some of our company has pressed through, past the gates of Carach Angren, and into Dor Amarth. When you have accomplished all that you wish to do here with us in Udûn, those in Dor Amarth could use your aid.'","When you have completed all you wish to do in Udûn you should speak to Gimli and Ingold about Dor Amarth.","The Burning Plains of Dor Amarth","'It is good to be in the thick of things again, isn't it ${PLAYER}. It was odd to see dwarves in Udûn. I did not realize any lived in Mordor! Do you suppose there are more of my lost kin in these lands?'"},
[11840]={"Legolas is waiting for you in Echad Taerdim, the Ranger camp in Cirith Ungol.\
\
You should talk to Legolas.","The Straight Stair marks the start of your journey into Cirith Ungol.\
\
You can find it through a pass just behind Halhir, who is stationed along the Morgul-road.","'Greetings, ${PLAYER}. It gladdens me to see a friendly face on the road! Legolas has asked for you. He is waiting at Mablung's camp just ahead. To reach it, just take this pass behind me and head up the Straight Stair. Be warned, if you are headed into Cirith Ungol, there will be many stairs and steep climbs in your future! And, of course, there's the spiders. Many, many spiders.'\
\
He shivers at the thought, and bids you farewell.","Find the Straight Stair","The Straight Stair climbs into the heights","'Good to see you again, ${PLAYER}! I am afraid I have little time to catch up. We have come to a dangerous place, and there is much to be done. I can share what information I have.\
\
'There is very little spider presence on the west side of Cirith Ungol, which does not surprise me as we believe they are mainly coming from Torech Ungol itself. However, we have found one puzzling thing for which I have no explanation: in several places, we have found sets of footprints—alike that of Men both in shape and size—that seem to disappear mid-stride! The others are speculating that they sprouted wings and flew! I am not sure I believe that, but it is certainly worth looking into. See if you can find some of these footprints to the north-west.'","The Business of Spiders","Talk to Mablung","Talk to Gladhir","Legolas has come to Cirith Ungol to address some unfinished business. What has become of Shelob, her brood, the Mirkwood spiders, and the tower of Cirith Ungol?","Talk to Mírthel","Echad Taerdim, the Ranger camp in Cirith Ungol under command of Mablung, can be found at the top of the Straight Stair.\
\
You should travel to Echad Taerdim.","Legolas can be found at Echad Taerdim, the Ranger camp in Cirith Ungol.\
\
You should talk to Legolas.","'Greetings, ${PLAYER}! How have you fared since the Battle of the Black Gate? I have done some scouting myself, and can tell you what I saw.\
\
'The spider presence is dense to the east, as expected. They continuously flow out of Torech Ungol like a foul stream. Among them are also several horrible varieties of gredbyg. None of this is surprising, but in the north-east I found a forest completely overwhelmed by webs, and a large brood of spiders that seemed to be separating themselves from the ones in Torech Ungol. Make of that what you will!'","'Welcome to Cirith Ungol, ${PLAYER}. I have much unfinished business to manage here, and I would appreciate the help of a skilled and trusted friend such as you.\
\
'When we last left the tower of Cirith Ungol, it was besieged by spiders; if the Gúrzyul failed to reinforce the garrison, the tower might fall to the spiders, and that would unleash the spiders upon Gorgoroth, and perhaps the larger world! I have heard no reports of spider activity beyond Lhingris, so perhaps the Orcs prevailed. We will have to investigate.\
\
'There is also the matter of the Mirkwood spiders. When my father faced our old enemy Iphantamel, she said that all of her daughters had left her. We suspect that they may have come here, at the call of their true mother.\
\
'Finally, we must discover if Ungwetári yet lives. As valiant as Master Samwise is, I do not believe she would have succumbed to such a small wound, though it was inflicted by a courageous heart. She is ancient and powerful.\
\
'There is much to do. We should begin by questioning the Rangers of Ithilien. They have begun scouting the area, and may already have some answers to our many questions.'","Legolas waves to you as you approach the camp","You relay to Legolas all of the information the Rangers shared with you.\
\
'Interesting. I am glad to have such skilled Rangers at our disposal. They have saved us a great deal of time.'\
\
Legolas' attention briefly drifts away as he considers all you have said.\
\
'Several mysteries now need to be unravelled. Why did the Uruk-hai pass this way? Did they come from the city or somewhere else? If they were headed to the tower, does that mean the pass from the east is no longer accessible to them? What are these spiders that sequester themselves from the others? What do these strange footprints mean, where Men can suddenly disappear mid-stride? We have much to consider, and much ground to cover.'","Find Echad Taerdim","'Greetings, ${PLAYER}. How have you fared since our last meeting? I am certainly glad for the help of Legolas and yourself. You are among the most skilled ${CLASS}s I have ever met.\
\
'Our goal in Cirith Ungol is to try to establish a knowledge of any threats to Ithilien that may still exist in this place. Specifically, where the spider presence is, their numbers, and if the Orcs have any forces here. Indeed, despite Shelob's apparent defeat, we have already established that the spiders linger still. As of yet, we have found no evidence of Shelob herself, living or dead, but have found many of her brood.\
\
'We know not the situation in the tower. I sent some Rangers to approach as close as they could to it, which is not especially close, for the path is treacherous and spider-infested. They reported they could detect little Orc activity on this side of the tower. I do not know if they have simply moved the garrison closer to Dor Amarth, or if they have abandoned the tower entirely.\
\
'We also noticed when we set up camp here that someone, likely an uruk based on the size of the prints, had passed this way very recently, heading east toward the tower. Mírthel and Gladhir may have more information for you.'","Habla con Legolas.","Legolas believes the first course of action is to gather information from the Rangers of Ithilien stationed at Echad Taerdim.\
\
You should talk to Mablung, Mírthel, and Gladhir."},
[11842]={"Follow Fastred's trail of slaughtered Orcs","Its legs slashed, this Orc looks to have attempted to flee before being run down","Talk to Fastred","As you explore, you notice a Rohirrim caked in black blood standing in the distance","Another slaughtered Orc lays at your feet. This one appears to have had two blades thrust through its skull","'While you were dealing with the guards, I learned from the townsfolk where Fastred often travels to hunt the Orcs of the Sutcrofts.\
\
'He is usually near his father's grave, just past the river to the east. If you can find him, convince him to return to Snowbourn. There are surely more pressing matters for his people than the deaths of a few more Orcs.'","Gísling recommends setting out to the east of Snowbourn in search of Fastred or any Orcs that he has slain in his wake.\
\
Gísling suggests that you try to find Fastred in the field and persuade him to return to Snowbourn.","Below you, an Orc lays brutally slain and dismembered... perhaps you have found Fastred's trail","Follow Fastred's trail outside of Snowbourn","The Butcher of Snowbourn","Black blood still pours from the neck of this recently beheaded Orc... Fastred must be nearby","'Aye? Can you not see that I am busy?'\
\
Fastred pulls his blade from the corpse of an Orc at his feet.\
\
'So... Gísil has failed to hold Garsfeld, and the forces in the north intend to wipe us out?\
\
'They will try, but they cannot succeed. I will fight to see every last bit of Orc-filth on these fields purged. It is only by your good fortune that I have had my fill of Orc-bloodshed for today, so yes, I will return to Snowbourn.\
\
'We can speak more in the Mead Hall... for now, leave me to my work.'","Fastred can be found near Dagred's grave to the west and slightly north of Snowbourn.\
\
You should deliver Gísling's message to Fastred.","You have followed Fastred's trail of slaughter far into the Sutcrofts. He must be nearby.\
\
You should search for Fastred.","Find Fastred","Gísling has discovered where Fastred routinely hunts the Orcs of the Sutcrofts on his own."},
[11843]={"The Uch-lûth were greatly displeased by the gift of meat presented to them, for they suspect the Grey Company of slaughtering their herds.","'Perhaps I was hasty in my judgement. These cuts were carefully taken from the carcass of a dead animal...our oxen which were slaughtered were gored, their meat ruined.\
\
'Perhaps if you could help us discover what creature has been hunting our herds, we will consider trading with your friends. There is a legend which tells of a great black boar the likes of which has not been seen west of the Mountains in many long ages. It is said it may be the mate or descendant of the Boar of Everholt. Perhaps the Black Sow is responsible for this slaughter.\
\
'Will you accept my offer? If so, look to our herd there to the north-east beneath the foothills. Almost nightly a beast or two has been slain.'","This ox does indeed appear to have been slain by a great boar","'You believe it is indeed the Black Sow that hunts our herds? The beast must then be slain, for it is too dangerous to be permitted to wander these lands.'","'So the Black Sow was indeed more than just a legend? Your deed then was heroic and worthy of song...even for a duvodiad, a stranger.'","'I wonder if the Black Sow is the inspiration for the Turch-gwirod which our cousins among the Turch-lûth worshipped?'","Defeat the Black Sow of the Windfells","Defeated the Black Sow of the Windfells","'Have you determined what creature it is that hunts our herds?'","The Black Sow wanders the wilds of the Windfells.\
\
Having determined that a great boar did indeed slay the oxen of the Uch-lûth, you should hunt down the Black Sow of the Windfells.","Alun is at Uch Cadlus in the Windfells of Enedwaith.\
\
You should return to Alun with news of your success.","'We are grateful to you for ridding us of the Black Sow!'","The Butchered Herd","There may be dead oxen among the herds of the Uch-lûth at Uch Cadlus in the Windfells.\
\
Alun has asked you to examine the dead oxen among the herds of the Uch-lûth to determine what may have slain them.","Examine slaughtered oxen (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Talk to Alun at Uch Cadlus"},
[11844]={"El Cairn de Honor","Arzhur ha regresado a Aughaire. Debes llevarle la piedra que recuperaste y prepararte para el próximo desafío.","Obtén una piedra del Cairn de Honor","El Cairn de Honor está en el centro de Fasach-Falroid, al norte de Aughaire. Se encuentra en la cima de una alta colina, al oeste del camino norte, y de noche el sendero está iluminado por antorchas.\
\
Arzhur te ha pedido que obtengas una piedra del Cairn de Honor. No debes derramar sangre de los montañeses que patrullan la zona.","'Otro desafío se ha presentado ante nosotros. De nuevo, necesitamos un símbolo de honor antes de poder luchar. Esta vez, me temo que la ley de los clanes está en nuestra contra, ya que ha habido una disputa sobre tu participación en el último desafío. Si queremos liberarnos de este lío, deberás luchar solo esta vez.\
\
Primero, necesitamos una piedra del Cairn de Honor. El Cairn está en Fasach-Falroid al norte, en territorio de los clanes hostiles, y sus exploradores y guerreros tienen derecho, según la ley de los clanes, a defender su tierra. Sin embargo, no debes derramar sangre de estos montañeses al obtener la piedra, o la piedra quedará manchada con deuda de sangre.\
\
Así que debo pedirte que viajes al norte hasta el Cairn, ¡y que no mates a ninguno de nuestros enemigos, aunque te ataquen! Encontrarás el Cairn en la cima de una alta colina al oeste del camino norte, y de noche el sendero está iluminado por antorchas.'","Evita matar a los montañeses","Tomas una piedra del Cairn de Honor","Otro desafío fue enviado al clan de Arzhur. Antes de aceptar el desafío, debe presentarse otro símbolo de honor.","'Debes obtener una piedra del Cairn de Honor.'","'Bien hecho. Ahora es momento de luchar una vez más.'","Lleva la piedra del Cairn a Arzhur","Has matado a un montañés: ¡Misión fallida!"},
[11845]={"Talk to Halhir","Legolas has asked that you come to Cirith Ungol when you are able to assist him with some unfinished business.","'${PLAYER}, Legolas has requested your assistance with a matter of great importance in Cirith Ungol. I was asked to send you his way, if you are able. Mablung and a few others have set up camp somewhere in the cliffs, but I do not know how to find the camp myself. Halhir should be stationed on the Morgul-road in that area; just follow it west and you should come across him eventually. He should be able to direct you further.'","Halhir can be found somewhere along the Morgul-road, somewhere to the west.\
\
You should find Halhir.","Halhir waves as you travel down the road. He smiles as you approach.\
\
'Greetings, ${PLAYER}! I see Legolas's call has reached you!'","The Call of Cirith Ungol"},
[11846]={"Took rubbings of the ancient pillars (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Call of Our Fathers","Take rubbings of the ancient pillars (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'These rubbings will be added to our fine library. The knowledge discovered will no longer be in danger of being lost like many precious things that once resided within our ancient halls.'","'Among the old ruins of our home, there are a series of pillars near the entrances to the halls. These pillars are etched with ancient runes. These runes are fine examples of our craftsmanship in this area, and the knowledge contained on these pillars cannot be replaced.\
\
'Will you find these pillars and take rubbings of the runes, so that this knowledge may be passed down to our future generations?\
\
'The rune-pillars are located among the ruins in the southern hills of Thrór's Coomb.'","Frithgeir is at Zudrugund within Nár's Peak, north of the ruins, through the mountain pass.\
\
You should return to Frithgeir and present him with the rubbings of these pillars.","The ruins on the southern hills lie to the south of Nár's Peak, through the mountain pass.\
\
Frithgeir has asked you to seek out the ruined pillars among the ancient dwarf-ruins and take rubbings of the runes found upon them.","'There is much knowledge in these ruins which must not be lost.'","Talk to Frithgeir at Zudrugund","Among the ruins in the southern reaches of Thrór's Coomb, several pillars with rune-carvings still stand. The messages on the pillars may speak of lost knowledge and should be recovered."},
[11847]={"Se han reportado desapariciones de marineros en las Islas Escudo del norte. Investiga las islas y descubre qué les está sucediendo a estos marineros.","'¡Qué historias tan increíbles cuentas! Bueno, deberíamos apresurarnos antes de que más cantos nos hechicen a ambos. ¡De vuelta a Umbar!'","Acechadores de sirenas derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota a las asesinas de sirenas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota a Sadâjah la Cruel","Derrota a los acechadores de sirenas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Asesinas de sirenas derrotadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","¡Escapa de la isla!","Investiga la isla","El Llamado del Mar"},
[11848]={"La biblioteca de los Grandes Smials está en el pueblo de Alforzaburgo, al este de Cavada Grande.\
\
No habiéndole inspirado tu informe sobre la deliciosa comida a la venta en el mercado, Bingo piensa que quizá un libro de cocina le dé la inspiración que necesita.","'Que tengas un buen día, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}. Si tienes un momento, ¿crees que podría robarte un ratito? Me llamo Bingo, de los Boffin de los Campos de Cavada. Es bastante raro ver a gente nueva en el camino que pasa por mi casa. ¡Es un placer conocerte!\
\
'Verás, me he sentido un poco solo estos días, y un evento festivo en el horizonte me daría un empujoncito y ocuparía mis pensamientos. ¿Quizás organizar una cena serviría? ¡Sí, es una idea excelente! Invitaré a mis vecinos, ¡y a ti también, por supuesto!\
\
'¿Podrías ir al mercado de Cavada Grande y echar un vistazo a los productos? Dime qué comida parece particularmente deliciosa, ¡y eso quizá encienda la chispa de la inspiración para uno o tres platos que servir a los invitados!\
\
'El mercado está al sur de mi agujero hobbit.'","La Casa de los Mathoms de Cavada Grande está en una colina al suroeste del agujero hobbit de Bingo Boffin.\
\
Bingo te ha pedido que lleves el mapa que cayó del libro de recetas de la biblioteca a la Casa de los Mathoms en Cavada Grande. No lo quiere.","'¡Esto servirá perfectamente, ${PLAYER}, gracias!'\
\
Bingo toma el libro de cocina y empieza a hojearlo, cuando un pergamino doblado cae de entre las páginas. El curioso hobbit lo recoge y lo desdobla.\
\
'¿Qué es esto? ¡Anda, si es un mapa! Alguien se ha olvidado un mapa en este libro de recetas, ${PLAYER}. Quebradas de los Túmulos... Colinas de los Vientos... Claro de los Trolls de Piedra... ¡mira estos pequeños dibujos! ¿Crees que son lugares reales?\
\
'¡Bah! ¡No puedo dejar que me mente divague! ¡Tengo una cena que planear! ¡Lleva el mapa a la Casa de los Mathoms, ${PLAYER}! No lo necesito, ¡y no lo quiero!'","'No hay día que no pueda alegrarse con una sabrosa comida compartida con amigos. Cualquiera de los libros de recetas de la estantería detrás de mí será suficiente, ¡te lo garantizo!'","'¿Podrías ir rápidamente al mercado de Cavada Grande y echar un vistazo a los productos? Dime qué comida parece particularmente deliciosa, ¡y quizá eso encienda la chispa de la inspiración para uno o tres platos que servir en mi fiesta!\
\
'El mercado está al sur de mi agujero hobbit.'","'Ah, me llevará algo tiempo recuperarme de ese ejercicio. ¡Nunca había corrido tan rápido en toda mi vida, ${PLAYER}! Y aun así, estoy más emocionado que nunca. ¡Una aventura! ¡Será justo lo que necesito! Pero me llevará algunos preparativos, eso seguro. ¡Necesitaré tu ayuda para prepararme para este viaje!'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Busca a Bert Bartolín cerca de los establos de Cavada Grande para canjear insignias de Bingo por recompensas.</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>La semana que viene: 'Entrenando para el viaje' (Nivel recomendado: 9)</rgb>","Donnamira te sonríe y escribe tu nombre en un trozo de pergamino","Bingo Boffin está fuera de su agujero hobbit, al norte del mercado de Cavada Grande, al otro lado del Agujero Municipal.\
\
Has juzgado la calidad de algunos productos del mercado de Cavada Grande, y ahora debes informar a Bingo Boffin.","El mercado de Cavada grande está al sur del agujero hobbit de Bingo.\
\
Bingo Boffin ha decidido organizar una cena para sus vecinos para aliviar un poco su soledad, y quiere que eches un vistazo a la comida disponible en el mercado. Espera que eso le inspire para saber qué platos servir a sus invitados.","'¡Me quedaré con el mapa, ${PLAYER}, y lo usaré para planear mi aventura! ¡Volvamos a mi agujero hobbit, hay mucho que hacer!'","Las patatas estarían muy bien cocidas, en puré o estofadas","'Hay una biblioteca en los Grandes Smials de Alforzaburgo. ¿Te importaría mucho hacer un pequeño viaje a la biblioteca para mirar un libro de recetas por mí? Quizá entre sus páginas encontremos algunas buenas ideas sobre qué puedo servir.'","Bingo ha subido corriendo la colina a la Casa de los Mathoms a una velocidad de vértigo, y ahora está exhausto. ¿Que puede querer?","Lleva el libro de recetas a Bingo, en el exterior de su agujero hobbit","Bingo Boffin disfruta de una vida pacífica en su agujero hobbit en Cavada Grande, pero se siente solo y quiere más actividad para sus días.","Bingo está fuera de su agujero hobbit en Cavada Grande, justo al norte del Agujero Municipal.\
\
Has tomado prestado un buen libro de recetas de la biblioteca de los Grandes Smials y debes llevárselo a Bingo.","El pastel huele maravillosamente... pero pertenece a Hugo","Vuelve con Bingo y dale tu informe","Bingo te ha pedido que te reúnas con él de nuevo fuera de su agujero hobbit al noreste de la Casa de los Mathoms, al norte del Agujero Municipal.\
\
El mapa dibujado a mano que encontraste ha inspirado a Bingo, aunque no para organizar una cena. En vez de eso, ¡quiere irse de aventuras!","'¡No puedo dejar que mi mente divague! ¡Tengo una cena que planear! ¡Lleva el mapa a la Casa de los Mathoms, ${PLAYER}! No lo necesito, ¡y no lo quiero!","Juzga la calidad de la comida disponible en el mercado de Cavada Grande (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","La selección de verduras luce apetitosa","'¿Y bien? ¿Alguno de los productos del mercado te ha llamado la atención, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
Bingo escucha tu informe de que todo parecía delicioso.\
\
'Eso es tanto una cosa maravillosa como una lástima, ¡porque me lo pone muy difícil para decidir qué servir en la cena! Necesito más que solo una lista de ingredientes, supongo. ¡Necesito un libro de recetas!\
\
'Hay una biblioteca en los Grandes Smials, en Alforzaburgo. ¿Te importaría hacer un pequeño viaje a la librería para mirar un libro de recetas por mí?  Quizá en sus páginas encontremos algunas buenas ideas sobre qué servir.'","'¡Pues ya estaría listo, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]} amante de los libros! ¡Gracias por tu confianza y apoyar a tu biblioteca local!'","Bingo recoge el mapa y lo mira con entusiasmo","La llamada de la aventura","Bingo ha subido corriendo la colina tras de ti, y parece exhausto","Viaja a la biblioteca de los Grandes Smials, en Alforzaburgo, y habla con la bibliotecaria","Las manzanas parecen casi maduras, firmes y deliciosas","Revisa uno de los libros de recetas que se encuentran detrás de Donnamira Tuk","'¿Sí? ¿Puedo ayudarte a encontrar algo en particular?'\
\
Le dices a Donnamira que estás buscando un libro de recetas para preparar cenas refinadas, y su cara se ilumina.\
\
'¡Muy bien, muy bien! No hay día que no pueda alegrarse con una sabrosa comida compartida con amigos. Cualquiera de los libros de recetas de la estantería detrás de mí bastarán, ¡te lo garantizo!'","Habla con Bingo en el camino que sube a la colina de la Casa de los Mathoms","Habla con Bingo Boffin fuera de su agujero hobbit","Donnamira Tuk, la bibliotecaria de los Grandes Smials, te ha recomendado un libro de recetas de la estantería que se encuentra detrás de ella.","'¡La mayoría de la gente que trae cosas a la Casa de los Mathoms no están tan dispuestos a quedárselas! Quizá Bingo sea una excepción a la regla. ¡Nunca había visto al señor Boffin correr tanto, se ha quedado sin aliento!'","Lleva el mapa al conservador Brombard Colazorro, en la Casa de los Mathoms","'¿Tienes un objeto que no quieres sin sitio donde ponerlo, pero no quieres tirarlo? Dámelo, y me aseguraré de ponerlo con los otros mathoms del mismo tipo que aquí conservamos.'\
\
Brombard extiende su mano para recibir el mapa, pero algo llama su atención y se detiene.\
\
'¡Quizá he hablado demasiado rápido! Parece que alguien reclama este mathom después de todo, ¡y ha corrido a toda prisa para recuperarlo!'","'¡He cambiado de idea, ${PLAYER}, he cambiado de idea! ¡No quiero que ese mapa acumule polvo en la Casa de los Mathoms! ¡Quiero saber más de los lugares que representa!\
\
'¡Quiero caminar por las Colinas de los Vientos, bastón de caminar en mano! Quiero cruzar el Último Puente, ¡y ver qué hay más allá! Quiero ver Rivendel... ¿de verdad hay Elfos allí?\
\
'¡Me quedaré con el mapa, ${PLAYER}, y lo usaré para planear mi aventura! ¡Volvamos a mi agujero hobbit, hay mucho que hacer!'"},
[11849]={"Klúso is startled as you approach, but he manages to slap a hand over his mouth before he can make a sound.\
\
'Oh, ${PLAYER}, it's just you! I thought I was about to catch an Orc-dagger in my back! Hahaha... give me a moment to calm my heart!\
\
'So Ausma sent you to get my report, hmm? Well, she was right that this is where the hobgoblins receive messages from elsewhere in Gundabad. Because of that, this camp has drawn the attention of spies, and I don't mean us! Ausma didn't specifically tell me not to do this so... I have an idea. You could do a lot of damage to the hobgoblins if you attack this camp, and because of the suspicion present on both sides, the warlord might assume it was the Orcs doing the backstabbing and not us dwarves! What do you say to that? Smart, eh?'","Klúso has been sent to investigate the hobgoblin out-camp called Stazg Vozag.","Talk to Klúso","Klúso needs your help.","'Great work out there, ${PLAYER}. I'll run around and place these Orc-swords before returning to camp, completing the ruse. I think we might actually pull this off! What do you have there?'\
\
You show Klúso the orders you found in the out-camp.\
\
'Hmm, you'd better bring those to Ausma right away.'","Complete 'Storming Stazg Vozag'","Complete 'Sentries from the Out-camp'","The Camps of Stazg Vozag","Find Klúso","'Klúso has been sent to keep watch on Stazg Vozag, the hobgoblin out-camp. We know this is where runners from elsewhere in Gundabad deliver their missives and receive their marching orders, rather than entering Shakhajât itself. It seems the warlord takes his precautions very seriously. You should meet up with Klúso and hear what he has discovered.'","Klúso is east of Out-camp Stazg Vozag, spying on the hobgoblins.\
\
You should find Klúso and help him however you can.","Complete 'Enemy Intelligence'","Complete 'Swords in the Shadows'","By order of Warlord Dushtalbúk,\
\
All raids on the Angmarim settlements are to cease immediately. The Frost-bound and the Cult of Drugoth are negotiating a deal. Anyone who has a problem with this should report to Loknashra at their own risk!","Find information about Loknashra","Klúso is east of Out-camp Stazg Vozag, spying on the hobgoblins."},
[11850]={"El Cabo de Belfalas","Visit the Cathlond, the cape docks","'So, my new friend, what do you think of the Cape of Belfalas? Is it not the most relaxing place in all of Gondor - nay, of Middle-earth?'","Falastír, the friendly lighthouse keeper of the Cape of Belfalas, has agreed to show you around the coast.","This is certainly the largest house you have seen in quite some time","Esta casa es muy impresionante","Visit one of the standard sized houses on the Cape","The house is stately and large","'The Cape of Belfalas is under rule of Dol Amroth and it has been this way since I can remember. Not that I have been to the city in many a long year. Ha, that is how it goes sometimes, I reckon!\
\
'Some prefer the view from this rock or that hill, but in truth there is hardly a spot to stand in the Cape of Belfalas that does not show a lovely sight! You should explore and see it for yourself. I know you will enjoy every moment! Be sure to visit the stage, the docks, and either of the islands!'","Visit the Court of Anglind","Nothing better than being so close to the water","The view of Tolfalas is impressive","Visit one of the largest houses on the Cape","Falastír wants you to see the sites of the Cape of Belfalas.","Falastír is located at the lighthouse on the Cape of Belfalas.\
\
You should let Falastír know that you have toured the Cape as he suggested.","Visit the interior of Narvindon","The sounds and sights of the shore are refreshing","Take a boat to one of the islands off the coast","The old man is happy to know you have seen the sights","Habla con Falastír","You admire the craftsmanship of the lighthouse","Visit one of the smaller houses on the Cape"},
[11851]={"'Thank you, ${PLAYER}, for all that you have done. The farmers and merchants of Tadrent shall always remember you. We should be able to resume shipping much-needed provisions to Dol Amroth soon.\
\
'The corsairs are planning something in Edhellond and I'm certain the other two captains you seek reside to the west.'","You have defeated Tabadam","Tabadam can be found at the corsair camp Makham Mijann.\
\
Find and confront Tabadam at Makham Mijann.","Speak with Bruidis in the village of Tadrent","Bruidis can be found in the village of Tadrent.\
\
You should report back to Bruidis and inform her of Tabadam's defeat.","Find and confront Tabadam at Makham Mijann","'Rossaran once told me that to cut the vein tying the head to the chest is to bleed the enemy dry. I believe that Captain Tabadam of Makham Mijann is that vein, and you, ${PLAYER}, are the blade.\
\
'As much as we need to investigate Edhellond, first you should enter Makham Mijann, find the captain in the camp, and defeat him. Tabadam is surely one of the corsair captains your friend Jajax spoke ill against.\
\
'Be careful, ${PLAYER}.'","Now that Bruidis understands Captain Tabadam's plans, she has asked you to enter Makham Mijann, defeat him, and bring the camp to its knees.","The Captain of Makham Mijann"},
[11852]={"Habla con Inufileg en Gwingris","'Gracias a vuestros esfuerzos, los dunlendinos ya no deberían suponer una amenaza para nosotros.'","'Mis exploradores me dicen que el cuerno de batalla de los dunlendinos se encuentra justo al otro lado del estanque, al este de Gwingris, en Sâd Rechu. Comienza tu búsqueda allí.'","Tudur derrotado","Inufileg está en Gwingris, al oeste de Sâd Rechu.\
\
Debes regresar a Gwingris y contarle a Inufileg sobre tu éxito.","Usa el cuerno de batalla para invocar a Tudur y derrotarlo","El cuerno de batalla está en el campamento al este del estanque en Sâd Rechu, al este de Gwingris.\
\
Inufileg te ha indicado que uses el cuerno de batalla de los dunlendinos para desafiar a su líder, Tudur.","'Bien hecho de nuevo, ${PLAYER}. Con su líder desaparecido, no dudo que los dunlendinos pronto regresarán a sus aldeas en el sur.\
\
'Te has ganado la gratitud tanto de elfos como de árboles hoy, ${PLAYER}. Gracias.'","El capitán de Sâd Rechu","'Nuestros exploradores han informado que los pocos dunlendinos que quedan han logrado reforzar su campamento maderero. Aparentemente, tienen un cuerno de batalla con el que pueden llamar a su líder, un hombre llamado Tudur.\
\
'Regresa al campamento dunlendino, ${PLAYER}, y mira al este del estanque. Busca su cuerno de batalla y úsalo para desafiar a Tudur. Cuando llegue, derrótalo... tal vez entonces los dunlendinos regresen a su propia tierra.\
\
'Date prisa, ${PLAYER}, antes de que Saruman pueda reforzar el campamento.'","Los dunlendinos han establecido un campamento maderero en la zona boscosa de Sâd Rechu, donde recolectan madera para uso de los lacayos de Saruman."},
[11855]={"The Caravan to Snowbourn","'We have made it, ${PLAYER}. Thanks in no small part to you.\
\
'I can only hope that my father and his men will hold Garsfeld in the days to come....'","Talk to Gísil","Pressured by foes from all sides, Gísil has prepared the crofters of Garsfeld to journey to the south and seek shelter within Snowbourn.","Gísling can be found in northern Snowbourn.\
\
You have successfully brought the crofters of Garsfeld to safety inside the walls of Snowbourn and should now speak to Gísling.","Gísil can be found inside the Mead Hall of Garsfeld.\
\
Gísil has ordered you and Gísling to escort the people of Garsfeld to safety in the south. He is waiting for you to make any final preparations.","Talk to Gísling","'The preparations have been made, ${PLAYER}. My people make ready as we speak.\
\
'They must reach the safety of Snowbourn, for no other place in the Sutcrofts will keep them from harm. The Reeve of the Sutcrofts, Fastred, is a brash young man, but a caring leader... he will not suffer the deaths of his people if they could easily be saved by our actions.\
\
'I cannot thank you enough for the aid you have provided me and my people. It is unfortunate that our paths must split, but it is my duty to hold Garsfeld to my last. When you are ready to depart, speak with me. Time grows short.'","'Gísling has gathered the crofters. Are you ready to depart?'"},
[11857]={"Hendrevail derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","El maullido del gato","La guarida abandonada debería estar al norte del refugio del cazador, cerca de las piedras erguidas.\
\
Thrasi se lastimó la pierna al rescatar a un lince herido de los hendrevail y te pidió que recuperaras a los cachorros sobrevivientes.","'Es bueno ver a una madre y a su cría reunidas, aunque sean de cuatro patas.'","Saca al cachorro de lince de su guarida","'¡Ja ja ja... me está lamiendo la cara!'","Derrota a los hendrevail (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Saca al cachorro de lince de su guarida.\
\
Con los hendrevail derrotados, el cachorro de lince parece sentirse lo suficientemente seguro como para salir de su guarida.","'No está lejos de aquí. Camina hacia el norte hasta las antiguas piedras erguidas. La guarida está en la ladera de una colina.'","Lleva al cachorro de lince a Thrasi","'Los linces crían a sus crías en guaridas o madrigueras pequeñas, especialmente en las abandonadas por otros animales.'","Busca en la antigua guarida de osos","Con palabras tranquilizadoras logras que el cachorro asustado salga de la seguridad de su guarida.","Thrasi, un cazador enano, rescató a una madre lince mientras cazaba osos. Fue atacado por una bandada de hendrevail y tuvo que dejar atrás a los cachorros de la madre.","'¡Qué precioso cachorro! Déjame quitártelo y... ¡ay! ¡Deja de arañar! Tiene mucho temperamento, ¿no? ¿O será una hembra?\
\
Pobrecito. Lástima que sus hermanos de camada no lo hayan pasado tan bien, pero así son las cosas. Mmm... ahora me está mordisqueando la barba. ¿Quizás el peque tenga hambre?'","'¿Qué me pasó? Estaba cazando osos cuando me encontré con esta madre lince y sus cachorros. La pobre había sido brutalmente atacada por unos hendrevail, y apenas pude agarrarla antes de que vinieran por mí. Me torcí el tobillo terriblemente, pero sanará, al igual que esta vieja gata.\
\
Dejó una camada atrás, pero los dos estamos demasiado magullados para salvar a los cachorros nosotros mismos. Me sentiría fatal si les pasara algo, pero no sirvo de nada hasta que mi tobillo sane.\
\
¿Podrías aventurarte hasta la guarida junto a las piedras erguidas al norte y traer de regreso a cualquiera de los cachorros que hayan sobrevivido? Te lo agradecería, y estoy seguro de que la madre también lo estaría.''","Hay hendrevail por todo el bosque.\
\
Un cachorro de lince asustado se acurruca en una vieja guarida, demasiado asustado para aventurarse a salir a la luz. Debes derrotar a los hendrevail que merodean cerca para demostrar que no les quieres hacer daño.","'¡Mira esas patas! Este será un cazador temible cuando alcance su tamaño adulto.'","Asomas la cabeza en la antigua guarida de osos y oyes el maullido lastimero de un cachorro de lince hambriento y asustado.\
\
El pobre tiene miedo de salir de la seguridad de la guarida, por temor a ser atacado por los hendrevail.","El cachorro de lince sale de su guarida","Thrasi está de regreso en el refugio del cazador, al sur de aquí.\
\
Recuperaste al cachorro de lince como Thrasi lo solicitó. Entrégaselo en el refugio del cazador."},
[11858]={"Oflár cree que el Caldero de la Muerte se encuentra cerca del lago central de Imlad Balchorth.","'¡Has hecho un trabajo excelente! ¡Realmente excelente! Mereces todo el elogio que pueda darte, junto con las pequeñas recompensas que pueda ofrecer. Pero temo que nuestro trabajo en Imlad Balchorth aún no ha terminado...'","Encuentra el Caldero de la Muerte.","Has derrotado al guardián del Caldero.","Derrota al guardián del Caldero.","'Debes abrirte camino hasta el Caldero de la Muerte y destruir cualquier criatura maligna que lo custodie.'","El Caldero de la Muerte y su guardián se encuentran frente al lago central de Imlad Balchorth, al oeste de Myrkworth.\
\
Oflár te ha pedido que luches hasta el Caldero de la Muerte y destruyas a su guardián. Sugirió que reunieras aliados.","Oflár se encuentra en Myrkworth, al este del Caldero de la Muerte.\
\
Con el gigante de hierro destruido, el Caldero de la Muerte ha dejado de vomitar tumularios... al menos por ahora. Debes regresar y informar a Oflár de tu éxito.","El Caldero de la Muerte","'Te he pedido que te aventures en el peligro suficiente hasta ahora. Pero creo que debo pedirte que enfrentes un riesgo aún mayor. De hecho, pienso que esto es demasiado pedirle a un solo aventurero, por valiente que sea, así que te pediría que reúnas aliados a tu lado.\
\
'Este Caldero de la Muerte... he oído historias sobre él contadas por los montañeses del oeste. Se dice que un cadáver puede ser sumergido en él, y de él surge un tumulario. Debe ser una especie de máquina de muerte, el lugar del que emergen todos estos temibles tumularios para atormentar la tierra.\
\
'Estoy seguro de que encontrarás muchos defensores en el corazón de Imlad Balchorth. Abre paso a través de la malvada multitud, encuentra el Caldero y destruye cualquier monstruosidad que encuentres custodiándolo.'","Has encontrado el Caldero de la Muerte."},
[11859]={"Igerna has been found alive, but injured and captive. Her freedom must be gained, but the door to her rusted metal cage sits firmly locked.","'Freedom! Thank you, my new friend. I have been trapped in there for days.'","Talk to Igerna","Retrieve the key to Igerna's cage","Igerna has asked you to find the key to her cage. She suggests the overseers may be the ones to carry the keys.\
\
Goblin overseers can be found throughout the cave and in Krauzhaf, in Pinnath Gelin.","After battling through the halls of Krauzhaf, you recovered an iron key that looks like it will fit the lock on Igerna's cage door.\
\
You should unlock Igerna's cage, in the cave at Krauzhaf, in Pinnath Gelin.","Unlock Igerna's cage","You have unlocked Igerna's cave, and she is now waiting to speak with you.\
\
Igerna is in a cave in Krauzhaf, in northern Pinnath Gelin.","'If I could, I would hug you, but the door to my cage is locked tight. I have only seen it unlocked with keys the overseers have. Hunt them down until you find the key.'","The Cave, the Cage, the Key","This goblin had the key!"},
[11860]={"Destroy the shadow torches in Kidzul-kâlah's depths (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Destroyed many shadow runes in Kidzul-kâlah's depths.","Destroyed shadow runes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Destroy the shadow runes in Kidzul-kâlah's depths (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Shadow runes and torches can be found within Kidzul-kâlah's depths.\
\
You should destroy the shadow runes and torches that you find.","Shadows haunt the ruins of Kidzul-kâlah. The darkness has set in to even the old statues and obelisks that decorate the aqueducts of the dwarf-made water-house. The shadow must be purged from these old ruins if exploration is to continue.","The Chambers of Kidzul-kâlah","You have destroyed the mysterious shadow runes that plague Kidzul-kâlah's depths. In return you have made the interior of Kidzul-kâlah safer to explore. Varthmath will be pleased with your efforts.","Destroyed shadow torch (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Completado","Enter Kidzul-kâlah","Shadows haunt the ruins of Kidzul-kâlah and must be purged."},
[11861]={"La Campeona de Minas Agar","Informa a Lindir.","Lindir tradujo el texto que encontraste de la Lengua Negra al Oestron.","'Los Angmarim son guerreros feroces y sin piedad, pero respetan una muestra de fuerza. Derrotaste a su campeona en combate, y nunca olvidarán esto.'","Invoca y derrota al Campeón de Minas Agar.","Lindir está en la Sala del Fuego en Rivendel, en el Bosque de los Trolls, muy al sur.\
\
Viajaste a Minas Agar y llamaste a su campeón. Tras una dura batalla, lo derrotaste. Deberías regresar con Lindir para informarle de tu victoria.","Minas Agar se alza en el lado occidental de Barad Gularan, al sur de Gath Forthnír.\
\
Debes viajar a Barad Gularan y lanzar un desafío a los Angmarin dentro de Minas Agar.","'Ese texto que tienes debería invocar a la campeona Angmarin.'","'El texto que recuperaste hablaba de una mujer malvada entre los Montañeses que traicionó a su tribu para servir al Falso Rey. Ahora habita en Minas Agar, comandando a los Angmarim que juran lealtad a la Corona de Hierro.\
\
'¿Es esto una leyenda antigua o son palabras verdaderas? No puedo decirlo, pero los siervos de Mordirith son numerosos y poderosos... no dudo de estas afirmaciones.\
\
'Deberías investigar el asunto. Regresa a Minas Agar y golpea sus puertas. Si esa campeona legendaria existe, sería imprudente de su parte ignorar tal desafío.'"},
[11862]={"'El texto que recuperaste hablaba de la traición de los barbiluengos por parte de los Duramano, y de un campeón que sobrevivió a la muerte de su señor, el pálido enano llamado Skorgrím.\
\
'Recuerdo aquel día oscuro, pero ¿es este campeón malvado parte de una leyenda? No puedo decirlo, pero los siervos de Mordirith son numerosos y poderosos... no dudo de estas afirmaciones.\
\
'Deberías investigar el asunto. Regresa a Minas Angos y golpea sus puertas. Si ese campeón legendario existe, sería imprudente de su parte ignorar tal desafío.'","Informa a Lindir.","Lindir está en la Sala del Fuego en Rivendel, en el Bosque de los Trolls, muy al sur.\
\
Viajaste a Minas Angos y llamaste a su campeón. Tras una dura batalla, lo derrotaste. Deberías regresar con Lindir para informarle de tu victoria.","Lindir tradujo el texto que encontraste de la Lengua Negra al Oestron.","El Campeón de Minas Angos","'Ese texto que tienes debería invocar al campeón duramano.'","Invoca y derrota al Campeón de Minas Angos.","Minas Angos se alza en el lado occidental de Barad Gularan, al sur de Gath Forthnír.\
\
Debes viajar a Barad Gularan y lanzar un desafío a los Enanos Malvados dentro de Minas Angos.","'He luchado codo a codo con nuestros aliados enanos, y puedo dar fe de su destreza en combate. Que hayas enfrentado a un campeón de los Duramano y sobrevivido es una hazaña asombrosa, y una que esos traicioneros villanos no olvidarán pronto.'"},
[11863]={"'Ese texto que tienes debería invocar al campeón Orco.'","Informa a Lindir.","El Campeón de Minas Caul","Lindir tradujo el texto que encontraste de la Lengua Negra al Oestron.","Invoca y derrota al Campeón de Minas Caul.","Lindir está en la Sala del Fuego en Rivendel, en el Bosque de los Trolls, muy al sur.\
\
Viajaste a Minas Caul y llamaste a su campeón. Tras una dura batalla, lo derrotaste. Deberías regresar con Lindir para informarle de tu victoria.","Minas Caul se alza en el lado occidental de Barad Gularan, al sur de Gath Forthnír.\
\
Debes viajar a Barad Gularan y lanzar un desafío a los Orcos dentro de Minas Caul.","'El texto que recuperaste hablaba de un campeón temible de Angmar, un Orco de gran fuerza que dio muerte a muchos de los míos.\
\
'¿Es esto una leyenda antigua o son palabras verdaderas? No puedo decirlo, pero los siervos de Mordirith son numerosos y poderosos... no dudo de estas afirmaciones.\
\
'Deberías investigar el asunto. Regresa a Minas Caul y golpea sus puertas. Si ese campeón legendario existe, sería imprudente de su parte ignorar tal desafío.'","'Abatir al Campeón de Minas Caul es una hazaña impresionante. Los Orcos pronto se darán cuenta de la amenaza que representas para su amo.\
\
'Celebra tu victoria, ${PLAYER}, pero no olvides el amor de los Orcos por la venganza.'"},
[11864]={"Lindir está en la Sala del Fuego en Rivendel, en el Bosque de los Trolls, muy al sur.\
\
Viajaste a Minas Maur y llamaste a su campeón. Tras una dura batalla, lo derrotaste. Deberías regresar con Lindir para informarle de tu victoria.","Informa a Lindir.","Lindir tradujo el texto que encontraste de la Lengua Negra al Oestron.","'El texto que recuperaste hablaba de un guerrero Trasgo, un campeón de Angmar que comandaba una legión de los suyos.\
\
'¿Es esto una leyenda antigua o son palabras verdaderas? No puedo decirlo, pero los siervos de Mordirith son numerosos y poderosos... no dudo de estas afirmaciones.\
\
'Deberías investigar el asunto. Regresa a Minas Maur y golpea sus puertas. Si es campeón legendario existe, sería imprudente de su parte ignorar tal desafío.'","'Ese texto que tienes debería invocar al campeón Trasgo.'","'Los Trasgos son una raza cobarde, cruel y malvada. Su campeón no era menos despreciable, pero según tu relato, parece que fue un oponente formidable.'","Minas Maur se alza en el lado occidental de Barad Gularan, al sur de Gath Forthnír.\
\
Debes viajar a Barad Gularan y lanzar un desafío a los Trasgos dentro de Minas Maur.","Invoca y derrota al Campeón de Minas Maur.","El Campeón de Minas Maur"},
[11865]={"The Champions of the Wargs","'You have done well, but new information gathered by our scouts informs us that the top two champions were not among the defeated. Unfortunately, we don't know who they are, but the scout heard goblins saying that a missive with the Wargs' names will be arriving at Dursh Hûl soon. Go grab that missive from the goblin messenger, will you? Then we shall deal with these so-called champions.'","Defeat the goblin courier","Valdi can be found in Amdân.\
\
You should talk to Valdi.","Defeat goblin-courier defender","Return to Valdi","Defeated goblin-courier defender","The goblin courier can be found on Gabilthurkhu, the Great-way, between Dursh Hûl and Kamaz-kala.\
\
Valdi has asked you to retrieve a missive from the goblin courier.","Defeated goblin courier","Recovered the champion missive","The enemy has been carefully watching the competition between the Wargs of Azanulbizar. The competition has narrowed down to two champions.","Recover the champion missive","'You have returned with the missive? Let us see what we have here.'"},
[11866]={"'We have no choice but to give chase. The Gut is filled with Jephai Corsairs meant to hinder us at every turn. We will have to pursue Khâshap into the depths of the Gut to wherever he flees. You must be prepared to deal with whatever the Jephai throw at us!'","The Chase Begins","'Everything we've done up until now has led to this moment.\
\
'The whispers around every corner are speaking of the trespasses of Khâshap.\
\
'His first mistake, he has made it publicly known that he plans to address The Gut to clear his name. It's our chance to spring the trap and capture him for good.'","The Lower Ward is bustling with chatter. The trap is set. Rumours abound that Khâshap plans to defend his honour before finally making his way to his master.","Khâshap plans to confront the rumours head on by appearing before the Gut. Hadorion believes we should spring the trap now.\
\
Meet Hadorion outside the Stonecliff Market in the Gut.","Khâshap has gathered his cohorts to clear his name. He must be stopped here and now.","Talk to Hadorion at the Stonecliff Market entrance","'It looks like the market is bustling. No doubt everyone has gathered to hear Khâshap's testimony regarding all of our allegations. Let us confront him once and for all!'","Crash Khâshap's Assembly","Khâshap has fled into the alleys of the Gut under the protection of his Jephai Corsairs. Find Hadorion at the entrance of the Stonecliff Market to discuss our next move.","'We shall stop him here! Let us make haste!'","Talk to Hadorion outside the Stonecliff Market"},
[11867]={"La Carrera de Gallinas","'¡Mira todas estas gallinas! Sin duda cumpliste con tu parte. Ahora debes recibir una recompensa.'","Cada año, los hobbits sueltan gallinas en el laberinto, y deben recogerse antes de que atraviesen los setos y se escapen hacia los campos.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000> NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro cuando finalice el festival actual.</rgb>","Ranúncula Nortuk está de pie frente a la entrada del laberinto en los Campos de Caballos.\
\
Deberías hablar con Ranúncula Nortuk y contarle todas las maravillosas cosas que lograste dentro del laberinto.","Recoge gallinas antes de que escapen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Me alegra muchísimo que hayas venido! No te imaginas la diversión que me estoy dando en el laberinto. ¡Gallinas! Oh, son encantadoras cuando corretean así por todos lados.\
\
'Si deseas participar en la carrera de gallinas, debes entrar corriendo y atraparlas antes de que escapen. La parte difícil es encontrarlas entre los pasillos del laberinto... y la otra parte difícil es encontrar la salida una vez que atrapes la tuya.\
\
'¡Ten cuidado de no perderte cuando entres! Puede ser muy complicado orientarse entre tanto follaje, ¿sabes?'","Cada hora, se sueltan gallinas dentro del laberinto de setos de Bree. Solo permanecen allí durante quince minutos de cada hora, ¡así que atrápalas mientras puedas!\
\
Debes recoger gallinas mientras corren alocadamente por el laberinto de setos.","Habla con Ranúncula Nortuk fuera del laberinto en los Campos de Caballos","Gallinas recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Asegúrate de darte prisa cuando anuncien la suelta de gallinas! No querrás que otros las atrapen todas antes de que siquiera llegues.'"},
[11869]={"Recoge la costilla del gran alce silvano de treinta puntas","Cenlieg se encuentra en Kauppa-kohta, al este de donde encontraste al alce macho.\
\
Deberías regresar con Cenlieg con la costilla de alce que hayas recogido.","El mejor corte","'Linden por fin ha recuperado el ánimo. Después de todo este tiempo, parecería que debería hacer el equipaje para viajar contigo en lugar de con mis compañeros, pero por desgracia debo ponerme en camino para reunirme con ellos.\
\
'Voy a prepararme para partir, pero antes quiero darte las gracias de todo corazón por tu ayuda, y sé que Linden también te lo agradece a su manera.'","Cazaste el alce como te pidió Cenlieg, pero el amigo oso del sabio no quedó satisfecho con la carne que le diste.","'Parece que el estómago delicado de Linden no es tan agradecido como yo por tu ayuda. Verás, es de la mejor estirpe y solo puede alimentarse de carne magra y tierna. Te prometo no volver a molestarte si tan solo puedes proporcionarle algo de comida adecuada.\
\
'He oído a los Lossoth —gente maravillosa, ya lo sabes— hablar de un inmenso alce macho que vigila el extremo sur del bosque. Sin duda, sus costillas serían fuertes y nutritivas para mi querido Linden.\
\
'Creo que lo encontrarás si viajas hacia el suroeste, al inicio de las estribaciones, justo más allá de la orilla sur.'","Lleva la costilla del gran alce silvano de treinta puntas a Cenlieg","'Linden es bastante exigente, pero si puedes traerle la carne magra que necesita, podremos continuar nuestro viaje.'","Has recogido la costilla del gran alce silvano de treinta puntas","El gran alce puede encontrarse al suroeste de Kauppa-kohta.\
\
Cenlieg te ha pedido que mates al gran alce y le lleves una de sus costillas."},
[11870]={"The Circle of Death","Talk to Candúr in Barad Arthir","Candúr can be found in Barad Arthir.\
\
You have aided Prince Faramir and secured the Circle of Death in Minas Morgul.","'You have done well, ${PLAYER}, and I hear Prince Faramir has changed his mind regarding the Dead City.\
\
'It would be a shame to let Minas Ithil fall to its final ruin by the hand of Gondor, I think. It is good he believes so as well.\
\
'These are glad tidings, but alas, there is another matter to discuss.'","Aid Prince Faramir in 'A Waxing Moon'","Complete quests in the Circle of Death (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'While you worked to secure the Circle of Despair, we worked to fortify the defences of Barad Arthir.\
\
'It is unlikely Gothmog will be able to muster enough forces to breach the walls of the tower, but I have seen more surprising things in my time. We shall remain vigilant.\
\
'After you left the tower, Prince Faramir led his company into the Circle of Death. I believe the Prince means to prepare a final assault against Gothmog, but he has kept his plans hidden... even from me.\
\
'Once you have secured the Circle of Despair, please return to me.'","You should complete quests in the Circle of Death and aid Faramir in his plans.","While you worked to secure the Circle of Despair, Prince Faramir led a company of Rangers of Ithilien into the Circle of Death."},
[11871]={"Dornach can be found in the Circle of Despair outside Barad Arthir.\
\
Candúr has asked for your aid in securing the Circle of Despair and has sent you to join Dornach's company. You should talk to Dornach.","Candúr can be found in Barad Arthir in Minas Morgul.\
\
You should talk to Candúr.","Talk to Candúr in Barad Arthir","After gaining a foothold in Barad Arthir, Prince Faramir himself has arrived to lead the Rangers of Ithilien in securing the Circle of Despair and the Circle of Death.","You should aid Dornach in securing the Circle of Despair.","El círculo de la desesperación","'It was a sorry tale Dornach told me of those who fell in the Circle of Mirth, but it heartens me to know that the Circle of Despair has been made safe.\
\
'I have received word that reinforcements are already ascending the Dead City to support our efforts in the tower.\
\
'We could not have done it without you, ${PLAYER}.'","Talk to Dornach in the Circle of Despair","Aid Dornach in securing the Circle of Despair","'Prince Faramir believes it would be ill-advised to press our attack against Gothmog from Barad Arthir. I am inclined to agree.\
\
'We may have taken the tower, but our position is precarious. The Circle of Despair has not been secured, and I dread to think what awaits us in the Circle of Death.\
\
'If we do not first hold the Circle of Despair, we may soon find ourselves surrounded... and fighting a losing battle.\
\
'To that end, Dornach has led a small company into the Circle of Despair. I would ask that you aid him as best you can.'","'You have come not a moment too soon, ${PLAYER}.'"},
[11872]={"Candúr can be found in Barad Arthir in Minas Morgul.\
\
You should talk to Candúr.","You should complete quests in the Circle of Madness in Minas Morgul.","Talk to Candúr in Barad Arthir","The Circle of Madness","Standing upon the Circle of Madness, Rhadrog believes that the merrevail invasion must contested before it is safe to continue the infiltration of Minas Morgul.","'It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}. With your help we have secured the tower of Barad Arthir.\
\
'We have both travelled a great distance since last we spoke on the blasted plains of Udûn. Faramir's return has given many of us the strength to brave the Dead City, despite the terrors that here await us! We shall persevere, and work side by side to secure both the Circle of Despair and the Circle of Death! There is much to be done.'","Complete quests in the Circle of Madness (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Enter Barad Arthir, the Lofty Watch-fort","'The Circle of Madness has been taken over by Lhaereth's forces. I can safely say we are not the only ones invading the city now! There is much to do here before we can move any further into the city.\
\
'Let us do what we can in the Circle of Madness, my friend.'","Rhadrog can be found in Barad Elenath in Minas Morgul.\
\
You should talk to Rhadrog.","Talk to Rhadrog in Barad Elenath","The entrance to Barad Arthir can be found in the Circle of Despair.\
\
You should enter the tower of Barad Arthir.","'Thank you for your assistance, ${PLAYER}. Some of the other Rangers are attempting to gain a hold further ahead in the city. Faeron and I will stay here to oversee the fight against Lhaereth's forces. We have found a nearby tower in the Circle of Despair that should lead to the Circle of Death, and the very top of the Dead City.\
\
'Seek out the tower of Barad Arthir, not far from here. Gather what you need to take hold of Barad Arthir. This will be a difficult journey. May luck be at your side, my friend!'","Complete 'Instance: Into the Circle of Despair'"},
[11873]={"The Circle of Sorrow","The entrance to Barad Elenath can be found in the Circle of Sorrow.\
\
You should enter the tower of Barad Elenath.","Complete quests in the Circle of Sorrow (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The Circle of Sorrow is nothing like what we just encountered upon the Circle of Wrath. This place is not for the living. No, it is the realm of the Dead. Streams of spirits move through the streets and strange glowing lights flicker among the old buildings. There is much here that we need accomplish before it is safe to delve further into the city.\
\
'You should assist those you can in the Circle of Sorrow. When you have done this, return to me and we shall continue our efforts.'","Enter Barad Elenath, the Star-gazers' Spire","Talk to Damrod in Barad Orhant","Damrod can be found in Barad Orhant in Minas Morgul.\
\
You should talk to Damrod.","'It is good to see you, ${PLAYER}. Thank you for helping us secure the tower of Barad Elenath.\
\
'Damrod believes my time in Agarnaith has best qualified me to deal with the threat of Lhaereth the Stained and her minions. I am glad you have also come to this Circle of Madness, though the name is ill-starred.'","You should complete quests in the Circle of Sorrow in Minas Morgul.","'You have done well to combat the Dead upon the Circle of Sorrow. I ask you now to continue upwards, further into the city. I will stay here and continue to command the Rangers in these first two circles. Our scouts have found a nearby tower that should bring us to the next level: the Circle of Madness.\
\
'Seek out the tower of Barad Elenath. We have all seen the merrevail flying above. It is certain they have already taken the next circle and the towers that stand upon it! When you are ready, prepare to take hold of Barad Elenath!'","Complete 'Instance: Into the Circle of Madness'","Rhadrog can be found in Barad Elenath in Minas Morgul.\
\
You should talk to Rhadrog.","Talk to Rhadrog in Barad Elenath","Standing upon the Circle of Sorrow, Damrod believes that there is much to do in this cursed section of the city before it is safe for the Rangers to continue their infiltration of Minas Morgul."},
[11874]={"Complete quests in the Circle of Wrath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Damrod can be found in Barad Orhant.\
\
You should talk to Damrod.","Complete 'Instance: Into the Circle of Sorrow'","Talk to Damrod in Barad Orhant","The Circle of Wrath is the lowest of the levels of Minas Morgul.\
\
You should complete quests in the Circle of Wrath.","'Our first order is to make sense of the city. While its layout is similar to Minas Tirith, we cannot mistake it for the White City! For many years, this place has suffered beneath the might of the Dark Lord and the corruption of the Witch-king.\
\
'This Circle of Wrath is but the first of many challenges we will face here. There are many Orkish forces encamped here, and we must learn what we can of them before we can safely delve further into the city.\
\
'Assist those you can in the Circle of Wrath. When you have done so, return to me and we shall continue our efforts, inward and upward.'","Damrod can be found at the tower of Barad Angarth.\
\
You should talk to Damrod.","Enter Barad Orhant, the Tower of the Treegarth","Talk to Damrod in Barad Angarth","'You have done well to assist our efforts within the Circle of Wrath. By using the various towers within the city we can conceal our presence and continue our mission, and I urge you to do the same. Our scouts have found a nearby tower that should bring you to the Circle of Sorrow.\
\
'Seek out this tower of Barad Orhant. It seems quiet and still; nothing stirs within it. But remain alert, and do not underestimate the wiles of those who dwell in Minas Morgul. Gather what is needed and take hold of Barad Orhant!'","'I thank you for leading the charge, ${PLAYER}. We have successfully secured the tower of Barad Orhant, and now I see the stillness here did not signify emptiness. No, for the Dead can be quite still indeed, when they so desire it! It is a useful lesson.\
\
'You have seen the strange glow upon this Circle, have you not?'","The Circle of Wrath","Damrod believes there is much to do in the Circle of Wrath before it is safe to continue infiltrating the Dead City.","The entrance to Barad Orhant can be found in the Circle of Wrath.\
\
You should enter the tower of Barad Orhant."},
[11875]={"La ciudad en el hielo","Viaja lejos hacia el noreste hasta encontrar Sûri-kylä, la Ciudad en el Hielo.","'¿Y bien? ¿A qué estás esperando?\
\
'Sé que los Lossoth son un pueblo difícil, ¡pero seguro que no tienes tanto miedo de la bienvenida que te darán en Sûri-kylä!'","Fotri ha accedido a darte indicaciones para llegar a la famosa capital de los Lossoth, Sûri-kylä.","Habla con Lothrandir en Sûri-kylä","'Has ayudado a todos los habitantes de Zigilgund con tus acciones, ${PLAYER}, directa e indirectamente. Te has ganado nuestra confianza y nuestra gratitud.\
\
'Me mencionaste que deseas seguir explorando las maravillas heladas de Forochel. Para eso, te recomiendo que abandones Länsi-ma y te dirijas al noreste, a la capital de los Lossoth, Sûri-kylä. Allí encontrarás a un viejo conocido mío, un montaraz llamado Lothrandir.\
\
'Es un largo viaje. Sigue el camino hacia el este desde aquí, a través de Itä-mâ, hasta que el camino gire hacia el norte. Una vez que estés en Jä-rannit llegarás a varias bifurcaciones en el camino; siempre mantente cerca del borde de la Bahía. Gira hacia el norte y luego hacia el oeste, siguiendo los colmillos de norsu.\
\
'Te deseo lo mejor, ${PLAYER}. ¡Adiós y buena suerte, dondequiera que vayas! ¡Espero que cuando vuelvas a visitarnos Zigilgund sea un lugar espléndido, y en las minas de Arrancahielo resuenen los picos y los brindis con cerveza!'","'Te doy la bienvenida, {amigo[m]|amiga[f]}. Los caminos te han conducido a Sûri-kylä, la legendaria ciudad de los Lossoth en el hielo. Entiendo que hay varias personas que necesitan ayuda.\
\
'Por ahora, descansa, come, bebe, ríe y sé {bienvenido[m]|bienvenida[f]} aquí.'"},
[11876]={"Here is a great old library, filled with ancient tomes and records of Gondor.","The Keep of the Swan-knights is in north Dol Amroth.\
\
You should make your way to the Keep of the Swan-knights.","The wharf is on the eastern side of Dol Amroth.\
\
You should make your way to the wharf.","Speak with someone in the Harper's Court","You have found the wharf of Dol Amroth","The Scholar's Quarter is in southern Dol Amroth.\
\
You should speak with someone in the Scholar's Quarter.","Inzibel's Walk is in north-east Dol Amroth.\
\
You should make your way to Inzibel's Walk.","You have found the Harper's Court","Speak with Laegened","Speak with someone in the Scholar's Quarter","The Court of the Fount is in the centre of Dol Amroth.\
\
You should speak with someone at the Court of the Fount.","'This is the finest place for a concert in all the world. Musicians come here to practice, too, so there is always music upon the air. Oh, but how I love a sweet melody!'","You have found the Mason's Court","The Artisan's Quarter is in north Dol Amroth.\
\
You should make your way to the Artisan's Quarter.","Lothíriel is in the Great Hall of the Prince.\
\
You should speak with Lothíriel.","The Scholar's Quarter is in southern Dol Amroth.\
\
You should make your way to the Scholar's Quarter.","You have found the Scholar's Quarter","'I am the master stone-mason in these parts. Only the best stoneworkers in Gondor may study under me, and most will never master the art themselves.'","'Welcome, honoured guest. Did you enjoy your tour of our fair city? It is a beautiful and peaceful place, full of art, music, and bustling markets.\
\
'Alas for the war that threatens us all. I fear that we will lose our way of life, if my father Imrahil cannot help Denethor uphold Minas Tirith against the shadow that looms in the east.'","Speak with someone in the Court of the Fount","Speak with Anírwen","The Harper's Court is in western Dol Amroth.\
\
You should make your way to the Harper's Court.","You have come to the beautiful coastal city of Dol Amroth, and the gate-guard has suggested that you tour the sights.","Anírwen is at the wharf on the east side of Dol Amroth.\
\
You should speak with Anírwen.","The City of Dol Amroth","You have found the Court of the Fount","'Welcome to the fair city of Dol Amroth, where Prince Imrahil rules. Alas that our prince has ridden to war; may he return whole and hale! Lothíriel now governs in his stead.\
\
'Dol Amroth is a great city of Gondor, and you will not see its like anywhere. Would you like a tour? Many of our folk would be happy to show you the sights.\
\
'You will find us a friendly peoples. Just walk around and you will be greeted by pleasant townsfolk.'","'Have you ever seen a finer fountain? I have lived here all my life, but I still come every day just to gaze upon it. It is the pride of Dol Amroth.\
\
'If you are travelling through, the Court of the Fount is where you want to be. Here we have the finest goods for sale from all over the world, brought from our ships. It is always bustling here. Never a dull moment!'","Find the Harper's Court","Speak with someone in the Artisan's Quarter","Speak with a swan-knight","You have found the Keep of the Swan-knights","The Harper's Court is in western Dol Amroth.\
\
You should speak with someone in the Harper's Court.","Find the Artisan's Quarter","The Mason's Court is in southern Dol Amroth.\
\
You should make your way to the Mason's Court.","Find the Scholar's Quarter","Find the wharf","'Well met, stranger. Are you here to see the wharf? It is perhaps not the best view of Dol Amroth, but I have always found it the most beautiful place in the city.\
\
'Here you will find all of the fishermen hard at work, and the tall ships rest ere they set out for another great adventure.\
\
'Is there a better smell on earth than clean sea air and fresh fish, and the salt of sea and sweat?'","The Court of the Fount is in the centre of Dol Amroth.\
\
You should make your way to the Court of the Fount.","Find Inzibel's Walk","Laegened, the master stone-mason, can be found in the Mason's Court.\
\
You should speak with Laegened.","Find the Library of Saphadzîr","Speak with Lothíriel","The Artisan's Quarter is in north-east Dol Amroth.\
\
You should speak with someone at the Artisan's Quarter.","'My pardons, I was lost in thought. People often come here to lose themselves in their thoughts, for this is the Scholar's Quarter. Here you will find the great minds of Dol Amroth.'","The Keep of the Swan-knights is in north Dol Amroth.\
\
You should speak with one of the swan-knights.","You have found the Artisan's Quarter","Find the Keep of the Swan-knights","Find the Mason's Court","Find the Court of the Fount","'Are you a travelling artisan, friend? If so, you have come to the right place, for you'll not find a better crafters' area for leagues upon leagues.'","'We get many travellers in Dol Amroth. I bid you welcome! I also say to you: Mind your behaviour while you are here. Drink and make merriment as you will, but do try not to cause a disturbance.\
\
'Here is the Keep of the Swan-knights, where the finest soldiers of Dol Amroth execute the will of Prince Imrahil, or the lady Lothíriel who now governs in his place. A fine prospect, is it not?'","You have come to a quiet and secluded part of the city, breathtakingly lovely","The Library of Saphadzîr is just south of the centre of Dol Amroth.\
\
You should make your way to the Library of Saphadzîr."},
[11877]={"La ciudad de sus padres","'Aragorn ha aprendido mucho del mundo desde que dejó por primera vez Imladris.'","Elrond te ha hablado del viaje que Aragorn hizo a Annúminas en su juventud y te ha dado su aprobación para que Narsil sea reforjada.","'En Annúminas se encuentra el último de los Silithair.'","'No sabía lo que Gwindeth deseaba, pero ahora creo que lo sé.'","'Vuelve con Aragorn y cuéntale mi decisión. Ha llegado la hora de reforjar la espada, tal y como Aragorn se ha reforjado a sí mismo.'","Aragorn está en uno de los cuartos de invitados de la Casa de Elrond.\
\
El Maestro Elrond te ha hablado de la juventud de Aragorn y ha accedido a que Narsil sea reforjada. Ha decidido otorgar un nombre a la nueva espada: Andúril, la Llama del Oeste.","'Aragorn llegó a nosotros cuando solo tenía dos años, habiendo muerto su padre Arathorn por las flechas de los orcos. Gilraen temía por la seguridad de su hijo y lo trajo a Imladris, buscando ocultar su nacimiento a los ojos del Enemigo. Le aconsejé a Gilraen que mantuviera su verdadero nombre y linaje en secreto, y le llamaba Estel, que significa \\qEsperanza.\\q\
\
'Cuando cumplió veinte años, vi que había alcanzado pronto la madurez, así que le hablé sobre su linaje y del nombre que su padre le había dado: Aragorn, un nombre fuerte. Ese día él rebosaba esperanza, que pronto disminuiría por un amor muy por encima de su condición, ya que caminando por los bosques cercano el atardecer del siguiente día se encontró con Arwen, mi hija, y se quedó prendado de ella.\
\
'No sé por qué fue a Annúminas, pero siempre había creído que hizo el viaje para probarse a sí mismo que era merecedor de amar a tal doncella. Fue a esa antigua ciudad, hace mucho tiempo desierta, en compañía de mis hijos y de Calenglad, un Montaraz que venía a veces a Imladris. Calenglad no volvió del viaje de Aragorn a la ciudad de sus padres, y la siguiente vez que vi a Aragorn, la experiencia le había dejado huella.\
\
'Vuelve a Aragorn y dile que estoy de acuerdo en que ha llegado la hora de que Narsil sea reforjada, y le daré un nuevo nombre: Andúril, la Llama del Oeste. Necesitaremos su luz antes del fin.'","'Aragorn fracasó en la tarea que le impuso Gwindeth, hace muchos años.'","'Me alegra que el Maestro Elrond esté de acuerdo con mi decisión, ya que su consejo me es preciado.\
\
'Es cierto que viajé en mi juventud a Annúminas, la ciudad de mis padres. Incluso por entonces llevaba vacía largos años, pero fue una vez la joya resplandeciente de mi pueblo, y deseaba verla con mis propios ojos. También pensé que si recuperaba el Silithar que se encontraba en Annúminas... la única de esas piedras que permanecía en este rincón del mundo... podría reforjar Narsil y probarme a mí mismo merecedor del destino para el que había nacido. Elladan y Elrohir me acompañaron en mi viaje a Evendim, y también mi hombre de confianza Calenglad, que había prestado juramento a mi padre y lo renovó hacia mí cuando partimos.\
\
'Mucho de la ciudad ya había sido reclamada por las aguas del lago Nenuial cuando llegamos, y perdí la esperanza de encontrar el Silithar en la tumba inundada donde se encontraba. Pero he aquí que apareció la doncella Gwindeth ante nosotros y me encomendó una tarea para probar si era merecedor de recibir el Silithar.\
\
'Mi juventud me traicionó; aunque tenía el aspecto de un hombre no tenía sabiduría o experiencia, y Gwindeth no me halló digno. El Silithar no me sería entregado ese día. Cuando llegué a los pasadizos inundados de la tumba vacía de Elendil en Annúminas, creí que era justo que Narsil fuera reforjada. No podía entender por qué Gwindeth me negaba el acceso al Silithar. Ahora creo que lo entiendo.'","Habla con Aragorn en Rivendel."},
[11878]={"'Another face unknown to me. There are many such now. Not long past, those like you would go west to the cells of Emax Dûl. Civility returns and Zajâna stirs, and the Doorwards seek again the name it bore of old: a city of esteem, and cross-roads of the wise. The City of Keys.\
\
'If you would earn regard of our folk, your deeds shall be weighed, and your worth measured. Speak with the Quartermaster—they will show what task may earn you standing.'","Entering the city of Zajâna is awe-inspiring. The weight of centuries dwells within her walls, and her people look to build a future free of tyranny. You are sure to become an ally.","Speak with Valakhâri in Zajâna","'To make a name here, you must act in service to Kighân and more, to Zajâna. Our land, like our people, stands at a turning. We seek again the freedom we once knew, and still desire.\
\
'Aid us truly, and your name shall be writ among those of good repute. Cross us, and it shall be stricken, and you marked foe. The choice lies with you.\
\
'Prove your worth, and we shall speak of trade and reward. For now, begone; I have much to address.'","Your introduction to the quartermaster is complete. Return to Valakhâri and tell her you are ready to assist the city and her people.","Speak with Quartermaster Alahamâr at Zajâna","The City of Zajâna","'Take no offence at our reserve. Zajâna has suffered long, and we have learned to be wary of open hands. Too often have gifts masked chains. We will watch. We will judge. Let your actions speak until your voice has earned its weight.'","You have spoken to Alahamâr","The leaders of Zajâna are not as welcoming as others may be. Too many times has an open hand quickly turned to a shackle. Valakhâri directed you to introduce yourself to the Alahamâr for further instruction."},
[11879]={"Driftwood has likely wandered the surrounds outside the city. You should look for him and see how he is feeling.","Driftwood asked you to leave him alone with his thoughts for a time, and you should respect his wishes.","Leave Driftwood alone with his thoughts","'I need some time to be alone with my thoughts for now.'","'I have been thinking, ${PLAYER}... I think I may have been wrong.\
\
'These past few months have been difficult. I abandoned my kingdom, my friends, and the woman I love, and I thought it was for their own good. I punished myself for the weakness I saw in myself, and I believed my wife and kingdom would be better off without relying on such a man as I am. Horn perished on the Pelennor, and Driftwood was born. But that death, and that birth... they changed nothing. I told myself it was right, but it was not.\
\
'I am done with being alone. I think once our mission is concluded... I might be brave enough to see Nona again. Will you go with me when that time comes?'\
\
You tell your friend that you will, and he smiles grimly.\
\
'I do not think she will be happy to see me, ${PLAYER}. I may need you to convince me to go through with such a meeting, if my courage fails me. But for now I intend it.'","Talk to Driftwood somewhere outside the city","The City: Alone With His Thoughts","Driftwood asked you to give him some time to think in peace.","'I am sorry, ${PLAYER}, but I am not really in the mood for talking right now. Do you think you could give me some time to walk outside the city? I would like to be alone with my thoughts for now.'"},
[11881]={"The Harbour Warden's assistant nods to you as you approach","Talk to dock-workers in the Sail-haven about the Kindred of the Coins","Talk to Legolas across the bridge in the Sail-haven","Gimli and Legolas have begun their investigation into the Kindred of the Coins in the Sail-haven.","'We should speak with this Harbour Warden and learn what we can of Nakási's whereabouts. She knows you by sight, and will not have forgotten your face. She could make things very difficult for us.'","'Gimli and I will keep our eyes open for some sign of Nakási Wave-reaper, ${PLAYER}. It is true that she may cause difficulty for us if she finds us before we locate the ones she took captive.\
\
'We will not relax our vigilance.'","'I have not seen Nakási or Tumúldo in some time, actually.'","Talk to Legolas in the Sail-haven","The Harbour Warden's assistant is outside the tall blue tower located in the water south of the Sail-haven.","Talk to Gimli across the bridge in the Sail-haven","'Yes, what is it?'","'Have you had good fortune or ill so far, ${PLAYER}?'","'Legolas and I have been trying to speak to the dock-workers in the Sail-haven, but they have not been very helpful to us. Perhaps you will have more good fortune than we have. If we could aid our mission here with suspicious glances, we would have the victory already and be halfway back to Gondor by now! I do not think these folk see many Longbeards here, and Elves are even more rare.'","Gimli asked you to speak with nearby dock-workers about the Kindred of the Coins.","Legolas stands in an alley in the Sail-haven.","'I never thought I would say something like this, but these Corsair vessels simply do not compare to the Wave-hunter. Now that was a fine ship! Ah, what has happened to me, ${PLAYER}? I have been beside the water for too long! I will be dreaming about the gulls next, like poor Legolas! No, it is only a jest. I like good strong earth beneath my feet, and always will!\
\
'Legolas and I have been trying to speak to the dock-workers in the Sail-haven, but they have not been very helpful to us. Perhaps you will have more good fortune than we have. If we could aid our mission here with suspicious glances, we would have the victory already and be halfway back to Gondor by now! I do not think these folk see many Longbeards here, and Elves are even more rare.'","'There was a time when asking questions would get you brought to the temple on the hill by the Church of the All Seeing. Be glad those times are past, stranger.\
\
'But I have nothing to say to you. Just be glad the Kindred of the Coins rules us now, and not the Empire of Ordâkh.'","'It is said \\qWherever Elves and dwarves go, trouble is sure to follow.\\q\
\
'I am not saying I agree with it, but this is something you will hear in Umbar, if you keep your ears open. There are other whispers, as well: that Tumúldo Fierce-water got himself killed in Gondor, and his wife Nakási burned the White City to the ground to avenge him. I do not know the truth of it. Why, Tumúldo is probably still alive. He has disappeared before for weeks at a time, and I do not believe something just because I heard someone say it.\
\
'The two of them are beloved by the folk of the Sail-haven, and have been ever since they helped us cast off the yoke of Ordâkh and the Church of the All Seeing. If something has happened to the two of them, Harbour Warden Eshmun will know of it. His office is in the tall blue tower to the south. I cannot guarantee he will speak to such as you... but you may find it valuable to try.'","The office of the harbour warden is in the tall blue tower out in the water south of the Sail-haven.","Find the office of the Harbour Warden in the tall blue tower","'The people here do not know some of what we know, ${PLAYER}, and I recommend we keep it that way. If it became clear that some of the rumours they have dismissed are true... let us say it may become more difficult for us to accomplish our mission.\
\
'We should speak with this Harbour Warden and learn what we can of Nakási's whereabouts. She knows you by sight, and will not have forgotten your face. She could make things very difficult for us.'","'Questions like this are like to get you in trouble, stranger, and sooner than you might be prepared for!'","The City: Elves, Dwarves, and Trouble","Gimli and Legolas stand across the bridge from the Harbour Warden's tower.","'Where has Nakási Wave-reaper gone? I do not like this, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'They say Elves and dwarves cause trouble? I say vengeful widows are more likely to cause trouble than we are, and that trouble will be worse!'","Talk to Eshmun's assistant outside the tall blue tower south of the Sail-haven","'Yes, what is it? Eshmun is too busy to speak with just anyone, but I am his assistant and can aid you with any of your needs, so long as it is in the power of the Harbour Warden to grant it. What do you want?'\
\
You ask the Harbour Warden's assistant what he knows about the ship of Nakási Wave-reaper. He seems about to answer quickly, and then catches himself. He thinks for a moment.\
\
'Do you know something? I have not seen Nakási or Tumúldo in some time. There have been whispers about them down in the Sail-haven, but now that you mention it... it is rather strange that they have not come to see Eshmun in the past few days. Their ship is hard to miss! Usually it is docked right over there.\
\
'Is that all? Good day to you, then.'"},
[11882]={"Talk to Azagath Sea-shadow at Galengam's market stall","Galengam's market stall is to the north, in the Sail-haven.","If Cruel Dancer kills him now, your plan to rescue Thorongil will be endangered!","That man was Azagath Sea-shadow, the leader of the Kindred of the Coins!","Talk to Galengam at his market stall","A richly-dressed man has commented on the notice you just posted.","Post notices for Galengam's market stall (0/3)","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> for Cruel Dancer in the vicinity of Galengam's market stall","Azagath said he would visit Galengam's market stall to the north. Is Cruel Dancer nearby? If she kills her target now, you might never see Thorongil again!","Galengam has asked you to put up notices for his new stall to the south, within the Sail-haven.","'A man from Gondor has opened a new market stall in the Sail-haven?' the man asks you. As you tell him that is true, something about his manner strikes you as odd. You ask him if he has an interest in goods from Gondor, and he smiles.\
\
'I do, my new friend. Why should that be unusual? We have had our differences, Umbar and Gondor, but my land desires only to maintain the stability it has earned. It has been different in Gondor, but it should not remain so, should it? My Kindred believes that peace between our lands is possible... if Gondor will meet us along that path. What did you say you were called?'\
\
You answer with your name, and he responds with another charming smile.\
\
'Enjoy your stay in Umbar Baharbêl, ${PLAYER}. Let Azagath Sea-shadow be the first to welcome you to his land. I will not be the last, I warrant. We are a friendly people, as you are certain to discover. Now I will go to see the goods your merchant friend has to sell.'\
\
This man is Azagath, leader of the Kindred of the Coins!","Galengam has wasted no time and is ready to open his market stall in Umbar Baharbêl.","There is no sign of Cruel Dancer... for what that is worth","Azagath Sea-shadow moves away and is lost in the crowd.","'Please take your time, my wealthy friend! You are certain to see something you will want!'","'The overland route from Gondor has been treacherous of late, and few merchants have come to my city during the months following the conclusion of the war. Did you come by ship?'\
\
Galengam happily chatters away, describing a dangerous voyage across the bay and a brief stay in the Shield Isles. Azagath nods sagely.\
\
'You have done very well to make the journey up Umbarkhîl, for the Cape has had its own share of troubles of late: famine, blight, and unsavoury types among them. You are to be commended for bringing your wares this far. \
\
'I must be about my own business now, but allow me to extend the welcome I gave to ${PLAYER} to you as well, Galengam. I hope you will find the custom in my city to your liking! Farewell, my friends. Perhaps I will see you again.'","Post the notices for Galengam's market stall (2/3)","Posted notices for Galengam's market stall (2/3)","Posted notices for Galengam's market stall (1/3)","Galengam's market stall is in the Sail-haven.","Wait for Azagath to leave","Galengam does not know this is Azagath Sea-shadow","Post the notices for Galengam's market stall (1/3)","'My first customer was not a customer at all, for he did not buy anything. Disaster! No, I must try and stay positive. Perhaps he will tell his other wealthy friends. Why are you staring at me like this, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You tell Galengam that the richly-dressed man was Azagath Sea-shadow, leader of the Kindred of the Coins, and that if Cruel Dancer had seen him out and about in the Sail-haven she would have likely killed him where he stood. Galengam frowns.\
\
'We should be glad that she did not see him, then. That would have been quite bad for business! Really, ${PLAYER}, I think your priorities are somewhat askew. You will never make it as a merchant in this world if you have such trouble remembering what is important!'","'Post those notices around the Sail-haven for me, perhaps to the south, and soon the customers will swarm my goods and you will have to save me from drowning... drowning in gold phârzi and silver gîmli, that is!'","'I told you the customers would come here in droves, ${PLAYER}! None can resist my rare and valuable goods, or my name is not Galengam! The coin will be rolling in before this day's end!\
\
'This man is my first customer, and...'\
\
Galengam lowers his voice to a hushed whisper.\
\
'...and see how finely he is dressed! This man has money to spend, and I will see to it that he spends most of it at my stall, and no others!'","The City: Galengam's First Customer","'The principles of buying and selling hold true no matter where you go in this world, ${PLAYER}. Have I not proved this to you already?\
\
'But I will do so again! I give to you this stack of notices advertising the new market stall I have opened. If you post these around the Sail-haven for me, perhaps to the south, soon the customers will swarm my goods and you will have to save me from drowning... drowning in gold phârzi and silver gîmli, that is!'","A man standing nearby comments on the notice you just posted","Talk to the richly-dressed man staring at the notice you just posted"},
[11883]={"The City: Gangur Farwend Finds Answers","Gangur Farwend is eager to speak with Carver Gírma at the Old Bastion Inn.","'Abâshal, the sea-opal! At last I have a name to apply to the most beautiful gemstone on which I have ever laid my eyes!\
\
'I will have many more questions for my new friend here, ${PLAYER}. Do not let me keep you! I am disappointed the Shoreward Stone must be closed to outsiders, but I am delighted to know that not all of the Temámir guard their tongues as closely as the others I have met!\
\
'I will remain and speak with Carver Gírma for a time. Abâshal! I would learn as much about it as I can!'","'It is my pleasure to speak of Abâshal! It has been a secret of my people, but as it grows in importance for Umbar I cannot avoid speaking of it to those who would hear more. That would not be right!'","'Lead on, my friend.'","Find the Old Bastion Inn to the south-west of the Shoreward Stone, in the Fleet-fast","'I understand that one member of the Kindred of the Coins is a Dwarf of the Temámir who goes by the name Khôltekh. He wears a medallion of some kind, and this medallion sparkles with a most unusual shine, the like of which I have never seen in any jewel buried within the earth. What is this material, and where may it be found? I have never seen anything like it... not while awake, in any case!'","Gangur Farwend is frustrated to learn that the dwarf-quarter of the city, the Shoreward Stone, is shut to outsiders.","Wait to see what happens","Carver Gírma offered to speak with you and Gangur Farwend at the Old Bastion Inn to the south-west, in the Fleet-fast.","'Carver Gírma has agreed to answer any questions I might have, ${PLAYER}, and I must admit that this is a much finer reception than that I was given in Furukzahar! The Shoreward Stone may be off-limits to me, but if he gives me the answers I seek I will forgive that refusal, and harbour no hard feelings about the matter!\
\
'Then let me ask the first question. I understand that one member of the Kindred of the Coins is a Dwarf of the Temámir who goes by the name Khôltekh. He wears a medallion of some kind, and this medallion sparkles with a most unusual shine, the like of which I have never seen in any jewel buried within the earth. What is this material, and where may it be found? I have never seen anything like it... not while awake, in any case!'","'Listen to me, my friends. I understand you have come a long way to be here, and that you were hopeful to see inside the Shoreward Stone?\
\
'Regretfully, I do not possess the authority to permit it. But if you will meet me by the Old Bastion Inn to the south-west, in the Fleet-fast, perhaps I can show you the hospitality you deserve? I do not want the good name of the Temámir besmirched in this fashion, if I might prevent it!'","A nearby dwarf of the Temámir calls for your attention","Carver Gírma is at the Old Bastion Inn.","Talk to Gangur Farwend at the Old Bastion Inn","'I thought I would find the answers I sought in the dwarf-quarter of the city, but now I see that it is shut to outsiders! I have come so far to learn about this gemstone... must I be turned away by these Temámir as I was by Hámisar of Furukzahar? Interolerable, that's what this is!'","Talk to Carver Gírma at the Old Bastion Inn","'You speak of Abâshal, my new friend! It can be no other! Some call it \\qsea-opal,\\q but unlike other jewels the iridescence that gives it value can shine with every colour of the rainbow, and the forces involved in its shaping can cause even those to shift in truly remarkable fashion! You will typically find it cut into small jewels or fashioned into flat panels, if you find it at all; it is most rare, and its naturally-occurring form is brittle. Only the finest of stone-workers can mould it effectively. I blush to tell you I am one such craftsman. The knowledge is known only to few.\
\
'The Empire of Ordâkh and the Church of the All Seeing that they brought with them to Umbar believed the ornamentation of Abâshal to be blasphemous; almost overnight as much of the jewel as could be salvaged was removed from the city and hidden away in secret vaults. When the temple collapsed at the moment of the Dark Lord's fall, it seemed clear the time of his church and the dominion of Ordâkh was ended. The Kindred of the Coins adopted Abâshal as a sign of not just wealth, but of defiance to foreign rule. You will not be surprised to learn that each of the Kindred's leaders possesses a medallion such as that you saw on Khôltekh's person, each one inlaid with a small piece of Abâshal.'","Carver Gírma has called for your attention.","Gangur Farwend is feeling frustrated.","'¿Qué es?'","'If you will meet me by the Old Bastion Inn to the south-west, in the Fleet-fast, perhaps I can show you the hospitality you deserve? I do not want the good name of the Temámir besmirched in this fashion, if I might prevent it!'","Talk to Carver Gírma outside the Shoreward Stone","Gangur Farwend is at the Old Bastion Inn."},
[11884]={"Talk to the Lower Ward resident outside the Cat's Grin Tavern about Khâsha","Sigileth wanted you to <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> for mention of Khâsha to the north, outside the Black Anchor Tavern in the Lower Ward.","You think you have overheard the name \\qKhâsha\\q and should ask the Lower Ward resident for more information.","Sigileth is helping you investigate the mystery of Khâsha in the Lower Ward.","Sigileth wanted you to <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> for mention of Khâsha further north, outside the Cat's Grin Tavern in the Lower Ward.","'Will you go north and <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> for further mention of this name outside the Black Anchor Tavern? If we have learned the fate of Khâsha's lost love, should we not tell her of it?'","Talk to Khâsha in the Lower Ward","Sigileth has come with you to meet with Phêlex in the Lower Ward.","'When I became She Who Remained, and haunted the dungeons of Dol Guldur, I often heard voices and names from my past. I believed this was due to the dreadful nature of those midnight vaults or the terrible artifacts held within them... but it is possible it was... just me.\
\
'I think it has happened again. While I walked here in the Lower Ward, I thought I heard the name \\qKhâsha.\\q It may be this is a common Umbari name, but is it also possible someone may speak of the woman to whom the note we found in the Shield Isles was addressed?\
\
'Will you go north and <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> for further mention of this name outside the Black Anchor Tavern? If we have learned the fate of Khâsha's lost love, should we not tell her of it?'","Talk to Sigileth in the Lower Ward","Talk to Phêlex by the Guild Hall in the Lower Ward","'My husband's name is Phêlex... and he is very much alive.'","Khâsha lives in the Lower Ward, north-east of the Cat's Grin Tavern.","'Yes? I am called Khâsha. Can I help you with something?'\
\
You tell Khâsha about the discovery you made on the Shield Isles of a bottle that contained a note addressed to someone with her name, and that if she is the Khâsha in question it properly belongs to her. She takes the note from you and studies it. When she finishes reading the message, she folds it up and puts it back inside the bottle. She looks at you carefully before she speaks again.\
\
'My husband's name is Phêlex... and he is very much alive.'","'Will you go further to the north and <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> outside the Cat's Grin Tavern for mention of this name? If we have learned the fate of Khâsha's lost love, should we not tell her of it?'","Did that woman just mention someone named Khâsha?","'Khâsha? Why yes, I do know a Khâsha! She is a friend of mine.\
\
'She lives to the north-east, here in the Lower Ward, if you seek her.'","Phêlex is by the Guild Hall in the Lower Ward.","The City: Sigileth's Curiosity","Khâsha says you can find Phêlex by the Guild Hall and he will tell you... if you can be trusted","Someone named Khâsha lives to the north-east, in the Lower Ward.","You were told you might find Phêlex near the Guild Hall in the Lower Ward.","'Phêlex is alive? Those are surprising tidings, for it sounded from his note as if he was about to be slain by the Corsairs that boarded his ship. How did he manage to escape?'","Find Phêlex outside the Guild Hall in the Lower Ward","<rgb=#00FF00>Listen</rgb> for mention of Khâsha further north, outside the Cat's Grin Tavern in the Lower Ward","'Phêlex is alive? It sounded from his note as if he was about to be slain by the Corsairs that boarded his ship. How did he manage to escape?'","<rgb=#00FF00>Listen</rgb> for mention of Khâsha to the north, outside the Black Anchor Tavern in the Lower Ward","'My husband's name is Phêlex... and he is very much alive. Find him by the Guild Hall and he will tell you the story... if you can be trusted.'","'Khâsha sent you to me? For what purpose? If I can help you I will, but I do not believe we have ever met before. I think I would remember it!'\
\
You tell Phêlex that you found a bottle among the Shield Isles with a note inside it, and his mouth drops open with surprise. You show it to him and he reads it with interest.\
\
'I never thought to see this again, stranger. You see... I wrote this note almost thirty years ago, when my ship was boarded by Corsairs. I did not think to escape alive, and indeed none others of the crew survived. But I... I am not proud of this, but I threw myself upon their mercy, and they took me into their crew. For more than twenty-five years I lived on that ship, raiding and pillaging, living the life of a Corsair, a brigand of the waves. I am not proud of it... but I was alive, and I intended to stay alive.\
\
'I returned at last to my Khâsha. It would have been a short reunion, and bittersweet, had I not befriended a smuggler by the name of Tumúldo Fierce-water. He encouraged me not to sail with Balakhôr, one of the Heirs of Castamir, and in that way he saved my life, for all who followed Balakhôr to Gondor perished in the war. Ever since that day I have supported the Kindred of the Coins. Loyalty to any others, and the life of a Corsair, are both behind me now.\
\
'I ask you to understand, stranger. I lived a criminal's life, yes, but it was the only life I had available to me. Tumúldo understood that, and so did Khâsha, and now I dedicate my life to serving each of them. It really brings me back, seeing that note in its bottle, but I was a different man when I wrote it, and I have become a different man than the man I became afterward.'","'It is not our place to judge this man. Have we not all done what we must to survive? She Who Remained is no stranger to need, and neither are you, ${PLAYER}. Will it be the same with my brother? Perhaps it will.\
\
'I will continue searching for information that will help us with our mission, but it is good to know the conclusion to the mystery of the note we found in the bottle in the Shield Isles. I was curious, and now that curiosity has been satisfied.'","'I ask you to understand, stranger. I lived a criminal's life, yes, but it was the only life I had available to me. Tumúldo understood that, and so did Khâsha, and now I dedicate my life to serving each of them. It really brings me back, seeing that note in its bottle, but I was a different man when I wrote it, and I have become a different man than the man I became afterward.'","Sigileth overheard someone mention the name \\qKhâsha.\\q Is it possible this could be the same Khâsha mentioned in the note you found in the Shield Isles?","Find the Khâsha who lives in the Lower Ward","You hear nothing specifically about anyone named Khâsha","Talk to Sigileth by the Guild Hall in the Lower Ward","You found Phêlex, the author of the note you recovered, and he is alive"},
[11885]={"'Yes, can I help you with something? What is it?'","Sirgon seems to ignore the nearby guards, and keep his eyes on Mêshka.","'I was not certain you would dare come here. But since you have, you will hear my words before you and your friend die.'\
\
Mêshka holds up her hand, signaling to her guards that they should await her command.\
\
'For years after Sirgon drove my intended to his death, I lived a life of mourning. Believing he died at sea, I married, and it was a marriage of great happiness... at least until its ending, when my husband was seized by the Church of the All Seeing and burned alive, sacrificed to its Dark Lord.\
\
'Why do I tell you this? I tell you this so you will know I am no wilting flower. I have been forged of tough steel, hardened by fire and by the salt-spray. There is a reason Belondor was my first intended, for he is the same: made durable by his experiences.\
\
'For he did not perish beneath the waves when Sirgon pursued him through the rocks of Shedax Khîn. He survived as a castaway among the Shield Isles, sun-scorched and bitter, until he was taken aboard an Ordâkhai galley. In time he came to Umbar and served in the Fleet-fast, becoming one of its dedicated defenders, but the rule of the Heirs of Castamir rankled him.\
\
'He began a friendship with Azagath the Sea-shadow and others who would come to supplant the Heirs. This Kindred of the Coins rules wisely and fairly, unlike either the Heirs of Castamir or the Steward of Gondor. What final words have you to say, Sirgon? Will you beg the forgiveness of my husband? I will give your words to him, if they please me.'","Mêshka waits for you outside her home, surrounded by guards","Mêshka stares at Sirgon for a long moment... and then motions for her guards to stand down.\
\
'We were all wounded on that night, Sirgon, and none of us knew how deeply. Your words ring true to me. I have spent years dwelling upon my hatred of you for the treatment suffered by Belondor at your hands, and at the hands of Gondor, and though that land is ruled now by a King and not a Steward, I believe in my heart that it would be no different if those events happened today and not long years ago. I did not forgive you then, and I do not forgive you now.'\
\
Mêshka shakes her head, and for the first time today you see her smile.\
\
'But men are weak, Sirgon. Know this: when the streets of Umbar Baharbêl filled with soldiers of Ordâkh and the Heirs of Castamir sailed with the Corsairs to Gondor, my husband Belondor weighed his hatred for Gondor against them... and he dispatched a ship for Pelargir, bearing a warning for you. I counselled against it, but it seems it did not matter, for the ship never arrived. No doubt it was sunk by the Heirs, and no warning ever came to you.\
\
'My first husband was a good man, slain by Ordâkh. My second husband, Belondor, helped to overthrow those who killed my first, and he established a new order in Umbar, the Kindred of the Coins, which will usher in an era of prosperity and peace. If he has any fault, it is that he forgives too readily, and is pleased to forget the sins of Gondor if it means Umbar will have a fresh beginning; this is not a fault that I share! Therefore I give you your life, Sirgon, but I banish you from the Upper Ward. If I see you return I will order my guards to slay you where you stand. Now begone. Our business here is done.'","Mêshka and Belondor live to the north-east, in the Upper Ward.","Mêshka stares at Sirgon coldly.","Mêshka hurries away.","You learned that Belondor's wife Mêshka was recently spotted on her way to one of the markets in the Upper Ward or the Sail-haven.","'The woman Belondor loved was a noblewoman of the city, and she was called Mêshka. I believe her home must be somewhere within the Upper Ward, and the folk within may tell us where she lives with Belondor. It is a gamble, of course: the two may dwell now within the Citadel of Winds, as befits a leader of the Kindred and his wife. But it might not be so, and folk of the Upper Ward may tell us.'","Talk to Mêshka at her home in the Upper Ward","Sirgon walks away, and does not look back","Sirgon has asked you to speak to residents of the Upper Ward so you may learn where Belondor now lives.","'I have... much to think about, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Let us leave the Upper Ward. I believe Mêshka was serious, and it is not safe for us to remain here.'","'I do not care for your choice of friend, stranger.'\
\
Mêshka addresses Sirgon with hatred in her voice.\
\
'You are bold to come here, Sirgon of Gondor, but foolish. My husband suffered much at your hands and those of your master. For you to come here now...'\
\
She falls silent.\
\
'Not here. You will come to the home I share with Belondor, and there we will speak. It is the north-east, here in the Upper Ward.'","You learned that Belondor's wife Mêshka was recently spotted on her way south, perhaps to one of the markets of the Upper Ward or in the Sail-haven.","'I cannot help you. I am sorry.'","'What final words have you to say, Sirgon? Will you beg the forgiveness of my husband? I will give your words to him, if they please me.'","Talk to residents of the Upper Ward and learn where Belondor lives","Sirgon has been banished from the Upper Ward. You should speak with him to the south-west, in the Sail-haven.","'I was not certain you would dare come here.'","Talk to Mêshka at one of the markets in the Upper Ward or in the Sail-haven","'I do not beg for forgiveness, Mêshka, for I know forgiveness is not deserved. If there is a message to give from me to your husband Belondor, it would be this: the wound I suffered the night we duelled after dinner was mortal. It was not a deep cut, not physically, but that wound has stayed with me since that night.\
\
'I will not beg for forgiveness, or say that following the command of the Steward Denethor protects me from your reprisal. But know that I was forever changed by what I did to your husband Belondor, though I did not know it. But now I see that I was.\
\
'I believed I missed the sea, and sailing, and traced my miseries to giving up that life. But I see now that it was my friendship with your husband that I truly missed, and the innocence of my youth before I committed the act by which I am now forever judged, and judge myself. If this is the wound that is to slay me now, I welcome it. I ask that you spare ${PLAYER}, who had no part in earning this, but I will not run from it.'","Wait for Sirgon to arrive","The City: Sirgon's Wound","Sirgon steps forward and Mêshka's eyes go cold","Talk to Mêshka at one of the markets in the Upper Ward or the Sail-haven","Mêshka goes inside her home, the conversation concluded","'I have not seen Belondor today, but you just missed his wife Mêshka! She was heading south toward the Sail-haven. She may have been bound for the market of the Upper Ward that is on the way, or one of those in the Sail-haven, and if you hurry you might still catch her.'","Sirgon stands outside the home of Mêshka and Belondor in the Upper Ward.","Wait for Mêshka to leave","Talk to Sirgon to the south-west, outside the Upper Ward","'Belondor? Aye, he is the Master of Fleets, and when he is not at sea you will usually see him walking through the Fleet-fast, down by the shore. He is a good man, well-loved by his people. They say he was instrumental in organizing the overthrow of the Church of the All Seeing and the casting off of our Ordâkhai shackles... but that is just what I heard.\
\
'I can tell you no more than this.'","'I know nothing that will help you. You have my apologies.\
\
'Now move on.'","Mêshka and Belondor live in the north-eastern reaches of the Upper Ward.","Sirgon is reluctant to face his unpleasant history with Belondor of the Kindred, but he knows that he must.","'I have spent our journey from the Shield Isles fearing a confrontation with Belondor, ${PLAYER}, but it seems I should have more feared his wife Mêshka! I warrant that she is more fierce than he is! I hope I have not endangered our own mission here. He will learn from her that I am in the city, that is true, but the personal nature of our conversation may mask that I came here at the command of King Elessar. Perhaps that will prove a helpful distraction for the Kindred of the Coins when the time comes to rescue the captives?\
\
'I have much to think about. Thank you for helping me with this, my friend, and I am sorry to have brought you into danger. It could... it could have gone worse. But it did not. My apologies all the same, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'I will continue seeking out information... just not within the Upper Ward of the city.'","Talk to Sirgon outside Mêshka's home in the Upper Ward","'I must confront my old friend Belondor, ${PLAYER}. I cannot put it off any longer, or I will never face it. No, do not seek to dissuade me! I am resolute. If you are a friend, you will aid me in this.\
\
'The woman Belondor loved was a noblewoman of the city, and she was called Mêshka. I believe her home must be somewhere within the Upper Ward, and the folk within may tell us where she lives with Belondor. It is a gamble, of course: the two may dwell now within the Citadel of Winds, as befits a leader of the Kindred and his wife. But it might not be so, and folk of the Upper Ward may tell us.'","Meet with Mêshka at her home in the Upper Ward"},
[11886]={"Nauriel asked you to linger by the clay jar to the south-west so you can observe the movement of guards within the Fleet-fast.","Talk to Nauriel to the north-east, outside the Fleet-fast","'If any harm should befall Azagath on one of these strolls I will look for you first, so you had better not try anything. No lingering in the Fleet-fast! I will not tell you again!'","Linger by the clay jar to the south-west, in the Fleet-fast","Nauriel asked you to linger by a clay jar so you can observe the movement of guards within the Fleet-fast.","Talk to the Fleet-fast guard","Linger by the clay jar further to the west","Nauriel asked you to linger at a clay jar further to the west so you can observe the movement of guards within the Fleet-fast.","Nauriel has asked you to learn the guard assignments within the Fleet-fast as she prepares a plan to gain access to the Citadel of Winds.","Nauriel waits for your report where you left her, to the north-east outside the Fleet-fast.","A guard of the Fleet-fast calls out to you","Observe the movement of guards within the Fleet-fast","Linger by a clay jar further to the west","'Can I ask you to become my eyes in there, and for you to linger by certain of the clay jars that stand at major cross-roads within the Fleet-fast? When you do, be sure to note the number of guards and the patrol routes they take as they pass by.\
\
'This information will help us craft a plan for making our way through the Fleet-fast when the time comes to rescue my Thorongil.'","'You there! You cannot just linger like this in the Fleet-fast! Do not make me haul you away to the Gaol, for I will do it.'\
\
You ask the guard if any visitors are ever permitted into the island citadel, and he laughs.\
\
'Oh yes, folk are allowed inside! But those folk need to have a personal invitation, and you don't have the look of someone who's likely to have that. Unless Azagath invites you himself, I think you had better keep moving.'\
\
You ask if Azagath ever comes out of the citadel, and the guard raises an eyebrow.\
\
'He does, for he is beloved by the people and sometimes walks among them... but if any harm should befall him on one of these strolls I will look for you first, so you had better not try anything.\
\
'No lingering in the Fleet-fast! I will not tell you again!'","Nauriel asked you to linger by a clay jar further to the west so you can observe the movement of guards within the Fleet-fast.","The City: The Eyes of Nauriel","A suspicious guard of the Fleet-fast has called you over to him.","'From your report it appears the Fleet-fast is well-patrolled by guards loyal to the Kindred of the Coins, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps Cruel Dancer would be able to get inside the Citadel of Winds, but for the rest of us... I will need to think of some other way.\
\
'An invitation by Azagath himself seems... unlikely. I will keep thinking.'","'The Fleet-fast is just beyond this gate, ${PLAYER}, and it seems to be guarded. Still, if we are to rescue my son we will need to penetrate its defences. Can I ask you to become my eyes in there, and for you to linger by certain of the clay jars that stand at major cross-roads within the Fleet-fast? When you do, be sure to note the number of guards and the patrol routes they take as they pass by.\
\
'This information will help us craft a plan for making our way through the Fleet-fast when the time comes to rescue my Thorongil.'"},
[11887]={"Daxamat is outside the arena in the Tor-gardens, considering his friend's likely fate if he faces Rothog the Storm in battle.","The guard comes back outside","'I was in the stands of the arena the night of the rebellion, when the Kindred of the Coins came to power and cast off the shackles of Ordâkh and the Church of the All Seeing, when the Heirs of Castamir lost their grip on Umbar.\
\
'The ground shook, and we saw flames erupt away across the harbour. Rothog had been put to work fighting the few of his Crow-feeders that remained alive, as well as Men who had defied the Heirs. But that all changed when the whispered rumours became facts proclaimed: Mâkhda Khorbo, the temple of Sauron, had fallen. Rothog turned to face his opponents in the arena, and he spoke a single word. From where I stood I could not hear it, but as it was repeated by others it grew in volume and intensity, until the echo of that one word shook the very foundations of the arena.\
\
'The word was \\qHêlsi,\\q and when the uprising of the Kindred was completed, Azagath Sea-shadow found Rothog the Storm sitting in the seats reserved for the Heirs of Castamir, surrounded by their half-eaten bodies. The half-troll did not join the Kindred of the Coins at once, but in time he did, and the people of the city love him. He still fights in the arena as often as he can, but now he does it for himself, and no other.\
\
'What does \\qHêlsi\\q mean? It means \\qFreedom.\\q'","'I asked around the city for information about... ah... the matter that brought us here. But I learned something else!\
\
'A good friend of mine, and Jajax's too, is locked up in the gaol here. His name is Itûr, and he got up to much the same things as my brother and me. When my brother and I returned to the city, it was Itûr who helped me escape from the notice of Khôltekh. It seems Itûr was not so fortunate.\
\
'Do you think you might ask the guard of the gaol if Itûr is in good spirits, and when he may be released?'","'Itûr? Yes, I know this prisoner. He was a Corsair that managed to avoid sailing to the war with all the rest, which means he sails under lucky stars... but his good fortune must have run out, because he robbed the wrong person and ended up in the Fleet-fast gaol.\
\
'But he is not to be here long. I understand he has agreed to trial by combat in the Dahâl Huliz, the arena of the gladiators. If he is victorious there he will be released. If he is not... well, he will no longer take up any wall-space in the gaol, if you understand my meaning.'","'Do you think you might ask the guard of the gaol if Itûr is in good spirits, and when he may be released?'","The Guard of the Gaol has gone inside to speak with Itûr.","'Thank you for the... donation. The Fleet-fast will make use of it.'","'What's this? Back so soon?'\
\
You press Daxamat's money-purse into the guard's hands and he tests its weight.\
\
'You want me to see if your friend will withdraw his request for a trial by combat? That is not usually done, stranger. What makes you think he should?\
\
'Ah. Rothog, eh? I understand now! I will see what I can do.'","The City: The Short Straw","The various match-ups for the arena can be found in the Tor-gardens.","You should see how bad things may be for Itûr by speaking to people familiar with the arena in the Tor-gardens.","Give Daxamat's money-purse to the Guard of the Gaol in the Fleet-fast","The guard goes inside","Only the guard outside the gaol in the Fleet-fast can save Itûr now.","'You are fortunate you spoke to me today, and so am I... for my coin-purse is feeling a little light. Who did you want to hear about?\
\
'Itûr? Yes, I know this prisoner. He was a Corsair that managed to avoid sailing to the war with all the rest, which means he sails under lucky stars... but his good fortune must have run out, because he robbed the wrong person and ended up in the Fleet-fast Gaol.\
\
'But he is not to be here long. I understand he has agreed to trial by combat in the Dahâl Huliz, the arena of the gladiators. If he is victorious there he will be released. If he is not... well, he will no longer take up any wall-space in the gaol, if you understand my meaning.'","'Hurry back to the gaol! There is no time to waste! We have to get the guard to allow Itûr to withdraw his request for trial by combat!'","Talk to Daxamat outside the arena in the Tor-gardens","Examine the arena match-ups in the Tor-gardens","'Itûr was no martial novice when I knew him, but he was never especially skilled in combat. I think his success in the arena will depend upon the Hûlaz against whom he is matched.\
\
'Let us go to the arena and see if they have posted the match-ups for the upcoming contests.'","'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. I know Itûr wanted to be set free, but I also know he would prefer to be alive than to face an unwinnable battle, and Rothog's reputation in the arena speaks for itself.\
\
'I do hope you will take pity upon me if I need coin in the future. I gave the last of my money away as part of this endeavour, after all. It was worth it, was it not?\
\
'Aye, surely it was worth it. But keep me in mind at meal-times, ${PLAYER}, or I will waste away to nothing.'","The guard of the gaol has finally come back outside.","Daxamat stands outside the gaol in the Fleet-fast.","'I am happy to report that your friend has withdrawn his request for trial by combat. He does not want to remain imprisoned... but when I told him he had drawn Rothog as an opponent, he was unable to speak. Through the stammering I was able to discern that he preferred remaining a guest of the gaol for awhile longer. \\qUntil Rothog has retired,\\q he may have said, but if I were a wagering man I would not expect that to happen any time soon. The half-troll Master of the Tor-gardens loves fighting that much, even when there is no need for it.\
\
'Our business is now done. I thank you for the donation to the Fleet-fast.'","'My friend Itûr has to withdraw his request for trial by combat! There is no possible way he can best Rothog the Storm in the arena! Perhaps if he was matched against someone else he would have some hope of victory... but Rothog is the most dangerous Hûlaz to ever fight in the Tor-gardens! Itûr could not have drawn a shorter straw than this!\
\
'Take my money-purse, ${PLAYER}, and hurry back to the gaol! There is no time to waste! We have to get the guard to allow Itûr to withdraw his request!'","'Who are the two combatants about whom you speak? Rothog the Storm?\
\
'You need not tell me the other name. Rothog never loses!'","Talk to visitors to the Tor-gardens about Itûr's chances against Rothog the Storm (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Daxamat has learned that his good friend Itûr, currently held in the gaol in the Fleet-fast, may have volunteered for something unwise.","Talk to Daxamat outside the gaol in the Fleet-fast","Wait for the guard to come back outside","A guard stands watch outside the gaol in the Fleet-fast.","Talk to the Guard of the Gaol in the Fleet-fast","'I ran as quickly as I could, but you still got here before me. I take it the guard is speaking to Itûr?'","'Here he is!'","'Rothog the Storm? He is my favourite of all the Hûliz who fight in the arena! How can you not have heard of him?\
\
'He is a mighty half-troll who began as a ferocious pit-fighter and rose to command a ship and crew of his own; the Crow-feeders, they were called, for a great mass of carrion birds followed in their wake. When Rothog crossed Balakhôr the Scourge, he found himself once again consigned to the arena, forced to fight his former crew and friends. Balakhôr thought he would die... but Rothog survived for more than a year, sometimes fighting as many as ten bouts in a week!\
\
'He became the favoured champion of the people, and though Balakhôr commanded the master of the arena to execute the half-troll and be done with him, she refused the command. \\qFight him yourself, if you wish so badly to see him dead!\\q I heard she answered.\
\
'But before he could, Balakhôr sailed to his death in Gondor. And now Rothog belongs to the Kindred of the Coins... but he still fights in the arena, because he enjoys it!'","Daxamat's friend Itûr is scheduled to battle Rothog the Storm in the arena","Talked to visitors about Itûr's chances (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'Trial by combat? Itûr was no martial novice when I knew him, but he was never especially skilled in combat. I think his success in the arena will depend upon the Hûlaz against whom he is matched.\
\
'Let us go to the arena and see if they have posted the match-ups for the upcoming contests.'","Daxamat hands you his money-purse and encourages you to hurry","'Oh no. If Itûr must face Rothog the Storm in the arena, he has no hope for survival!'"},
[11888]={"Talk to Bruidis by the south-eastern gate in the Fleet-fast","Bruidis has asked you to <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> the defences of the barracks, and the eastern and western ends of the bridge that spans the Fleet-fast.","You appraise the number and quality of guards that patrol the western end of the Fleet-fast bridge","Talk to Rossaran in the Lower Ward","'Bruidis suggested I find some garb that would allow me to pass undetected within the Fleet-fast, but I refused her; it was not easy, but I do not want to skulk about in secret! If my swan-knight armour is not welcome here, then neither am I!\
\
'She was not pleased about it, but she sent me into the Lower Ward to learn what I could about our opponents. I cannot say that what I have discovered will be of use to us, but I was able to learn how the people feel about some of the various leaders among the Kindred of the Coins.\
\
'Azagath and Belondor are both well-loved by the people, who give them a large portion of the credit for the Sea-stone Mutiny. That is the name given to the overthrow of the Heirs of Castamir and the Church of the All Seeing, when the oppressors of the Empire of Ordâkh were cast out of the city.\
\
'Hármelak, the Golden Queen, is respected more than she is loved. She is one of the wealthiest people in Umbar, but the folk of the Lower Ward distrust her riches; many of them believe she is indifferent to their plight, and would not spend a single coin on their behalf.\
\
'Rothog the Storm is considered a champion of the Lower Ward, for no one lives there who has not heard of his exploits in the arena, or of the manner with which he dispatched many of the Heirs of Castamir during the Mutiny. They love him... but they fear him as well.\
\
'Of the others I was not able to learn very much. I hope this information is of as much use to you as the recounting of the Fleet-fast's defences are to Bruidis! We shall see, I suppose. I will keep looking, ${PLAYER}.'","'I could not utilize Rossaran effectively in the Fleet-fast, so I sent him to conduct his investigation within the Lower Ward. Seek him out to the north and find out what he learned while he was there.'","'The Fleet-fast is well-defended, ${PLAYER}, and it will prove nearly impossible for one of us to walk around while remaining undetected. There are a number of places of interest that we should <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> for their military readiness. Can I ask you to conduct such an appraisal of the barracks and both the eastern and western ends of the bridge that spans the Fleet-fast?\
\
'I would ask my husband Rossaran to do this... but his swan-knight armour makes him stand out even more than you do! He took only a dozen steps within before he was pulled aside by one of the guards. You are more likely to escape their notice.'","Bruidis is located by the south-eastern gate in the Fleet-fast.","You appraise the readiness of the guards stationed at the Fleet-fast barracks","Bruidis has taken on the responsibility for appraising the defences of the Fleet-fast, since her husband Rossaran's armour stands out too much for him to move about freely in this part of the city.","<rgb=#00FF00>Appraise</rgb> the eastern side of the Fleet-fast bridge","'What have you learned of the defences within the Fleet-fast, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You give your report to Bruidis and she thinks it over.\
\
'I see. If I believed most of the Corsairs' martial forces had perished at Pelargir, it seems that the Kindred of the Coins has rebuilt them enough to man the Fleet-fast, at least, very effectively. A frontal assault upon the Citadel of Winds is, in my opinion, out of the question.\
\
'I could not utilize Rossaran effectively in the Fleet-fast, so I sent him to conduct his investigation within the Lower Ward. Seek him out in the Lower Ward to the north and find out what he learned while he was there.'","<rgb=#00FF00>Appraise</rgb> the barracks in the Fleet-fast","Rossaran is to the north of the Fleet-fast, in the Lower Ward.","You appraise the quality and number of guards that patrol the eastern end of the Fleet-fast bridge","The City: The Strategist and the Swan-knight","<rgb=#00FF00>Appraise</rgb> the western side of the Fleet-fast bridge"},
[11889]={"Talk to Driftwood outside the arena in the Tor-gardens","Driftwood has asked to you meet you in the Tor-gardens.","Talk to visitors to the Tor-gardens about what the future might hold for Driftwood (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'I should not remain in this district. It is not safe for me to stay here. Let us continue on to the Tor-gardens, ${PLAYER}. There we will speak, and I will find it easier to resist my more dangerous impulses.'","'This place is better for me.'","Driftwood asked you to speak with visitors to the Tor-gardens about what the future might hold for such a man as he.","Talk to Driftwood in the Tor-gardens","'Old habits are the hardest to lose, ${PLAYER}, and in another life I preyed upon the wealthy merchants and nobles who sailed upon the River Anduin. I relieved them of their wealth, at least, and in some cases of their lives as well. Even today I feel the pull of that life, though I have spent the years since then seeking to leave it behind me.\
\
'What might have happened had I succumbed to that pull again? Had I climbed through one of the windows of a mansion in the Upper Ward and stolen the valuables I found within, would I be seized by the guards? Would I have been brought to yon building, there to fight and die for my crime? Would that have been right?\
\
'I am curious about this, friend. Ask some of the folk nearby what might have happened to me in that case. I am interested to know.'","'What did visitors to this place have to say about my future, ${PLAYER}? To what ending do they believe I will come to when I breathe my last?'\
\
You recount the words of the folk with whom you spoke, and Driftwood listens intently.\
\
'They are all right, my friend, and they are all wrong. How can this be so? It is because you asked them what would happen if I gave in to my thieving impulses and returned to my past life, and I do not doubt that I would arrive at one of those endings if I did.\
\
'But it is possible for a man to change, even one such as I am. I strive every day to prove it. It is not easy. But it is worth it.\
\
'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. None of those endings are mine today... and for today that is enough.'","You found Driftwood wandering through the Upper Ward, wrestling with himself about a personal matter.","'I do not know why I came to the Upper Ward; something compelled my feet to bring me hither. I find myself eyeing the upper stories of the manors and mansions of this district, and wondering if the windows might be unlocked, the balcony doors unbarred. It is a remnant of my old life that brings these thoughts to me, a relic of the brigand once I was.\
\
'I should not remain in this district. It is not safe for me to stay here. Let us continue on to the Tor-gardens, ${PLAYER}. There we will speak, and I will find it easier to resist my more dangerous impulses.'","The City: Today's Endings","'What might have happened had I succumbed to that pull again? Had I climbed through one of the windows of a mansion in the Upper Ward and stolen the valuables I found within, would I be seized by the guards? Would I have been brought to yon building, there to fight and die for my crime? Would that have been right?\
\
'I am curious about this, friend. Ask some of the folk nearby what might have happened to me in that case. I am interested to know.'","Driftwood is by the arena in the Tor-gardens.","Meet up with Driftwood in the Tor-gardens","'You ask what might happen to a friend of yours that steals? I can answer this very simply for you. Is he of the nobility? For if he is a nobleman, I say he is likely to escape judgement. If he is from the Lower Ward, I do not like his chances. Consider Hármelak, the Golden Queen! Her family has always been wealthy, but you cannot tell me that all of her dealings are and have ever been aboveboard!\
\
'What is your friend's station in life? That will determine not only if he can commit his theft and live, but also how rich a lifestyle he will be able to maintain... and the duration of it!'","'This is most unusual. You want to know what might happen to a friend of yours that commits a crime, such as theft or burglary? If he is not caught by the guards and slain at once, it is true that he might request a trial by combat in the arena, where he would need to face one of the Hûliz. These are the gladiators who make their living in the arena by dealing death, and unless your friend is very skilled, he is not like to survive it.\
\
'His chances decrease to near zero if he has the misfortune of drawing Rothog the Storm for an opponent. He is the deadliest fighter I have ever seen!\
\
'I would advise your friend not to steal. This ending, to me, seems most likely: death for him, and for any who aid him!'","'You want to know what will happen to your friend if he begins a life of theft and burglary? I do not have enough information to answer this for you. The reason? I do not know how skilled he is at this trade!\
\
'Yes, I call it a trade. If you speak to others about this matter, they will tell you he will be caught or killed by the guards, or be sent to face Rothog the Storm in the arena, or fall to his death from an upper balcony when he seeks to escape notice. But I say differently.\
\
'I think if he is well-practiced at the art of thievery, he might well escape and live a long and full life feasting upon the fruits of his labours! It can be so in other areas... why not burglary as well?'"},
[11890]={"'The Heirs of Castamir, in league with the Empire of Ordâkh and the Church of the All Seeing, ruled this city for many years... but now their star has fallen so low that their supporters consist mainly of brigands and lawless toughs. They are no match for such as we are, ${PLAYER}, but they do not yet understand it.'","Elladan and Elrohir were approached by a man in the Lower Ward who claimed to have information for them, but the brothers are not certain he can be trusted.","Talk to Elrohir by one of the farms to the east, outside the city","You have successfully defended the Elves from their attackers","'Will you join us when we go to speak with this man? He suggested a location far to the east, beside one of the farms outside the city.'","The City: Watched and Watchful","'I do not know if this man speaks the truth, but we should hear what he has to say, should we not?'","'We are about to see if this is a trap, ${PLAYER}. But what is of most interest to me is learning if the predator is actually the prey, as I suspect may be the case. These Men likely do not have much occasion to see Elves, after all.'","Elladan is by the White Gate on the eastern side of the Lower Ward.","'I told Elrohir I do not trust this man... but that is not enough for us to refuse him.\
\
'I suspect he would need many men indeed to get the better of us. Will you join us when we go to speak with him? He suggested a location far to the east, beside one of the farms outside the city.'","Talk to Elladan outside the White Gate on the eastern side of the Lower Ward","Talk to Elladan at the White Gate on the eastern side of the Lower Ward","Elladan and Elrohir agreed to meet you back outside the White Gate on the eastern side of the Lower Ward of the city.","Elladan and Elrohir have decided to investigate the man's information, meeting him beside one of the farms outside the city.","Talk to Elrohir outside the White Gate on the eastern side of the Lower Ward","'My brother and I were walking through the Lower Ward of the city when a man approached us and said he had information for the two of us. I do not know if he speaks the truth, but we should hear what he has to say. If we are watched, we will be watchful too. It is the wise course, is it not?'","You have failed to protect the Elves!","'So it was a trap, but it turns out it was a trap in which the ones who set it were the first caught. That is a pity for them, but perhaps it will teach other supporters of the Heirs of Castamir not to cause trouble for us in the days to come.\
\
'Their mention of \\qElves from the oasis\\q is very interesting! I have not heard of Elves living across the southern desert before. I would learn more about them, and I am sure Elrohir feels similarly! It is most intriguing.'"},
[11891]={"'Iba de vuelta a Herne cuando esos malditos me atacaron. He visto lo que quería ver, así que volveré y te veré allí.\
\
'¡No! No necesito ayuda para volver. Un amigo vendrá a buscarme. Sin embargo, puedes usar tus habilidades de otra forma. Expulsa a los orcos que se han infiltrado en Tharbad. Si sobrevives, ver a verme a Herne con sus orejas cuando hayas acabado, y te recompensaré.'","Los orcos han infestado las ruinas de la antigua ciudad de Tharbad. ¡Cadwallon Nevit, alcalde de Herne, no permitirá que continúe esta profanación!","La purificación de Tharbad","Consigue orejas de orco cortadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Deberías llevar las orejas de orco cortadas al alcalde Cadwallon Nevit.\
\
El alcalde Nevit ha vuelto a Herne, en el centro de Cardolan.","El alcalde Cadwallon Nevit te ha pedido que acabes con los orcos en las ruinas de Tharbad.\
\
Tharbad se encuentra en el sudoeste de Cardolan.","Lleva las orejas al alcalde Nevit","'Así que has vuelto. Te lo agradezco. Algún día Tharbad será nuestra de nuevo.'","Orejas de orco cortadas conseguidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[11892]={"Garrun is encamped against a cliff face far to the west of Forthbrond, north of Cuvnerth.\
\
Ardwyn has asked you to seek out the scout Garrun at the western edge of the Isendale and lend him your aid.","The Cleft Rumbles","Talk to Garrun in the Isendale","'Hail, ${PLAYER}! I was told to expect you. You are highly regarded by many of our captains here in Dunland, and I am honoured to make your acquaintance.\
\
'There have been massive movements of Dunlending forces to and from Wulf's Cleft, and we have much work ahead of us.'","Following the rout at Brôntrig, Ardwyn proposes shifting his forces' focus in the Isendale.","'With our defeat at Brôntrig, we must refocus our efforts in the Isendale. The army at Wulf's Cleft is growing stronger with every passing day, and we must now turn our attention to weakening that force.\
\
'Garrun, another of my scouts, has encamped near Wulf's Cleft to observe their muster and report on their movements. You should join him there and lend him what aid you may.\
\
'Journey due west into the valleys until you reach the cliff face north of Cuvnerth, another village of the Dunlendings.'","'Find Garrun, ${PLAYER}, and lend him your aid.'"},
[11894]={"Habla con Gil Plover fuera del laberinto en los Campos de Caballos","'¡Hola, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}! ¿No es un hermoso día de primavera? Este es justo el tipo de clima que hace que un festival sea tan agradable, con las suaves brisas y los nuevos verdes brillantes. ¿Estás mirando ese laberinto allá? Eso es justo lo que yo estaba pensando también. ¡Es un gran día para perderse entre el follaje!\
\
¿Así que quieres probar suerte eligiendo un camino? Es un objetivo digno. Yo fui el otro día, en tiempo récord. Te aseguro que no puedes atravesarlo ni aunque te diera mucho más tiempo del habitual. De hecho, estaría dispuesto a apostar un buen premio en ese mismo reto.\
\
¡Grita si te pierdes y necesitas que vaya a buscarte! No pensaré menos de ti -- algunas personas se pierden bastante en tal confusión de caminos. Pero no camines tan rápido que olvides disfrutar los dulces aromas de las cosas verdes que crecen, porque no los encontrarás en otra época del año.'","La salida del laberinto de setos está por aquí en algún lugar... ¿o no?\
\
Deberías intentar encontrar la salida antes de que se acabe el tiempo. Gil Plover salió en un instante comparado con el tiempo que te han dado.","Gil Plover está de pie cerca del laberinto de setos, que está muy cerca del recinto del festival de las Tierras de Bree, al norte de Bree.\
\
Deberías hablar con Gil Plover, para demostrarle que pudiste superar su reto y atravesar el laberinto en un tiempo admirable.","Has encontrado la salida","'¿Te atreves a aceptar mi reto?'","Encuentra la salida antes de que se acabe el tiempo","La entrada al laberinto de setos está cerca del recinto del festival en los Campos de Caballos, al norte de Bree.\
\
Gil Plover te ha retado a atravesar el laberinto, de principio a fin, antes de que se acabe el tiempo.","Gil Plover, el Maestro del Laberinto de Bree, te ha retado a atravesar el laberinto antes de que se acabe el tiempo. ¡No te demores dentro de los muros de setos!\
\
<rgb=#FF0000> NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu bitácora de misiones cuando termine el festival actual. </rgb>","Se te ha acabado el tiempo","'¡Oh! ¡Me sorprendiste! No esperaba verte por lo menos en varias horas. Lo hiciste bastante bien, ${PLAYER}, pero tienes que ir mucho más rápido si quieres superar mi tiempo. Pero no importa; estoy impresionado de todos modos.\
\
Pensándolo bien, ¡mereces una recompensa! Acepta este símbolo de mi respeto para un aprendiz de Maestro del Laberinto. Espero que hayas disfrutado de la vegetación tanto como yo cuando pasé por allí.''","El Sendero Hendido","Entra al laberinto"},
[11895]={"'The gwiber spread like a plague across Thrór's Coomb, but your efforts will at least slow their growth.'","'In the valley below, gwiber have begun to emerge from their caves in the mountains and build new nests. With each new gwiber, the creatures will grow in power and will eventually overrun the whole of Thrór's Coomb.  \
\
'Not only do the gwiber themselves need to be destroyed, but their eggs as well, so as to stem their growth. Would you do that for us?\
\
'Travel south across the river and seek nests full of eggs. Destroy these, then return to me here.'","Destroyed gwiber egg-clutches  (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Destroy gwiber egg-clutches (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Frithgeir is at Zudrugund, north of the gwiber-nests. \
\
You should return to Frithgeir and inform him that you have destroyed many gwiber-eggs.","'Gwiber are foul beasts and dangerous, and they are fast becoming a threat to all the peoples of Enedwaith.'","Talk to Frithgeir at Zudrugund","Gwiber-nests may be found to the south of Zudrugund.\
\
Frithgeir has asked you to hunt down nests of gwiber-eggs and destroy them.","The Clutch Collapses","In the valley below, in the eastern reaches of Thrór's Coomb, gwiber have begun building nests to swell their numbers."},
[11896]={"'¿Qué tienes ahí, ${PLAYER}? ¡Ah! ¿Acaso esos hermosos cristales eran el origen de la luz que vi, y no un fuego de trasgo? ¡Es maravilloso! Podemos recolectar esos cristales para hacer lámparas en estas tierras desoladas.'","Cristal de color conseguido (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Öndótt ha visto una luz extraña que proviene de un extremo lejano de la Vieja Ciudad del Cuerno de Plata y quiere que averigües de dónde viene.","Los colores de los cristales","Encuentra el origen de la luz (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Öndótt se encuentra en lo alto de la escalera de la Vieja Ciudad del Cuerno de Plata.\
\
Deberías volver a ver a Öndótt con los cristales que has conseguido.","'He visto una extraña luz multicolor que proviene del extremo más alejado de esta antigua ciudad, ${PLAYER}. ¿Qué podrá ser? ¿Irías a echar un vistazo? ¡Me preocupa que haya alguna hoguera de trasgos cerca y que estén a punto de abalanzarse sobre nosotros!'","La extraña luz provenía del extremo más alejado de la Vieja Ciudad del Cuerno de Plata, desde donde se encuentra Öndótt.\
\
Deberías encontrar el origen de esa extraña luz.","Lleva los cristales a Öndótt"},
[11897]={"Defeat Uruk-hai Raiders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Coming Storm","'The hour has come, ${PLAYER}. We have received no answer from Théoden King to our request for reinforcements, and Reeve Athelward has made it known that our fate is now our own. Retreat is not an option, we must stand against the first waves of the coming storm.\
\
'I think now upon my father's training and his wisdom. I must rally my people, and trust in the great skill of the Elfward. I ask that you ride north and assist Norbald with the defences. You have done much to help the people of Faldham, we must not let it fall in its most crucial moment!'","Norbald awaits at the north-west part of Enswith's farm.\
\
Norbald needs to know that you have repelled several of the mounted Orcs approaching Faldham.","'You are not a moment too soon! The first waves of the Uruk force have begun to arrive in earnest. We must hold off the enemy's riders, and grant Thane Elfmar and the others a moment to rally.'","Defeat Uruk-hai Skirmishers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Fine work, that ought to slow the enemy's advance. We have stopped their first efforts but we must not lower our guard, there will surely be more on the way.'","Speak to Norbald at Enswith's farm, north of the mead hall","Thane Elfmar begins the rally of the Elfward for the imminent siege of Faldham. Some of the Elfward have already gone to secure the perimeter farms, and to repel the enemy's scouts.","Speak to Norbald at Enswith's farm","Defeated Uruk-hai Raiders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The enemy Uruk-hai can be found west of Norbald's location, north of the mead hall.\
\
Norbald has asked for your help in repelling the mounted Uruk-hai approaching Faldham.","Defeated Uruk-hai Skirmishers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Norbald can be found at the north-west edge of Endwith's farm, north-east of the mead hall.\
\
Norbald has gone to scout the enemy forces at the perimeter of Enswith's farm."},
[11900]={"The Commander of Zudramdân","Commander Mozgúth can be found at Zudramdân.\
\
You should find and defeat Commander Mozgúth.","You have successfully defeated Commander Mozgúth.","When conflict broke out, Zudramdân was the first hold to be lost to the Orkish forces of Gundabad.","'I have urgent need of someone with your skill set, ${PLAYER}. There is a vile Orkish leader, Commander Mozgúth. He has taken control of the ruins of Zudramdân! Yes, you have heard me correctly! We had only recently secured those ruins for ourselves. When the war began, we could not hold Zudramdân and had to fall back. I ask of you, infiltrate Zudramdân, find their commander, and defeat the Orc wretch. Can I count on you?'","Commander Mozgúth has been defeated","You have successfully defeated Commander Mozgúth. Those with the war effort will be pleased with what you have accomplished today.","Find and defeat Commander Mozgúth","Completado"},
[11901]={"Eiricháv can be found in north west Câr Bronach.\
\
You should complete quests for the hillmen in Eiricháv.","Complete: 'Cave Growth' with Fuisach","Eiricháv can be found in north west Câr Bronach.\
\
You should travel to Eiricháv.","Complete: 'Thwarting the Iron Pass' with Suilgál","'While we have managed to take Grúmachath, our numbers are too little to succeed against the Angmarim and Dourhands. If the Gabil'akkâ is to succeed in Câr Bronach, we may need some allies. I have sent my best scout, Uzvát, to seek out potential allies in the mountains. My hopes were not high.\
\
'To my surprise, Uzvát returned with word of a group of hillmen working against the Angmarim. They work from a secret cave, high upon the slopes to the north. You and Uzvát are to return to Eiricháv and offer our assistance. We must show these hillmen that the Zhélruka are willing to work with them to hurry their cause.'","Enter Eiricháv","'This is the cave of Eiricháv, ${PLAYER}. I have already made an initial contact with the group. It seems your name precedes you, as a couple of the hillmen seem to already know who you are. They are expecting you within, my friend.'","Talk to Soltakh of the Trév Gállorg in Eiricháv","Eiricháv can be found in north west Câr Bronach.\
\
You should enter Eiricháv.","Uzvát knows this cave to be the entrance to Eiricháv","Travel to Eiricháv","'It has been a long while, ${PLAYER}. I would wager that you did not expect to see those of the Trév Dúvardain and the Trév Gállorg working as one. Yet, here we are.\
\
'You have met our leader, Domongart, before. He is on an urgent mission of diplomacy in the north. That is all that I can say. I have heard from Uzvát that you wish to assist us in our efforts. You have assisted me in the past. I know that you will be able to do so once more, old friend.\
\
'The Trév Duvárdain have been sundered by choice. Many remain loyal to the Iron Crown. Those here see the folly in servitude. Assist us in our efforts here and then we will consider returning the favour to assist the Zhélruka.'","Eiricháv can be found in north west Câr Bronach.\
\
You should talk to Uzvát outside Eiricháv.","Complete: 'A Warning to Tâg Fógarrach' with Monathár","Familiar echoes command you further into the cave","Eiricháv can be found in north west Câr Bronach.\
\
You should talk to Soltakh of the Trév Gállorg in Eiricháv.","The Zhélruka expedition and a faction of hillmen may share a common goal and common enemy upon the slopes of Câr Bronach.","The Common Enemy","Complete: 'Roots of the Land' with Aighrig","Talk to Uzvát outside Eiricháv","'You have done well. We thank you for your assistance. Just as you have already done, I continue to make a name for myself in these lands.'"},
[11902]={"The Conquest of Dor Amarth","Ingold, a soldier of Gondor, has scouted Dor Amarth and found many foes still remain.","Ingold has asked you to defeat foes in Dor Amarth.","'Many foes still wander throughout Dor Amarth. If you find yourself travelling in these lands, you should defeat any foes you come across.'","Enemigos derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","A notice is pinned to the board, signed by Ingold:\
\
'Many foes still wander throughout Dor Amarth. A brave adventurer is needed to defeat foes in these lands.'","Defeat foes in Dor Amarth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[11903]={"Bregdal, a soldier of Gondor, has scouted Talath Úrui and found many foes still remain.","Bregdal has asked you to defeat foes in Talath Úrui.","Defeat foes in Talath Úrui (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Many foes still wander throughout Talath Úrui. If you find yourself travelling in these lands, you should defeat any foes you come across.'","A notice is pinned to the board, signed by Bregdal:\
\
'Many foes still wander throughout Talath Úrui. A brave adventurer is needed to defeat foes in these lands.'","Enemigos derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Conquest of Talath Úrui"},
[11904]={"'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para partir? No sé qué está ocurriendo dentro de la cámara de enfriamiento, pero sé que debemos movernos rápido si queremos averiguarlo.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Nota: Esta instancia está pensada para un jugador en solitario, pero puede completarse con hasta dos personas en una comunidad.</rgb>","Habla con Slagvi en el campamento del Mirador de la Gran Excavación","Slagvi se encuentra en el campamento del Mirador de la Gran Excavación.\
\
Slagvi desea entrar en la Cámara de Enfriamiento con la esperanza de restaurar el sistema de agua natural de la Gran Excavación a un estado funcional.","Explora la cámara de enfriamiento con Slagvi","La cámara de enfriamiento ha sido restaurada","Slagvi se encuentra en el campamento del Mirador de la Gran Excavación.\
\
Deberías hablar con Slagvi.","'${PLAYER}, me gustaría saber más sobre por qué los sistemas de agua de la Gran Excavación no están en funcionamiento. No me agrada la idea de que nuestra expedición tenga que depender de agua importada.\
\
'Hay una Cámara de Enfriamiento no muy lejos de aquí, y quizá deberíamos investigarla. No soy ajeno a este tipo de sistemas, así que creo que podré ser útil para intentar ponerlo de nuevo en funcionamiento.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Nota: Esta instancia está pensada para un jugador en solitario, pero puede completarse con hasta dos personas en una comunidad.</rgb>","La Cámara de Enfriamiento es una antigua estructura utilizada para recoger, enfriar y purificar el vapor caliente de las forjas que se encuentran debajo.","La Cámara de Enfriamiento","'¡Gracias por tu ayuda, ${PLAYER}! No habría podido restaurar esos sistemas yo solo con tantos trasgos alrededor. Has hecho mucho por el campamento del Mirador de la Gran Excavación, pero creo que ya estamos preparados para valernos por nosotros mismos. ¡El Descenso Profundo te espera!'"},
[11905]={"El Auge de los Corcur","'¿Los Corcur han llegado a vivir dentro de los muros de Helegrod? Ese lugar es maligno, y no dudo que el poder oscuro de Angmar pretenda usar a estos nuevos aliados para alguna fechoría.\
\
'Debemos poner fin a este mal, ${PLAYER}.'","'Mis hijos han establecido un campamento, Thorenhad, entre las Gargantas del Bruinen, al oeste de Imladris. Desde allí vigilan las tierras salvajes del Bosque de los Trolls en busca de señales del Enemigo. Elladan estará muy interesado en oír sobre los Corcur que ahora habitan Helegrod.'","elladan está en Thorenhad, su campamento entre las Gargantas del Bruinen, al oeste de Rivendel.\
\
El señor Elrond te ha pedido que lleves noticias sobre los Corcur, que ahora viven en Helegrod bajo el poder de Angmar, a su hijo Elladan, quien ha luchado contra ellos durante mucho tiempo.","'Los montañeses de Rhudaur se fragmentaron en muchas facciones tras los combates que quebraron el Reino del Norte, y muchos siguieron viviendo entre las ruinas dispersas por la naturaleza salvaje del Bosque de los Trolls. Muchos intentaron cruzar los pasos de las montañas, pero la mayoría fue vencida por la nieve en las alturas. Los que sobrevivieron tomaron el nombre de Corcur y aún viven en tierras duras.\
\
'Siempre guardaron rencor por su derrota antigua, buscando sin descanso aliados poderosos que les ayudaran a recuperar lo que perdieron. En Angmar encontraron al aliado que buscaban, y los Corcur habitan ahora en Helegrod al servicio de la voluntad de Angmar.\
\
'Mi hijo Elladan ha combatido a los Corcur durante largo tiempo y conoce bien sus costumbres. Habla con él en su campamento de Thorenhad, entre las Gargantas del Bruinen, al oeste de Imladris.'","'Mis hijos son fuertes y mantienen la vigilancia en Thorenhad en busca de signos del Enemigo.'","Los Corcur de las Montañas Nubladas cayeron bajo la influencia de los Angmarim que ahora controlan Helegrod.","'Los Corcur siempre han sido peligrosos para quienes no están preparados, pero sus nuevos aliados los vuelven enemigos aún más mortíferos.'"},
[11906]={"You have entered into the láthbear den","Find and enter the láthbear den","Sahard resides at his farm just east of the Faldham mead hall.\
\
Sahard awaits at his farmstead for the outcome of your endeavours against the láthbear sloth.","Nothwulf can be found inside the mead hall of Faldham.\
\
Nothwulf will be eager to hear the news of the defeat of the láthbear threat.","Defeat the láthbear matrons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'It is as I feared. The spirits will not be intimidated, and our problem can only be resolved when the matrons of the sloth have been dealt with.\
\
'Finding the matrons may prove difficult, the láthbears have been secluded in darkness, lurking among the shadows of the valley to the east. I believe this is where their den may lie. Search for the láthbear den beyond the trees, and eliminate any matrons found within. Take courage, for the dark spirits that infest the láthbears may still be restless within their dwelling.\
\
'I must soon return to Faldham. The hour draws near, and I am needed by my allies. When you have seen to these matters, speak to Sahard at his home. Good fortune to you, ${PLAYER}.'","Return to Sahard with news of the láthbear matrons","Nothwulf awaits news of the láthbear threat","Speak to Nothwulf in Faldham","Inhere believes that the most permanent solution to the láthbear menace will be to disrupt the Matrons of the sloth, that dwell within the hill caves east of Faldham.","The láthbear matrons lie hidden in the den east of Faldham, beyond the curtain of trees.\
\
Inhere is convinced that the láthbears will not relent until the possessed matrons have been overthrown.","'Admirably handled, ${PLAYER}! Without their matrons, the láthbear numbers should be fragile enough so as not to risk assaulting our homes directly.\
\
'I will endeavour to pass on the tale of your deeds, so that the accounts of the láthbears' danger might be heeded as a warning of true peril, and not told as a harmless fable or children's tale. Had you not intervened, we may have learned a most difficult lesson. Return to Nothwulf and put his mind at ease.'","The láthbear den lies hidden in the valleys of  hills east of Faldham, beyond the woods.\
\
Inhere believes that the láthbear matrons dwell within a cave, and has asked you to find this den within the valley.","The Corrupted Matrons","Defeated láthbear matrons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I am encouraged that we were able to prevent these láthbear beasts from overwhelming the people of Faldham. With one danger behind us, I look only to facing the Orc threat.\
\
'You have my gratitude, ${PLAYER}.'"},
[11907]={"'¡${PLAYERNAME:Bienhallado[m]|Bienhallada[f]}, ! Es bueno verte de nuevo.","Purifica la estatua corrompida de Elendil en Tyl Ruinen","'¿Has purificado la estatua corrompida? ¡Me alegro!'","'Te he dado un brebaje purificador para que lo uses en la estatua de Elendil en Tyl Ruinen, al este. ¿Has cambiado de opinión y decidido abandonarla a las salamandras?'","Lithuifin te ha dado un brebaje purificador con el que limpiar la estatua corrupta de Elendil en Tyl Ruinen.","'La estatua de Elendil en Tyl Ruinen todavía no ha sido purificada.'","'¿Gwindeth te envía? No cruza a menudo la cascada que cubre la entrada a su hogar, pero la he visto bajo los árboles de cuando en cuando.\
\
'Conozco el gran respeto que profesaba a los reyes de Annúminas, y los que ellos le profesaban a ella. Se dice que el ultimo rey de la ciudad le pidió que alzara las aguas del lago Nenuial para que cubriera los muros, pero no sé por qué pediría una cosa así.\
\
'¿Buscas un brebaje que pueda limpiar la piedra de la corrupción de las salamandras? Puedo darte uno. Llévalo a Tyl Ruinen y úsalo para restaurar la estatua de la que hablas. ¡No hay nada que agradecer! Es suficiente con tener una breve y refrescante conversación con alquien nuevo... Ramalarga habla muy lentamente como hacen los suyos, y Erchiel ya no tiene paciencia para mis travesuras, ¡aunque eso habla en su favor!'","La estatua corrompida","La estatua corrupta de Elendil está en una de las islas de Tyl Ruinen, al sur.\
\
Lithuifin te ha dado un brebaje para limpiar una de las estatuas de Elendil en Tyl Ruinen."},
[11908]={"The woman grimaces at your approach.\
\
'Apologies. My injuries -- they are minor, but not at all painless. I didn't notice the Corsairs until it was too late.\
\
'You are a ${CLASS}, are you not? My daughter and I wish to return to Melgobas, but with Corsairs brazenly roaming so close to the road, I do not like our chances.\
\
'Their encampment lies to the north-east. If you can cause trouble and defeat some of them, I'd feel better about those chances.'","You have defeated enough Corsairs.\
\
You should let Sadrech know at her camp.","Talk to Sadrech at her camp","Defeat Corsairs at Bel Tâkhmar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Corsairs of Bel Tâkhmar","Sadrech has asked you to defeat Corsairs at Bel Tâkhmar.\
\
The encampment can be found north-east of her camp.","Corsarios derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I shall rest easier now. Many thanks, ${CLASS}.'","The Corsairs' presence in Anfalas weighs heavily on Sadrech's mind."},
[11910]={"The Cost of Corruption","Defeat the Angmarim overseers","'Well done, friend. Gunvald was right about your prowess. I suspect many will be the songs that sing of your glory when this is all over.'","Brágha Fellwinder has gone to the tower of Caivád Sâr, in central Elderslade.\
\
You should defeat Brágha Fellwinder before she can pass on the knowledge of the crystals and the corruption her spells bring.","Brágha Fellwinder must be defeated before she can pass on her fell knowledge.","Borghild is in the Angmarim tower of Caivád Sâr in central Elderslade.\
\
Talk to Borghild.","Defeated the Angmarim overseers","Defeat Natmoz","Talk to Borghild","Defeated Brágha Fellwinder","'My eyes and ears are better than my sword arm, or I would join you in this task.'","Defeated Natmoz","Defeat Brágha Fellwinder"},
[11911]={"Talk to Doron","'This symbol fills me with dread and invokes in me a feeling I have not felt since the day my men and I became cursed.\
\
'I failed Gondor at Ost Celebrant, the large fortress to the south, and condemned myself and my men to this unnatural existence. \
\
'You must be told what happened, else you can never understand my fate.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This instance quest is meant to be run Solo and cannot be run in a group.</rgb>","'So, now you understand my past. After a time, a few of my men and I returned to the front with Cirion, but by then, word had spread of our treachery. \
\
'Cirion cursed all of us and condemned us to serve until the Horde no longer posed a threat to Gondor.\
\
'I feel my guilt, but I do not understand what can be done to lift my curse. The Easterlings are just unorganized raiders...how would they ever pose a threat to Gondor now? These are puzzling times, ${PLAYER}....'","The Cost of Loyalty","After looking over the crude symbol you recovered from the brigands, Doron has decided to share how he and his men came to be cursed.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This instance quest is meant to be run Solo and cannot be run in a group.</rgb>","Doron is among his men on the Field of Celebrant.\
\
Doron wishes to tell you the tale of the Oatbreakers' curse.","Doron is among his men on the Field of Celebrant.\
\
You should speak with Doron regarding the tale he told you.","'Let me tell you the tale. Listen to me, and you will understand.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This instance quest is meant to be run Solo and cannot be run in a group.</rgb>"},
[11912]={"Remove disgusting harbour-filth from the waters of the Sail-haven (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'It is a great shame of mine that the harbour has been left in such disarray since the Mutiny's end. There are vast patches of filth floating in the water, and it seems that almost every morning, I wake to the news that another Heirsworn traitor has 'mysteriously' found their way into the waters of the Sail-haven.\
\
'As Captain of the Haven, I have many duties that demand my attention, and as obvious a problem as this is, I simply have not had the time or men to spare to see to it. I know what I ask of you, so I will see to it that you are well-compensated for this task.\
\
'Will you help me to cleanse the harbour?'","Removed disgusting harbour-filth from the waters of the Sail-haven (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Costs of Mutiny","'It is unpleasant work, but I am afraid it is necessary, especially in the wake of the Mutiny.\
\
'It will not be long before the rest of the Heirsworn are routed or slain, but I only hope that some of my kinsmen will give more careful thought to where they dispose of them. After all, these are our waters!'","Disgusting harbour-filth and the bodies of Heirsworn traitors can be found in the waters of the Sail-haven.\
\
Eshmun has asked you to help cleanse the waters of the Sail-haven by clearing it of filth and the bodies of Heirsworn traitors.","Remove Heirsworn traitors from the waters of the Sail-haven (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Removed Heirsworn traitors from the waters of the Sail-haven (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","In the aftermath of the Sea-stone Munity, the waters of the Sail-haven have been befouled by filth and the corpses of those found to still harbour loyalties to the Heirs of Castamir.","Talk to Eshmun at the Harbour-warden's Tower","Eshmun, Captain of the Haven, can be found at the Harbour-warden's Tower in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.\
\
You have done a great deal to cleanse the waters of the Sail-haven. You should return to Eshmun."},
[11913]={"The Dome of the Sun is filled with the scattered notes of the recent meeting of the Council.\
\
Arodor asked if you would gather up the scattered papers within the Dome of the Sun.","Arodor is in the Dome of the Sun, writing resolutions recently decided by the Council of Gondor.","'Echadon sent you? I have nothing to say to him. As the Warden of the Green, it is my duty to preserve the townlands and its people. I refuse now as I refused then to call back the few scouts and guards that now defend them! They are the folk who will first face the swords and axes of the Orcs!\
\
'Ah, I have recovered my temper. The Council dismissed his suggestion. That made me feel rather better.\
\
'I have compiled a report of the situation on the Pelennor Fields. Can I trust you to deliver it to Thalhír, the Warden of Laws? Many of the farms there have been evacuated, and this report may help their owners receive recompense if their homes are destroyed by the Orcs. Thalhír can be found in the Second Circle of the city.'","Talk to Arodor in the Dome of the Sun","'What is this? It is a report concerning the land holdings of folk who had to abandon their homes on the Pelennor? I see. I suppose Parthadan is doing his duty to take care of the townlands by preparing this report, but I think he is dreaming if he thinks the city will repay the owners of these farms for any damage the Orcs inflict upon them.'\
\
Thalhír snorts mirthlessly.\
\
'He may be dreaming if he thinks there will be anyone left to repay them, ${PLAYER}. The word out of Osgiliath is not good, and the army arrayed against us sounds vast.\
\
'Well, I promise nothing, but bring this report back to Arodor for filing. If we do survive the siege that must be coming, we may need paper to burn, and Parthadan's report may be good for that, at least.'","Arodor is in the Dome of the Sun.","'You have just missed a meeting of the Council, but if you go within you may be able to lend some aid to Arodor, chief scribe of the Council. The meetings have been contentious of late, and the number of raised voices I have heard from my position here has only increased in recent days.'","Talk to Parthadan, Warden of the Green, in the south-east section of the Sixth Circle","Bring scattered papers to Arodor in the Dome of the Sun","Deliver the resolution to Celephir in the Citadel","Wait for Arodor to finish writing the Council Resolutions","Parthadan, the Warden of the Green, can be found in the Sixth Circle of the city.\
\
Echadon asked you to find Parthadan once you finished delivering the Council resolutions throughout the city.","Arodor is in the Dome of the Sun, writing out the resolutions of the Council.","'Can I trust you to deliver that report to Thalhír, the Warden of Laws? Many of the farms there have been evacuated, and this report may help their owners receive recompense if their homes are destroyed by the Orcs. Thalhír can be found in the Second Circle of the city.'","'Welcome, ${PLAYER}, to the Dome of the Sun. Word of your deeds is moving throughout the city like a fire in the brush. It sounds as if you have had many adventures, and saved many good folk from the swords and axes of evil! May you continue to do so on our behalf, worthy ${CLASS}!\
\
'You have just missed a meeting of the Council, but if you go within you may be able to lend some aid to Arodor, chief scribe of the Council. The meetings have been contentious of late, and the number of raised voices I have heard from my position here has only increased in recent days. It seems no two voices can agree on a single course of action, for each member of the Council has his own interests to look after. Can they not see that we must be united if we are to survive the coming storm?\
\
'Ah, I am just a doorward. It is not my place to speak so. There are some in the city who speak against the Council, but you will not find me speaking such sedition!'","You have agreed to deliver resolutions of the Council to several leaders of the city throughout Minas Tirith:\
\
Torchún, the Warden of the Houses of Healing.\
Echadon, the Captain of the Garrison.\
Celephir, the Warden of the Coffers.\
Mirudil, the Warden of the Stores.","Deliver the resolution to Mirudil in the south-east section of the Fifth Circle","Arodor is in the Dome of the Sun.\
\
You have gathered up the scattered papers that remained behind after the meeting of the Council of Gondor, and should bring them to Arodor.","The Council of Gondor meets within the Dome of the Sun to decide matters of state. Their meetings have been more frequent of late as the situation in Gondor worsens.","'I am grateful that you have brought the Council's resolution to me with such haste, ${PLAYER}. As the Warden of the Coffers, it is my duty to maintain the guard upon the treasury.\
\
'To my relief, the Council agreed with my proposal that the guard upon the treasury doors be increased. If the city is soon besieged, as seems certain, the gravest threat to the coin of the city might not be the enemies outside the walls but the folk within them. Indeed, an unsavoury group has already begun speaking out against the Council and the Steward, and I am sure they would try and pilfer the treasury if given the opportunity.\
\
'I thank you once more for bringing this resolution to me.'","The Council of Gondor meets inside the Dome of the Sun on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.\
\
Othnar has invited you to enter the Dome of the Sun and lend your assistance to Arodor, chief scribe of the Council.","'Thank you for bringing this to me so quickly, ${PLAYER}. I am the Captain of the Garrison, which means the training and command of warriors in the city falls to me. I take this duty very seriously.\
\
'At the latest Council meeting, I spoke on behalf of my men. The garrison lacks the weapons and armour needed to mount a true defence of the city, should our enemies breach the gate. Furthermore, we simply do not have enough men! To that end, I argued that the scouts should be recalled from the Pelennor and Talath Anor and put to work as part of the garrison. Parthadan did not like this suggestion. When you have finished with this duty, perhaps you can see if his temper has cooled?\
\
'The Council did not agree with me, and there was much sympathy for the ideas of Parthadan. Still, the Guild of Smiths has been commanded to double its production of weapons and shields, so the men I do have can hope to be better equipped for the battle ahead. It is not everything for which I hoped, but it is something, at least.'","'Ah, thank you very much. Let me copy down any of the important matters from these papers, and then I will have another request for you. It will not be long.'","'I wonder if you might do me a favour? I need to finish organizing these papers. Perhaps you might gather up the rest of the notes scattered about the chamber? The members of the Council are masters of their various duties, but they trust that I will note down the matters of decision and do not stay behind to ensure I have recorded everything. I do my own duty as best I may, but I must ensure nothing slips by my notice amid the confusion.'","Bring the grim report to Thalhír in the north-east section of the Second Circle","'That was very fast, ${PLAYER}! Perhaps you should become an errand-rider for the city! I suppose it would be difficult for you to leave the adventuring life behind, but prompt delivery of messages is something to be prized, and you seem quite skilled at it.\
\
'As you know, I am the Warden of the Houses of Healing. At the Council-meeting that just concluded, I requested an increase in supplies and goods for the use of my healers: spare cloths, water for boiling, warm blankets. The Council agreed with the principle of my request, but not to its whole extent. I have been granted an increase, but a small one.\
\
'It is better than no increase at all, I suppose. We will take blankets and cloths from evacuated houses, for their owners have no current need of them, and I will arrange with the Warden of the Wells to provide me with spare buckets.'","'Ah, the Council resolutions are already written? That was very fast. It is good to see such haste, for it usually takes much longer for the orders of the Council to be put into action. Everyone is worried about what lies ahead, and it spurs them to move with haste.\
\
'I am the Warden of the Stores, which means that all the food and goods brought into the city fall within the scope of my duty. I find where they can be stored safely and free from theft or spoilage, and ensure that the folk who need access to them have it.\
\
'I must confess some trepidation to you, ${PLAYER}. If the city is besieged, I will surely become the most hated man in Minas Tirith. The man who rations the food is never loved by the hungry.\
\
'This resolution will allow me to conduct a full inventory of the stores, so I will know how much food and other supplies we will have at our disposal. If the gates are sealed by war, that inventory may become very important indeed!'","Enter the Dome of the Sun, where the Council of Gondor holds its meetings","Arodor is in the Dome of the Sun, on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.\
\
Thalhír asked you to deliver Parthadan's grim report to Arodor for filing.","Deliver the resolution to Torchún in the south-east section of the Sixth Circle","Arodor looks up from his work","'You have just missed a meeting of the Council, but if you go within you may be able to lend some aid to Arodor. The meetings have been contentious of late, and the number of raised voices I have heard from my position here has only increased in recent days.'","'Bring that report back to Arodor for filing. If we do survive the siege that must be coming, we may need paper to burn, and Parthadan's report may be good for that, at least.'","'Echadon wanted you to speak with Parthadan? That is a good idea, ${PLAYER}. The two of them became quite heated during the last Council meeting, and those bridges ought to be repaired before the next.'","A model of the White City stands in the centre of the room","'Yes? You must be ${PLAYER}, the ${CLASS} of whom Mithrandir speaks so highly. I am sorry to tell you that you have just missed a meeting of the Council. See the state in which they have left this place?\
\
'I wonder if you might do me a favour? I need to finish organizing these papers. Perhaps you might gather up the rest of the notes scattered about the chamber? The members of the Council are masters of their various duties, but they trust that I will note down the matters of decision and do not stay behind to ensure I have recorded everything. I do my own duty as best I may, but I must ensure nothing slips by my notice amid the confusion.'","Deliver the resolution to Echadon in the south section of the Second Circle","Gather the scattered papers in the Dome of the Sun (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bring the grim report to Arodor in the Dome of the Sun","Thalhír, the Warden of Laws, can be found in the Second Circle of the city.\
\
Parthadan gave you a grim report of the situation in the Pelennor to show to Thalhír.","'Thank you again for agreeing to deliver those resolutions, my friend. Here is the list of recipients:\
\
   Torchún, the Warden of the Houses of Healing.\
   Echadon, the Captain of the Garrison.\
   Celephir, the Warden of the Coffers.\
   Mirudil, the Warden of the Stores.\
\
'You will be doing the city a great service!'","'Thank you very much, ${PLAYER}. Those Council resolutions will help the defenders of Minas Tirith work to safe-guard the city!\
\
'I will take this report from you and make sure it is put in the proper place, but I share Thalhír's belief that we should first survive the battle before thinking about the aftermath!\
\
'I am sure I will see you again, friend. Take care of yourself until then.'","The Council of Gondor","Collected papers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'There we go! I have finished writing out the Council of Gondor's most recent resolutions. Now I need someone to bring these throughout the city so the city leaders can take the appropriate action. Normally I would send an errand-rider, but if you'd like to meet some members of the Council perhaps you would like to perform this duty?\
\
'Very good! Here is the stack of resolutions that will require immediate action. They are labeled with the correct recipient, do you see? Here is the list:\
\
   Torchún, the Warden of the Houses of Healing.\
   Echadon, the Captain of the Garrison.\
   Celephir, the Warden of the Coffers.\
   Mirudil, the Warden of the Stores.\
\
'Thank you for this, ${PLAYER}. You will be doing the city a great service!'"},
[11914]={"'The advisors are on their way here, and the council meeting should begin in a few moments.'","'I believe I may trust the council, as they were always loyal to my father, Heremond. However, I have doubts regarding some of their motivations.\
\
'Arnwi's observation about the missing guards is very troubling. Had they been there to help, my family might still live.\
\
'Nevertheless, I believe that speaking with the guards who remain at their posts will yield our best chance of discovering the source of the attack.'","Herubrand is in the cellar of the farmhouse near the farm fields of Woodhurst.\
\
Herubrand is gathering his advisors for a council meeting, at which you should be present.","The Council of Herubrand","'I feared that outcome, but am grateful for the truth. I vow to find whoever killed my wife and father and rout the evil from this city.\
\
'It is time my advisors and I discuss our plan. We must discover who was behind the attack and reclaim my seat in the mead hall. If I returned now, I feel it might become my tomb, as it almost did before.'","Herubrand has decided to meet with his council to discuss what should be done in the aftermath of the attack on the mead hall of Woodhurst.","Herubrand is in the cellar of the farmhouse.\
\
The council meeting has ended, and Herubrand wishes to speak with you.","Talk to Herubrand"},
[11915]={"'What is this? Orders from the Reeve? If this is what she truly desires....\
\
'Let the Reeve know that I will do as she commands.'","Ordlac and Grimmar are in the Mead Hall of Stoke. Baldmund is at the inn in Stoke. Dudsig is at the Oserley encampment outside the north-east gate of Stoke. Alfbert stands outside Reeve Fríthild's house.\
\
Fríthild has asked you to summon the leaders of Stoke to council and deliver a letter to Alfbert at her house.","'I do not know why I should waste my time sitting in council. There are too many preparations to be made. Nevertheless, I will come.'","Talk to Grimmar","Talk to Reeve Fríthild","Reeve Fríthild is in the Mead Hall of Stoke.\
\
You should return to Reeve Fríthild and let her know that all is ready for the council.","'${PLAYER}, I believe the time has come to summon my advisors to council. Return to Grimmar, Ordlac, Baldmund, and Dudsig and inform them of my decision. We must decide what action to take and how best to fulfill it. The leaders of Stoke and Oserley each have their own opinions, and they are at odds. We must come to a compromise and work together, or we shall fall to the White Hand.\
\
'As well, bring this letter to Alfbert, the guard at my house. Return to me when your messages have been delivered.'","The leaders of Stoke are at odds as to the best course of action to be taken to protect the town and drive the enemy from the Broadacres.","The Council of Stoke","'Ah! This is welcome news, my friend! At last, we will join a battle worth a song or two! Let us join the council!'","Deliver Reeve Fríthild's letter to Alfbert","Talk to Baldmund","Talk to Reeve Fríthild to join the Council of Stoke","Talk to Dudsig","Reeve Fríthild is in the Mead Hall of Stoke.\
\
You should speak with Reeve Fríthild regarding the course she has chosen.","The Council of Stoke has ended","'I am honoured that Reeve Fríthild values my opinion. I have never heard of a lord or lady of Rohan calling upon the common folk for counsel.\
\
'I will come at once.'","'Ah, ${PLAYER}! It has been long since a shield-maiden of Rohan has actually taken to the field. This is a glorious day.\
\
'All that remains to be decided is which front to assail, for we are surrounded.'","DNT -- Will not be seen","Talk to Thane Ordlac","'Good! It is of utmost import that we convince the Reeve to bolster our defences!'","'You have my thanks.\
\
'Let the Council of Stoke begin!'"},
[11916]={"'¿Te ha enviado Arohir, verdad? Que él te haya hablado de nuestra existencia dice mucho de la confianza que deposita en ti... y por ello tengo grandes esperanzas de que puedas ayudarnos en nuestra causa desesperada.'","'He oído rumores de que existe un campamento oculto muy cerca de las mismas puertas de Carn Dûm, en el lejano norte, donde valientes héroes se reúnen para desafiar el poder de Angmar en persona.\
\
'No puedo decir con exactitud dónde se halla Gath Forthnír —como lo llaman—, pero si llegas a encontrar este lugar, habla con una llamada Annábla, y ella podrá contarte más acerca de su propósito.'","El Concilio del Norte","'Debes hablar con Annábla en Gath Forthnír, en Angmar, ${PLAYER}.'","Habla con Annábla de Gath Forthnír.","Arohir de Esteldín te ha pedido que busques el campamento oculto de Gath Forthnír, en el lejano norte, en algún lugar al este de las puertas de Carn Dûm, y que una vez allí hables con Annábla."},
[11917]={"Wil Trigal está en la granja de Cal Sprigley, al sur de Archet, aguardando noticias de sus compañeros de trabajo y de su padre.\
\
Debes dar a Wil la noticia de que su padre y los otros peones fueron asesinados en su valiente persecución de los Montebruno.","Walt Trigal ha sido asesinado por los Montebruno","Bill Lanzaheno ha sido asesinado por los Montebruno","Busca a Walt Trigal","Busca a Thornton Bosquedal","'¡No! ¡No puede ser! Mi pobre padre..... y los demás, no, no puede ser, no puede ser.'\
\
Wil guarda silencio por un largo momento, con los ojos cerrados, pero tras una gran pausa se reincorpora.\
\
'¡Tendré mi venganza sobre esos Montebruno, o moriré intentándolo! Archet nunca caerá ante tales asesinos.'","Algunos valientes peones de granja ahuyentaron a los bandidos que atacaron la granja de Sprigley, pero aún no han regresado, y Wil Trigal teme lo peor.","'Mi padre y los otros peones, ellos persiguieron a los bandidos después del ataque a nuestra granja. No creo que los bandidos esperaran que nos defendiéramos tan bien después de sorprendernos. No eran muchos, pero nunca los había visto actuar con tanta audacia hasta hoy.\
\
'El único problema es que aún no han vuelto. Corrieron hacia el este, persiguiendo a los bandidos hacia el bosque. Pero eso fue hace horas, y ¡estoy muy preocupado!\
\
'¿Podrías ir a buscarlos y traerlos sanos y salvos?'","Busca a Bill Lanzaheno","Esta misión no puede completarse fuera de la introducción.","Los Valientes Peones de Granja","Los peones de la granja de Cal Sprigley se dirigieron hacia el este tras unos bandidos Montebruno que atacaron.\
\
Debes buscar a los peones desaparecidos y traerlos de vuelta sanos y salvos a la granja para que Wil y Cal puedan aliviar sus temores.","Thornton Bosquedal ha sido asesinado por los Montebruno","Regresa con Wil Trigal con las trágicas noticias","'Mi padre ya no es tan joven como solía ser. Debería saber que no debe salir así a perseguir gente. Estoy muy preocupado por él y por los demás.'"},
[11921]={"Dos de las tribus de orcos de Angmar, los Blogmal y los Tarkrîp, están en conflicto por los derechos de minería en Bornabar.","Derrota a Zurm","Zurm ha sido derrotado","'¡Saludos, ${PLAYER}! ¿Estás aquí para ayudarnos en nuestra lucha contra los Orcos de Angmar?\
\
'Angmar ha enviado dos tribus de orcos de fuego a la Falla, que llaman Nûrz Ghâshu, para extraer los metales que se pueden encontrar allí, que sospecho son de la mejor calidad. Sería demasiado peligroso para mí aventurarme solo en sus minas, pero quizás tú podrías hacerlo, con ayuda.\
\
'Si vas allí, busca a Barz y Zurm, los supervisores gorthorogs de Bornabar, y derrótalos. Tengo entendido que no solo ponen a trabajar a los Orcos, sino también a esclavos entre los Montañeses de Angmar.'","Derrota a Barz","Jónsi se encuentra en el campamento de Iorelen.\
\
Debes regresar a Jónsi y contarle tu victoria contra Barz y Zurm.","El arte del Enemigo","'¿Has derrotado a Barz y Zurm? ¡Esa es una noticia maravillosa, ${PLAYER}! Esas bestias viles no harán más daño a la piedra de la Falla.\
\
'Toma esta recompensa...¡te la has ganado!'","'Barz y Zurm son terribles capataces.'","Barz ha sido derrotado","Barz y Zurm están en Bornabar, dentro del sello derrumbado bajo el campamento de Iorelen.\
\
Jónsi te ha pedido que entres en las minas de los Orcos y derrotes a los supervisores gorthorogs, Barz y Zurm.","'Hiciste bien en destruir a esos Gorthorogs...¡su minería estaba destruyendo la piedra de la Falla!'"},
[11922]={"'Justo antes de tu regreso, una gran bandada de pájaros salió volando apresuradamente de la Puerta del Cuerno Rojo. Esperemos que les hayas infundido suficiente temor como para expulsarlos de Eregion, aunque no dudo que volverán para devorar los huesos de los caídos.'","'Los crebain se pueden encontrar en la Puerta del Cuerno Rojo, al noreste de Echad Dúnann.'","'Sin duda las cumbres de Celebdil, Caradhras y Fanuidhol habrán captado tu mirada, pero una gran sombra a menudo me ciega. Grandes y oscuras nubes se mueven contra el viento y pasan sobre la tierra en busca de algo.\
\
'Bandadas de crebain de alas negras de las Tierras Brunas han estado sobrevolando la Puerta del Cuerno Rojo. Es evidente que buscan a la Compañía, y temo que tengan noticias o hayan encontrado alguna pista que nosotros mismos no hemos descubierto.\
\
'Ve al noreste hacia la Puerta del Cuerno Rojo y derrota a esos espías de Saruman, luego vuelve aquí.'","'Esperemos que hayas expulsado a los viles crebain de Eregion.'","Crebain, procedentes de las Tierras Brunas y al servicio de Saruman, espían los resquicios de la Puerta del Cuerno Rojo, poniendo en riesgo los esfuerzos de los Elfos en Eregion.","Los crebain se pueden encontrar al noreste de Echad Dúnann en la Puerta del Cuerno Rojo.\
\
Authlanc te ha pedido que derrotes a los Crebain en la Puerta del Cuerno Rojo.","Authlanc se encuentra en Echad Dúnann, al sureste de la Puerta del Cuerno Rojo.\
\
Debes regresar con Authlanc y contarle sobre tu éxito.","Habla con Authlanc en Echad Dúnann","Los crebain de Caradhras","Crebain derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota a los crebain (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[11923]={"Puede haber señales del paso de la criatura en la orilla oriental. Deberías seguir buscando indicios de la criatura","Advierte a los habitantes de la cabaña del peligro cercano","Los habitantes de la cabaña parecen ilesos, pero deberían ser advertidos del peligro","La cabaña está en la orilla occidental del río.\
\
Deberías advertir a los habitantes de la cabaña del peligro cercano.","La cabaña está en la orilla occidental del río.\
\
Has encontrado huesos de pescado roídos. La criatura debe de estar cerca, así que quizá haya entrado en la cabaña en la orilla occidental.","Seguiste el rastro de la criatura que devoró al ciervo blanco a lo largo del río hasta perderlo. Puede que la criatura haya cruzado a la orilla oriental.","Sigue buscando indicios de la criatura","Algo ha roído toda la carne de estos huesos de pescado","Puede haber señales del paso de la criatura en la orilla oriental.\
\
Deberías seguir buscando indicios de la criatura.","La Sombra Reptante","'Llegas tarde para advertirnos, pues ya conocemos el peligro.\
\
'Anoche, apenas oscureció, apagamos las velas, cerramos la puerta y nos disponíamos a acostarnos cuando escuché algo moviéndose en la habitación del pequeño Whelan. Whelan es apenas un bebé, así que comprenderás mi preocupación: pensé que un pájaro podría haber entrado por la ventana, que siempre dejamos entreabierta para que entre la brisa, y no quería que se asustara. Pero cuando entré a su habitación para revisarlo, no vi un pájaro, sino un monstruo: ¡una criatura terrible y reptante, encorvada sobre unas patas huesudas! Se movía hacia la cuna de Whelan y emitía un sonido espantoso desde su garganta.\
\
'Su intención estaba clara: ¡quería hacer daño a mi hijo! Lancé un grito como jamás habrás oído y me abalancé sobre ella; no sé qué pretendía hacer, pero la criatura saltó por la ventana por donde había entrado y desapareció en la noche.'","Registra la cabaña en la orilla occidental en busca de señales de la criatura"},
[11927]={"The Crew: Carver of Distant Stone","Gangur Farwend stormed from Zarsatrâd after being embarrassed by the dwarves there. It looked to you as if he was heading in the direction of Erynos, but he likely wishes to stay away from people.","'They laughed at me, ${PLAYER}. Why would they do that? What is it about that gemstone that they do not want to share with outsiders?'\
\
Gangur strokes his beard, deep in thought.\
\
'The Temámir of Furukzahar did not want you to know they were visited by an emissary of the Kindred of the Coins, and they kept the details of what he spoke about a secret from you and from the King of Gondor. Then the Dwarves of Zarsatrâd dodged my questions about the gemstone that emissary carried. Why? What were you saying earlier, ${PLAYER}? Something about a voyage?'\
\
You tell Gangur, once again, about your mission to Umbar and your desire for him to join your crew. This time he thinks it over.\
\
'I have come a long way from my home already... what is another hundred miles, even if those carry me across the Bay? The answers I seek may lie in Umbar with the Kindred of the Coins. I will join you, ${PLAYER}! I must learn about the unusual gem carried by Khôltekh the Cunning, and the reasons for his folk to maintain such secrecy when asked about it! I will be there when you begin your voyage!'","'Oh, I know you.'","Gangur Farwend will be more likely to join your crew if you help him, so you agree","Gangur Farwend, the carver of distant stone, has joined your crew!","'Do I know you? I don't have a very good mind for faces.'\
\
You remind Gangur that he warned you about some suspicious dealings within the Temámir fortress of Furukzahar, and he nods.\
\
'Yes, I remember now. I am pleased that my words proved some help to you, although as you can see I am no longer welcome there. Ah, it is fine. I have always been a traveller, and the hospitality of Furukzahar was not especially to my liking.'\
\
He lowers his voice.\
\
'You remember Khôltekh the Cunning? He carried a talisman on his person, and it shone in a very curious way, as if it contained a gem possessing unusual qualities. I have mentioned it to some of the dwarves here, in a roundabout way so as not to give away my interest, and they say they will tell me more if I help eliminate some of the beasts nearby. Would you like to help me accomplish this?'","Gangur Farwend is at the outpost of Zarsatrâd, south of Furukzahar.","You have found Gangur Farwend at Zarsatrâd","'¿Si?'","'I told the dwarves here we did as they requested, and they laughed at me! \\qA special gemstone? What makes you think we would tell an outsider like you anything?\\q they said! They called me too trusting! Me! Gangur Farwend!'\
\
You try to calm him down and ask if he will be interested in joining your crew, but you have only just brought it up when he interrupts.\
\
'I am not in the mood for conversation, ${PLAYER}! I cannot stay in this place! They are laughing at me even now, behind my back!'","'Do I know where Gangur Farwend went after he left Furukzahar? You are going to have to remind me who that is.'\
\
You tell Kutúkh that he was a Longbeard that departed shortly after the arrival of King Elessar. The dwarf strokes his beard and contemplates your description.\
\
'Yes, I remember him now. Hámisar sent him from the fortress in disgrace, as I recall. You should not waste any time seeking one such as he, for he is a bad penny and will bring you nothing but trouble. If you insist upon it, perhaps so you can make him a better dwarf, I believe he mentioned stopping at Zarsatrâd before continuing his journey. Zarsatrâd is the outpost to the south. Good day to you.'","Talk to Gangur Farwend north of Erynos, in King's Gondor East","The dwarves at Zarsatrâd agreed to tell Gangur Farwend something about the strange gemstone he saw at Furukzahar if he aided them by defeating beasts near the outpost, and you agreed to help.","Talk to Gangur Farwend in Zarsatrâd","'I remember Gangur Farwend now. Hámisar sent him from the fortress in disgrace, as I recall. You should not waste any time seeking one such as he, for he is a bad penny and will bring you nothing but trouble. If you insist upon it, perhaps so you can make him a better dwarf, I believe he mentioned stopping at Zarsatrâd before continuing his journey. Zarsatrâd is the outpost to the south. Good day to you.'","Gangur grunts in recognition as you approach","Defeated foes of Zarsatrâd (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Khôltekh the Cunning carried a talisman on his person, and it shone in a very curious way, as if it contained a gem possessing unusual qualities. I have mentioned it to some of the dwarves here, in a roundabout way so as not to give away my interest, and they say they will tell me more if I help eliminate some of the beasts nearby. Would you like to help me accomplish this?'","Gangur storms off, leaving Zarsatrâd and hurrying to the south-east","Find Gangur Farwend at Zarsatrâd, to the south of Furukzahar","Find Gangur Farwend somewhere to the south-east of Zarsatrâd","Gangur Farwend is south-east of Zarsatrâd and north of Erynos, in King's Gondor East.","Kutúkh told you that Gangur Farwend mentioned stopping at the outpost of Zarsatrâd to the south before continuing his journey.","Defeat foes of the dwarves near the outpost of Zarsatrâd (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Caebar believes Gangur Farwend, the dwarf who warned you about Khôltekh the Cunning during your stay at Furukzahar, might be willing to join your crew."},
[11928]={"Stand near the caged songbird and blow the whistle given to you by Leafshade","Talk to Leafshade in Tumbamálë","'Hrum, hoom... you have come back again, little one? Have you returned to Tumbamálë to bring me news of Nestinanessornë?'\
\
You tell Leafshade that you are looking for crew-members to sail with you to Umbar, and you hope to rescue both Nestinanessornë and the young heir of Pinnath Gelin from the Kindred of the Coins. Leafshade exhales heavily, shaking the leaves of his grove.\
\
'Hoooooooom...'\
\
When the leaves finally settle, Leafshade speaks again.\
\
'I do not like boats, hoom, toom. My friend Nestinanessornë sailed away on one such vessel, but it is not the first time I have lost a companion to the branches-that-float. Another friend of mine, Gwallang the Limlinn, built a nest here in Tumbamálë, but a wooden boat passed nearby and he flew over to it. He never, hoom, never came back. Ferien told me long ago that sailors sometimes take birds with them on their voyages. Perhaps it was the same with Gwallang.'\
\
Leafshade slowly extends a long arm down to you. After a moment you realize he is holding a small wooden whistle.\
\
'If you find Gwallang... blow this whistle and remind him of Tumbamálë. It may be he has, hrum, forgotten.'","Gwallang is in Tumbamálë, and apparently wants to tell you something.","'He would like to speak to you, hoom, toom.'","'Hm, hm, hm. My friend Gwallang the Limlinn says that he misses travelling, and his happiest days were spent accompanying Sirgon the Sailor on his voyages. Hoom! Happier than spending time with me?'\
\
Gwallang trills for a moment, and then Leafshade continues.\
\
'He says he was very disappointed when Sirgon left the seafaring life behind him, hoom. He desires to accompany you, if you will have him. Hm, hm! Perhaps when your voyages are done, my friend will return to Tumbamálë? But until then he desires to go with you.'","Is it possible the caged songbird in Sirgon's room of keepsakes could be Gwallang?","Gwallang trills a lovely song.","'He did seem to recognize the whistle? Then by all means set him free, my friend.'","The Crew: Dweller of Tumbamálë","Find Leafshade's friend Gwallang the Limlinn","Gwallang the Limlinn, dweller of Tumbamálë, has joined your crew!","Talk to Sirgon in his room of keepsakes about the caged songbird","Gwallang jumps around, chirping and trilling. After several minutes of this, Leafshade rumbles in satisfaction and calls you over to him.","'I hope my little friend has found freedom and happiness. I enjoyed my time with him, and the sound of his song.'","The caged songbird tilts his head and hops excitedly. Is this Gwallang?","The caged songbird at the far end of Sirgon's room of keepsakes may be Gwallang.","Leafshade thinks an old sailor might have sailed away with his friend Gwallang, a songbird of the Limlinn species. If you could find him, Leafshade's whistle will apparently remind the bird from where he came.","'I will miss the little fellow, if he is the friend of this Leafshade, but I do not want to keep him a prisoner here if he wishes to be elsewhere! Well do I know what it is to be kept from the place where sings your heart! Go to him and blow the whistle; perhaps he will stay here, but if he does not I will be pleased to set him free.'","Sirgon is in his manor's room of keepsakes.","'What is it, my friend? Ask me anything and it shall be yours.'\
\
You ask Sirgon how he came to possess the songbird caged at the far end of his room of keepsakes.\
\
'Oh, it was years ago, now. I sailed to speak with my friend Belondor of Langstrand about some matter or another, I confess that I cannot bring it so easily to mind. He is dead now, drowned among the Shield Isles; a story for another time! But I do remember that as we sailed along the coast of Anfalas, that bird flew across the water to my vessel and settled upon one of the ropes! He was a boisterous little fellow! At first I thought he was there for the fish my crew had caught that day, but he quite ignored them. He stayed on the ship for that entire voyage, and as he did not disturb any of the crew I kept him onboard for other journeys as well. Now he keeps me company here at home.'\
\
You tell Sirgon about the possibility that the songbird might be Gwallang, a friend of Leafshade, and that the Ent gave you a whistle to call him home.\
\
'Oh, I see. I will miss the little fellow, but I do not want to keep him a prisoner here if he wishes to be elsewhere! Well do I know what it is to be kept from the place where sings your heart! Go to him and blow the whistle; perhaps he will stay here, but if he does not I will be pleased to set him free.'","The songbird flies out of the cage, circles the room, and vanishes outside","'I do not like boats, hoom, toom. A friend of mine, Gwallang the Limlinn, built a nest here in Tumbamálë, but a wooden boat passed nearby and he flew over to it. He never, hoom, never came back. Ferien told me long ago that sailors sometimes take birds with them on their voyages. Perhaps it was the same with Gwallang. If you find him... blow the whistle I gave you and remind him of Tumbamálë. It may be he has, hrum, forgotten.'","Leafshade the Ent is in Tumbamálë, in south-western Anfalas.","Leafshade is in Tumbamálë.","Talk to Gwallang the Limlinn in Tumbamálë","'You found my friend Gwallang, ${PLAYER}, hoom, toom, boom!\
\
'He has quite a story to tell, hm, hm!'","Open the cage and free the songbird in Sirgon's room of keepsakes","The caged songbird certainly appeared to recognize the whistle. Sirgon has given you permission to open the cage and free the bird.","Caebar has an interest in learning more about Leafshade, and while the Ent is unlikely to join your crew, perhaps he will know of something that might be of use to you."},
[11929]={"King Elessar suggested that you recruit the Lady Nauriel for the mission to Umbar.","Retrieve Nauriel's shield from the armoury in Ost Arndír","Carandolion ties a small handkerchief to the hilt of his wife's sword","'Will you retrieve my sword and shield from the armoury on the lower level? I have had the sword sharpened and the shield reinforced since the Corsairs raided Tûm Rost, and they should now be ready for me.'","'Thank you for bringing me my equipment, ${PLAYER}, and for speaking with my husband. I will carry his favour into battle on behalf of our son Thorongil, should battle prove necessary. My husband would be the first to tell you he is no fighter, but I love him all the more for it. I do our fighting for us, and without regret.\
\
'Carandolion will see that Pinnath Gelin does not suffer in my absence, and when I return I will return with our son, and only his father will celebrate more loudly and happily than I.\
\
'I will await your command, and the rest of your crew, at the Wave-hunter.'","Retrieved Nauriel's shield","The Crew: Knight of the Green Hills","'Every day that passes brings my son further into danger, ${PLAYER}. There must be no more delay.\
\
'I will join the crew of the Wave-hunter so I may ask the Kindred of the Coins to return Thorongil, but I will ask only once. If they refuse I will bloody my sword and dent my shield on their carcasses! They have remained unused for too long, anyway. My husband Carandolion always speaks of the need for patience, and for thinking things through, but see where that has gotten us! Our son stolen away by enemies of Gondor! Well, they have made an enemy of Nauriel, and she does not forgive as readily as Gondor. Recruit the crew you think we will need for the voyage, ${PLAYER}, but remember the need I have for haste.\
\
'Will you retrieve my sword and shield from the armoury on the lower level? I have had the sword sharpened and the shield reinforced since the Corsairs raided Tûm Rost, and they should now be ready for me.'","Nauriel's sword and shield have been made ready for the voyage, and can be found on the lowest level of Ost Arndír.","'My husband was looking for you. Return to the lowest level and find him.'","Nauriel is in the main hall, on the upper level of Ost Arndír.","'I will remain here to oversee Pinnath Gelin while Nauriel is away, but my thoughts will sail alongside her as she rides the waves to Umbar. I will give her a favour to carry into battle, so she knows her husband's heart goes with her.'","Nauriel's husband Carandolion is on the lowest level of Ost Arndír.","Talk to Carandolion on the lowest level of Ost Arndír","Nauriel, Knight of the Green Hills, has joined your crew!","'I am no fighter, ${PLAYER}, but that does not mean I do not want my son safely returned to his home. My wife has always been the firebrand, and she has temper enough for the both of us! But she matches it, nay, she exceeds it, with her martial skill. There are none more deadly in all the Green Hills with a blade than she!\
\
'I am unlike my brother, you know. Duinhir rode to Minas Tirith with trumpets and banners, and when he came back he did so without his sons, for they were of fighting age. My Thorongil was not, but he has been taken away all the same, and now I must rely upon my dangerous wife to retrieve him. Do I risk losing them both? These are the thoughts that keep me awake at night, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'I will remain here to oversee Pinnath Gelin while Nauriel is away, but my thoughts will sail alongside her as she rides the waves to Umbar. I will give her a favour to carry into battle, so she knows her husband's heart goes with her.'","Retrieve Nauriel's sword from the armoury in Ost Arndír","Bring her sword and shield to Nauriel in Ost Arndír","Retrieved Nauriel's sword"},
[11930]={"Defeat foes in the Blackroot Vale, King's Gondor West (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Look for Sigileth somewhere on the road to the Dark Door, north of Morlad in King's Gondor West","'You really expect this Elf-warrior to come through the Paths of the Dead? I have not seen her, at any rate. If you go to the Dark Door perhaps you will intercept her on her way, but I find this hard to believe.'","'I will meet you at your ship when the time comes to depart.'","Sigileth has come to the Blackroot Vale, in King's Gondor West, in search of her brother Corudan.","'This sounds like quite the adventure, ${PLAYER}! I would go with you, but I am commanded by my Prince to make safe the Vale, and I have never desired to do other than that.\
\
'Good fortune go with you on your voyage, my friend. I hope you accomplish all that you set out to do.'","King Elessar suggested that you recruit Corudan's sister Sigileth for the mission to Umbar.","Defeated foes in the Blackroot Vale for Rovalang (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Wait for the newcomer to arrive","Sigileth is not here, but you have found a friendly face: the Swan-knight Rovalang","'What brings you once again to the Blackroot Vale, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You tell Rovalang that you are waiting for a friend to arrive, and you plan to ask her to join your crew on a secret mission to Umbar. The swan-knight nods, and looks as if he has some questions to ask. Then he smiles.\
\
'I will not press you any further on this, my friend, for a secret mission should remain secret, no matter how intriguing it may be for me to hear more of it! While you wait for your friend to arrive, perhaps you will help me with my own task? I have been ordered to make safe the Blackroot Vale, and I could use your help with that, as before and as always!'","'This is quite a tale!'","'Saludos a ti.'","The Swan-knight Rovalang asked for your help making safe the Blackroot Vale in King's Gondor West.","'Thank you, my friend. It is always a pleasure to work alongside you!\
\
'But wait... someone comes!'","'I did not expect to see you on the road, ${PLAYER}. I would have found you, just as we will now find my brother Corudan!'\
\
You ask Sigileth if she truly passed through the Paths of the Dead on her way to the Blackroot Vale, and she looks at you quizzically.\
\
'I am no stranger to places of evil, my friend; my stay beneath the dungeons of Dol Guldur has seen to that. I was untroubled by the Paths of the Dead; any of the spirits that still dwell beneath the Mountain chose not to hinder my passage... a wise choice. Now, tell me what you have learned of Corudan's whereabouts. Time is wasting.'\
\
You tell Sigileth, briefly, of what you know of her brother's captivity by Nakási Wave-reaper and the Kindred of the Coins, and of your plan to rescue him.\
\
'Your ship is docked at a lake to the west? I will meet you there, and sail with you to Umbar. My brother will be freed from captivity and death, just as I was when you thought me dead on the stairs of Dol Guldur. Let us not delay.'","The Crew: She Who Remained","'While you wait for your friend to arrive, perhaps you will help me with my own task? I have been ordered to make safe the Blackroot Vale, and I could use your help with that, as before and as always!'","If you really expect Sigileth to pass through the Paths of the Dead, you should look for her on the road to the Dark Door, north of Morlad in the Blackroot Vale, in King's Gondor West.","Someone approaches from the direction of the Dark Door.","'I am pleased to see you again, ${PLAYER}. King Elessar sent word that he will come in person to the Blackroot Vale after all, and I believe I have you to thank for that. It is important for the folk of Morlad and the wider Vale to see their king. But what brings you here now?'\
\
You ask Duinhir if an Elf-warrior named Sigileth has come to Morlad, and he says that he has not seen anyone by that name or description come from the south. You shake your head, and tell the Lord of the Blackroot Vale that Sigileth would likely come from the north. He marvels at you in surprise.\
\
'From the north? Does that mean you expect this Elf-warrior to come through the Paths of the Dead? I have not seen her, at any rate. If you go to the Dark Door perhaps you will intercept her on her way, but I find this hard to believe.'","The Elf-warrior Sigileth has answered your call","Sigileth of the Hidden Guard, she who remained, has joined your crew!","The Swan-knight Rovalang stands by the road to the Dark Door, in King's Gondor West.","Talk to Sigileth on the road to the Dark Door in the Blackroot Vale, in King's Gondor West","Talk to Rovalang by the road to the Dark Door in the Blackroot Vale, in King's Gondor West"},
[11931]={"Collect beast parts from crawlers, crabs, or oxen near Melgobas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Elestren in Melgobas","King Elessar suggested that you recruit Legolas and Gimli for the mission to Umbar.","Collected beast parts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I know why you are here, my friend, and of course I will agree to sail with you into danger! I hope you did not expect me to refuse! But I have set foot upon one too many boats for my liking in these past few months, ${PLAYER}. I simply do not like them. Show me a dwarf who does and I will be very surprised!\
\
'The folk hereabout say that the Bay is generally calm... generally... but I know that even the calmest waters can shake a boat to its very foundation. Do I say foundation? A boat has no such thing, and tosses and turns at the merest whim of the waves! Sea-sickness is a concern, friend.\
\
'Legolas inquired on my behalf, seeking a remedy for it, and learned that an herbalist in Melgobas may prepare a suitable concoction. Will you go there and see if it is ready, and you may also ask the Elf if he desires to join your crew as well. I assume he will, but you should ask him yourself.'","Talk to Legolas in Melgobas","Elestren has a home in Melgobas and may know how to make a sea-sickness remedy for Gimli.","Bring the flowers and assorted beast parts to Elestren in Melgobas","'Thank you for bringing me these; they will not all be used in the same mixture, but I assure you they will all be used in something! Your friend returned shortly before you did, and I have given him the sea-sickness remedy I promised. I give to you the same warning I gave him: it may not have the desired effect upon the dwarf for whom it is intended! It truly does vary based on the individual, and if it does not work as you expect it is not a failing of the potion, or of she who brewed it!\
\
'But I hope it does help him. Sea-sickness is not a pleasant thing for anyone.'","Elestren has a home in Melgobas and is waiting for you to return to her with the flowers and beast parts she requested.","Collected Langstrand wild-flowers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Legolas is outside the home of Elestren in Melgobas.","Langstrand wild-flowers can be found north of Melgobas, in the grass alongside the road. Crawlers, oxen, and crabs can be found outside the village.","The Crew: The Boon Companions","Legolas and Gimli, the boon companions, have joined your crew!","'A sea-sickness remedy? You are the second person to ask for such a concoction today. The first was an Elf, and I will tell you what I told him: the effectiveness of such an elixir varies depending upon the person who takes it, and what works for one may not work for another. I do not give back the purchase price in the event you are dissatisfied!\
\
'I sent the Elf to collect some Langstrand flowers and beast parts from the creatures hereabout, and while he has not yet returned, if you perform the same task as he the work may be finished more quickly. I make use of parts from crawlers, aurochs, and crabs in the various unguents and potions I create, and will appreciate any you bring back to me.'","'I hope my remedy does help your dwarf friend. Sea-sickness is not a pleasant thing for anyone.'","'I hope possession of this remedy will ease the turmoil of Gimli's stomach when the Wave-hunter sets out! He may not even need to ingest it, if he knows it is near-at-hand and might be taken if necessary. I will not tell him of the chance that it will do nothing, unless he asks directly. I will not lie to my friend, but this information can do no good in advance and may instead do harm.\
\
'There was no need for you to come all this way to speak with me, ${PLAYER}! I of course will join you on your mission. The sea-longing has me and will not abate, but I understand the Wave-hunter will remain in the Bay and not pass out into the Great Sea. There are still things for me to see and to do before I begin that last voyage, and I count high in that number aiding you in the rescue of young Thorongil from the clutches of the Kindred of the Coins.\
\
'I will be pleased to join your crew, my friend. Both I and Gimli will meet you by the Wave-hunter when you are ready to depart.'","'I sent the Elf to collect some Langstrand flowers and beast parts from the creatures hereabout, and while he has not yet returned, if you perform the same task as he the work may be finished more quickly. I make use of parts from crawlers, oxen, and crabs in the various unguents and potions I create, and will appreciate any you bring back to me.'","Collect Langstrand wild-flowers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Legolas inquired on my behalf, seeking a remedy for it, and learned that an herbalist in Melgobas may prepare a suitable concoction. Will you go there and see if it is ready, and you may also ask the Elf if he desires to join your crew as well. I assume he will, but you should ask him yourself.'"},
[11932]={"Prince Imrahil's scouts reported seeing Jajax near Abadec's Watch to the south-east of Dol Amroth, in King's Gondor West.","Talk to Daxamat outside Abadec's Watch, in King's Gondor West","Daxamat, one of the Corsair brothers, has joined your crew!","'${PLAYER}! Are you here to rescue me? Please say that is what brings you here, for otherwise I fear I might die bound to this post, and that would make my brother very displeased, I am sure of it!'\
\
You tell Daxamat that Jajax waits for him outside Abadec's Watch, and untie him.\
\
'Thank you for this! I will not forget it!'","'I will join your crew, ${PLAYER}. I will be there when the voyage begins.'","King Elessar suggested that you recruit the Corsair Jajax, if you think he can be trusted to help.","'I did not expect you to return to Dol Amroth so quickly, ${PLAYER}. And where is the King?'\
\
You tell Prince Imrahil about Nakási Wave-reaper's raid upon the Green Hills and her seizure of young Thorongil. When you speak of King Elessar's suggestion that you assemble a crew to rescue the heir of Pinnath Gelin, the Prince grasps the hilt of his sword.\
\
'I can leave at once. You have but to say the word and I will voyage with you to Umbar Baharbêl, the City of Sails! The Kindred of the Coins will not stand long against us, for they will know my face and my reputation! But... you are not here to recruit me for your mission, are you? I can tell from your expression that the King wishes this to be a more secret quest. Yes, I see the need for it. I apologize for getting carried away. Who does the King suggest?'\
\
You say that you are considering the Corsair Jajax for your crew, and the Prince is overcome by a coughing fit.\
\
'What? Tell me you are not serious about this, ${PLAYER}! This Jajax is a Corsair, and will betray you at the first opportunity, if he has not already! My scouts report that he has gone in the direction of Abadec's Watch, south-east of Dol Amroth, likely to meet with those of his fellows encamped there. They are a danger to Gondor, and always will be! I hope you know what you are doing. If the King believes this is the right course I will not speak against it.'","Daxamat stands outside Abadec's Watch, in King's Gondor West.","Talk to Jajax outside Abadec's Watch","'Look who has turned up!'","Imrahil's scouts spoke true: Jajax stands outside Abadec's Watch","Daxamat is being held prisoner inside Abadec's Watch, in King's Gondor West.","Talk to Jajax outside Abadec's Watch, in King's Gondor West","Wait for Daxamat to escape","'¿Habéis venido para ayudarnos?'","'Now get in there, kill his captors, and keep my brother alive. We'll talk once you've done that... and not before.'","Find Jajax at Abadec's Watch, south-east of Dol Amroth, in King's Gondor West","You have freed Daxamat from his bonds.","'Well look who turned up, and just in time!\
\
'I have learned what happened to Dax, my friend, and I was just about to go inside and rescue him... but now that you are here I see the blessing of happy chance is upon me! I have always been one of the lucky ones, ${PLAYER}; that is why I have lived so long!\
\
'Now get in there, kill his captors, and keep my brother alive. We'll talk once you've done that... and not before.'","'I told you I was lucky, ${PLAYER}. All I had to do was wait, and you rescued my brother for me! How very fortunate. The stars truly smile upon Jajax... they always have, and they always will! Now what brought you in search of me?'\
\
You tell Jajax that you are assembling a crew to sail to Umbar to rescue the kidnapped heir of Pinnath Gelin from the Kindred of the Coins, and you want him to join you. When you have finished, Jajax laughs, but his laughter is free of mirth.\
\
'Why would I do this? What could you possibly offer to me that would make it worth my while to return to Umbar while it is under the control of the Kindred? I told you what happened when Dax and I returned there! No. My answer is no. You will sail to Umbar without us.'","'So that is the way of it, Dax?'\
\
Jajax scowls at you.\
\
'My brother has always been one who follows, ${PLAYER}. First he served Balakhôr the Scourge as a deckhand on the Night-jewel, and then he served Azgarzôr his brother until we slew him, and only then! Always Dax needs someone to tell him what to do! Well, I am different.'\
\
The Corsair's scowl deepens.\
\
'Jajax is a captain, not a crew-member! He gives the commands! He is the one who leads!'\
\
Jajax shakes his head at his brother and gives you a curt wave with one hand.\
\
'This is where we part ways, ${PLAYER}. I will find a crew and a ship of my own. May my brother serve you better than he served the Heirs of Castamir! Without me to keep him in line, I believe your ship will be doomed. A pity, that! A pity! Farewell.'","'Wait.'\
\
Daxamat stares off into the distance, as if gathering his courage.\
\
'I will join you, ${PLAYER}, if you will have me. I fear the Kindred of the Coins, but I fear the Heirs of Castamir more, and they still have supporters throughout these lands; the Corsairs here in Abadec's Watch belong to that number. They imprisoned me as a traitor to the Heirs, and would do so again if given the chance.\
\
'My brother says he is the lucky one, but I think in recent days I have had the best fortune in our family, for your path brought you here to rescue me. I cannot be certain you will be near the next time, unless I go with you on your ship. Count me among your crew, ${PLAYER}.'","Your rescue of Daxamat from Abadec's Watch will require you to defeat the Corsairs camped inside.","Free Daxamat inside Abadec's Watch","Defeat Corsairs inside Abadec's Watch (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Jajax stands outside Abadec's Watch, in King's Gondor West.","Defeated Corsairs inside Abadec's Watch (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Crew: The Corsair Jajax","'This Jajax is a Corsair, and will betray you at the first opportunity, if he has not already! My scouts report that he has gone in the direction of Abadec's Watch, south-east of Dol Amroth, likely to meet with those of his fellows encamped there. They are a danger to Gondor, and always will be! I hope you know what you are doing. If the King believes this is the right course I will not speak against it.'","'No. My answer is no.'"},
[11933]={"'You have removed all the notices? Good, good! There are new markets to discover and new goods to acquire, and when we do return I shall become even more profitable than I had previously expected!\
\
'It will be an honour to profit from your mission, ${PLAYER}! I mean, it will be an honour to aid you with the provisions you need to conduct a successful voyage. I will be ready when you are set to depart, my auspicious friend!'","Talk to Bandron by the brazier in Calembel, in King's Gondor West","'What wonderful tidings you bring! My son will be delighted to hear it as well: at last we will have a break from Galengam's orders! He is always sending us all over Gondor, ${PLAYER}, with nary a rest in-between each journey. Do you think you could make this voyage take as long as possible, and give my boy and I a true holiday? Endless thanks to you, my friend!'","Galengam is inside his shop in Calembel, in King's Gondor West.","You burn Galengam's notices to ash in the brazier","Collect Galengam's notices throughout Calembel, in King's Gondor West (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Galengam inside his shop in Calembel, in King's Gondor West","'Well now, this is quite a surprise! What brings you back to Galengam's Divine and Delicate Draughts, ${PLAYER}? Did the King come with you? I saw an increase in visitors to my shop after his previous visit, and I look forward to any future return he might make!'\
\
You tell Galengam the purpose of your visit: that you are recruiting crew-members for a dangerous journey to Umbar so you may rescue the kidnapped heir of the Green Hills. The merchant adjusts the hat upon his head.\
\
'Ah, I see why you have come to me. Who else would have the extensive knowledge of provisions and supply necessary for such a voyage? But what would be my payment for providing such a service? Answer not so quickly! I have the answer: this will permit me to open up new markets across the Bay! What new goods will I be able to acquire? The mind truly reels at the possibilities!\
\
'I accept! There is one small complication, however. I had some of my workers put papers up all over town advertising my status as the King's Own Merchant and detailing the movement of my shop to Minas Tirith, but if I am to join you on your ship I will not be able to make the move just yet. The posters must come down! Burn them in a brazier here in Calembel after you have removed them. I cannot join your crew until this is done!'","'Excuse me, I could not help but notice that you have gone and burned up all the notices my son and I were ordered to put up around town. It took us all morning to do, and now you've gone and ruined all that work! What is the meaning of... the meaning of...'\
\
The man pauses.\
\
'${PLAYER}? It IS you! It has been a long time since our paths crossed! I did not expect to see you again, let alone for you to work at cross-purposes to me and my son! Galengam had us putting up those notices to advertise that his shop will be moving to Minas Tirith. Why have you taken them down?'\
\
You tell Bandron that Galengam will be sailing with you to Umbar, and therefore his other plans have been halted for now. The waggon-driver's eyes light up, and despite his age he dances a merry jig on the cobblestones.\
\
'What wonderful tidings you bring! My son will be delighted to hear it as well: at last we will have a break from Galengam's orders! He is always sending us all over Gondor, ${PLAYER}, with nary a rest in-between each journey. Do you think you could make this voyage take as long as possible, and give my boy and I a true holiday? Endless thanks to you, my friend!'","'I had some of my workers put papers up all over town advertising my status as the King's Own Merchant and detailing the movement of my shop to Minas Tirith, but if I am to join you on your ship I will not be able to make the move just yet. The posters must come down! Burn them in a brazier here in Calembel after you have removed them. I cannot join your crew until this is done!'","The brazier by the southern entrance to Calembel, in King's Gondor West, will be an effective way to dispose of Galengam's notices.","The Crew: The King's Own Merchant","Galengam, the King's own merchant, has joined your crew!","Bandron, standing nearby, has attracted your attention.","Burn Galengam's notices in the brazier located near the southern entrance of Calembel, in King's Gondor West","Caebar believes the merchant Galengam might prove a useful member of the crew, if he can be convinced to join your cause.","'There is one small complication. I had some of my workers put papers up all over town advertising my status as the King's Own Merchant and detailing the movement of my shop to Minas Tirith, but if I am to join you on your ship I will not be able to make the move just yet. The posters must come down! Burn them in a brazier here in Calembel after you have removed them. I cannot join your crew until this is done!'","Collected Galengam's notices (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Galengam's notices can be found throughout Calembel, in King's Gondor West."},
[11934]={"'It will be just like the old days, ${PLAYER}, when I sailed the waves and risked life and limb against the harsh elements! Oh, you never feel so alive as when you stand on the deck of a ship; any mariner will tell you so!\
\
'I will meet you beside the Wave-hunter when you are ready to depart. I look forward to meeting the rest of your crew, my friend! Together we will rescue young Thorongil, and no Corsair shall prevent us... and live!'","'Please watch out for my husband on your voyage. I do worry, even as I know he cannot stay.'","'Thank you, ${PLAYER}! Tell me about the ship we will be sailing to Umbar! Ah, it has been too long!'\
\
You tell Sirgon what you know about the Wave-hunter, little as it is, and he nods eagerly.\
\
'Golasgil of Anfalas was a mariner of great skill and ability. I knew him well, and we sailed together more than once. I believe he was as I am: a man of the Sea, but one whose duties called him away from the waves, to his great regret. I remember him fondly. It is right that his prized vessel will bear us to Umbar on the King's mission.\
\
'My wife and son will want to speak to you. They think I am too old to be of use, but I tell you they are wrong.'","Celebros and Faltharan are in Sirgon's manor, and will want to speak to you.","Talk to Faltharan in Sirgon's manor","'My husband believes he is still the same man he was when he commanded the fleets of Gondor, but it is not so. Time marches onward, and while his mind is as sharp as ever it was, my Sirgon has lived long since those days.'\
\
You ask Celebros if she wishes for you to withdraw your request, and she shakes her head.\
\
'I do not ask this of you, for I know he can be of great help to you and to King Elessar; I do not say he should remain behind, for I believe it would do him an injury, ${PLAYER}. Aye, being left behind while others sail again on such an urgent mission would deal him a grave hurt, perhaps his last.\
\
'He is a sailor, my Sirgon, and he has always been a sailor. He must go with you. But do keep a watchful eye on him, ${PLAYER}. I do worry, even as I know he cannot stay.'","King Elessar suggested that you recruit Sirgon, former Lord of Lebennin, for the mission to Umbar.","'My wife and son want to speak to you. They think I am too old to be of use, but I tell you they are wrong.'","Pick up Sirgon's trunk in the southern dining room","Talk to Sirgon inside his room of keepsakes","'I will continue to perform my duties as Lord of Lebennin while my father sails with you on your voyage. Please return him safely at the end of your mission, ${PLAYER}!'","Sirgon already packed his trunk, and he wants you to carry it to him from the southern dining room.","The Crew: The Sea-longing Lord","Sirgon is delighted you have brought him his trunk","Talk to Celebros in Sirgon's manor","'I have already packed my trunk, hoping beyond hope that a ship would have need of an old sailor for its crew. By the Valar, it has come to pass! Will you bring the trunk in here for me? It is in the southern dining room of my manor.'","Sirgon is inside his keepsake room in the northern part of his manor.","Sirgon, the sea-longing lord, has joined your crew!","'I understand you will sail with my father to Umbar on a mission of some secrecy, ${PLAYER}? No, I do not ask for any of the details. I think I have expected him to depart ever since I agreed to take over his duties as Lord of Lebennin. At least this seems to be on the King's behalf; my mother told me privately that she feared my father might sneak aboard a merchant ship and vanish in the night, just to set sail again. I do not think he would go so far... but it is better this way, I think.\
\
'Do what you can to keep him safe, my friend. He is not the man he was in his youth, when he freely sailed the Bay of Belfalas at the Steward's command, and challenged Corsair ships among the waves.'","'You return from your tour of Gondor with the King, and so quickly? What brings you back to my manor with such haste, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You tell Sirgon of what befell young Thorongil of Pinnath Gelin, and of the mission to bring him safely back from Umbar. His eyes light up and he eagerly grasps your hand.\
\
'I will be delighted to join your crew, my friend! I confess to you that thoughts of the Sea have occupied my dreams, and even my waking thoughts have dwelt upon it! Ever since I spoke with King Elessar and stepped down as the Lord of Lebennin I have desired to sail once again! My son Faltharan will take up the charge of rebuilding the vessels of the Gondorian navy; he is already well-acquainted with what must be done.\
\
'I have a further confession: I have already packed my trunk, hoping beyond hope that a ship would have need of an old sailor for its crew. By the Valar, it has come to pass! Will you bring the trunk in here for me? It is in the southern dining room of my manor.'"},
[11935]={"'You seek my husband Rossaran? I believe he departed Tadrent and headed to the north-east. Look for him there if you wish to speak with him.'","Collect Belfalas wild-flowers from the camp of Makham Mijann (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Thank you for these, ${PLAYER}. I will go now to Tadrent and speak with my wife, and if she is in a warm mood perhaps she will permit me to join your crew. You should follow along afterwards and see if we were successful in this.\
\
'If she does not permit it, I must refuse your offer. I hope you understand.'","'Perhaps you will help me gather some flowers for a bouquet? I will present them to her and she may be agreeable to this plan. I will, however, defer to her judgement in this, no matter what decision she arrives at. She is my wife, and I will not defy her wishes. You must understand, my friend.\
\
'I have seen wild-flowers growing throughout the camp of Makham Mijann, just to the west.'","The Swan-knight Rossaran is at Tadrent in King's Gondor West, preparing for the voyage.","Rossaran and Bruidis, the Swan-knight and the strategist, have joined your crew!","'What brings you back to these lands, ${PLAYER}? I believed you would spend longer than this in Outer Gondor with the King.'\
\
You tell Rossaran what befell young Thorongil in Pinnath Gelin, and of the Wave-hunter's need for a loyal crew to rescue him. The swan-knight rubs his chin, thinking deeply.\
\
'I want to serve my King in this, ${PLAYER}, but I have only just returned to my wife Bruidis after being long away. I do not think she will be pleased if I leave her again so soon!\
\
'Perhaps you will help me gather some flowers for a bouquet? I will present them to her and she may be agreeable to this plan. I will, however, defer to her judgement in this, no matter what decision she arrives at. She is my wife, and I will not defy her wishes. You must understand, my friend.\
\
'I have seen wild-flowers growing throughout the camp of Makham Mijann, just to the west.'","Talk to Rossaran north-east of Tadrent, in King's Gondor West","The Crew: The Swan-knight","'Greetings to you, ${PLAYER}. There is, as always, much work to be done here!\
\
'You seek my husband Rossaran? I believe he departed Tadrent and headed to the north-east. Look for him there if you wish to speak with him.'","Bring the Belfalas wild-flowers to Rossaran outside Makham Mijann, in King's Gondor West","Collected Belfalas wild-flowers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You! ${PLAYER}!'\
\
Bruidis holds your gaze with her eyes, but before you can speak any words in your defence, she laughs.\
\
'My husband Rossaran came here moments ago with a bouquet of flowers, thinking that would be enough for me to say he can sail away with you to Umbar, a fool on some other fool's errand. Aye, I say \\qfool,\\q for I know my dear Rossaran: he is brave and courageous, but he does not think things through as he should. For example: he believed a bouquet of flowers would so warm my heart that I would allow him to leave my side again, and so soon after he returned from the War! Can there be any other word for that than fool?'\
\
You apologize to Bruidis for asking her husband to join the crew of the Wave-hunter, and she looks at you curiously.\
\
'I did not say he could not join your crew, ${PLAYER}. I said he could not leave my side. That is why I am coming with you! Even now I have sent him to collect some supplies for the journey. Speak to him and see what he thinks of this; I believe you will find he is agreeable.'","The Swan-knight Rossaran is just outside the eastern entrance of Makham Mijann, in King's Gondor West.","'You came here for one crew-member, ${PLAYER}, but now you have two! To speak truthfully, I think my wife Bruidis may be a better addition to the crew than I, myself! She is a master of strategy and brilliant in tactical matters. In fact, I believe she made only a single mistake in her lifetime to this point, ${PLAYER}... marrying me! But I am glad for it.\
\
'We will be there when the Wave-hunter begins its voyage.'","'I will go now to Tadrent and speak with my wife, and if she is in a warm mood perhaps she will permit me to join your crew. You should follow along afterwards and see if we were successful in this.'","Rossaran's wife Bruidis is at Tadrent, in King's Gondor West, and she will have the final word on whether her husband joins the crew of the Wave-hunter.","Talk to Rossaran at Tadrent, in King's Gondor West","The Swan-knight Rossaran left Tadrent heading north-east.","The Swan-knight Rossaran has (conditionally) joined your crew!","Wild-flowers grow in the camp of Makham Mijann, north of Tadrent, in King's Gondor West.","'I did not say he could not join your crew, ${PLAYER}. I said he could not leave my side. That is why I am coming with you! Even now I have sent him to collect some supplies for the journey. Speak to him and see what he thinks of this; I believe you will find he is agreeable.'","The Swan-knight Rossaran will be a good addition to the crew of the Wave-hunter, if his wife Bruidis can be convinced to permit it.","Talk to Bruidis at Tadrent, in King's Gondor West"},
[11936]={"'I will not take you upon the river until you bring me the toll I require.'","The River-woman may be found along the banks of the river in the Mournshaws.\
\
You should return to the River-woman with the Cun Annun teeth that you have collected.","Talk to the old woman of the river in the Mournshaws","Collect Cun Annun teeth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bring the Cun Annun teeth to the River-woman in the Mournshaws","Tûm, a mystic of the Algraig clans known as a Derudh, told you of an old woman who plies the waters of the river. He believes this crone may know more about the spirits they call the Forest Lords than any other.","Cun Annun can be found throughout the Mournshaws.\
\
The River-woman has offered you passage along the river's length if you can bring her the teeth of the Cun Annun that haunt the forest in the Mournshaws.","Collected Cun Annun teeth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","La barca de la anciana","'So, you seek the Forest Lords? They are here, but no mortal may approach their halls uninvited. It is said that the Rhi Helvarch resents such intrusions upon his court. Mayhap one of his servants might call you forth, yet the Master of the Hall may still find you unworthy and your life forfeit. Who can say?\
\
'I can take you hither and yon upon the waters of this river, but the banks of it have become dangerous in these days, and I demand a toll for your passage first. The Cun Annun who stalk this forest are not of this place. They come upon evil winds, blowing out of the graves of Men to the East.\
\
'Slay these beasts and bring me a string of their teeth. Then shall I ferry you upon the river's length as you please, though it does not lead to the Huntsman's hall.'","'The Forest Lords may not heed our calls, Duvodiad, but there may be other ways to find their ancient halls. One such path may be through the old woman who has long plied the river that passes through Galar-gwig -- this place you call the Mournshaws.\
\
'No one has ever seen her beyond the boundaries of the forest, nor do the wild spirits of the wood seem to trouble her. We do not know who she is, save that she will occasionally allow others to ride the river's length with her in silence.\
\
'I have long suspected that she may be a servant of the Forest Lords, but she has never admitted this to me or any other. Seek her out along the banks of the river. Perhaps she will help you... or perhaps not.'","'Perhaps the old woman of the river may help you.'","'Give the teeth here. Yes... yes....\
\
'Very well, this will have to do. I shall grant you passage upon the river, Duvodiad.\
\
'But be warned that the Derudh here do not care for duvodiad -- outsiders -- and the Huntsman has no love for mortals of any nature, so you must be wary!'","The old woman Tûm spoke of can occasionally be found along the banks of the river that passes through the Mournshaws.\
\
Tûm suggested you find the old woman who plies the river of the Mournshaws. It is possible that she knows something of the Forest Lords."},
[11937]={"Myve, the child who seemed to covet the shiny toy, is somewhere in Galtrev.\
\
You should speak with Myve to see if she is hiding the shiny ball from its rightful owner.","'Envus is missing that silly shiny ball? Sure I looked at it, but I did not take it. What would I do with a ball like that? I want to play with spears, not useless, shiny toys.'","'So you come seeking to reclaim the palantír? I knew someone would be back for it; yes, it was my craban that brought it to me!\
\
'But hearken: a palantír is no toy for a child. \
\
'I am Rook, an apprentice Wizard. You should leave this dangerous object in my capable hands for the time being.'","'I heard you mention Envus' missing toy -- a shiny ball, you say? I think I saw a crow taking off with just such a ball last night.\
\
'It is strange, I know, but there could be no mistake. It was a black bird flying off with a shiny object clutched in its talons, heading north-west.'","Talk to Myve in Galtrev about the missing toy","Search Galtrev for someone with information about the toy ball","Someone who may have witnessed the pilfering of Envus's toy would likely be in Galtrev.\
\
You should look around and see if anyone saw someone make off with the shiny ball.","The Crow-thief","'My shiny ball is gone! It was a gift from my father, before he went away to battle the strawheads. I would give anything to find it, but it does not seem to be anywhere I look.\
\
'Could you ask around, please? Please, please, please! Maybe one of the other children took it. I know Myve was looking at it quite a lot when my father first gave it to me....'","Find the crow that stole the child's toy ball","A child's toy ball seems to have gone missing, and a witness is positive it was stolen by a crow.","'The shiny ball is the only toy I really care about. This is terrible!'","It would appear that a crow has flown off with the shiny ball","The crow that stole the ball was seen flying to the north-west.\
\
You should head north-west to try and recover Envus' favourite toy.","Myve had no interest in the toy, but perhaps someone else in Galtrev saw something"},
[11938]={"The bird seems to say, 'Drive me off, I care not. My belly is full. I have already won.'","Talk to Miruhir","The Crows of Iáphel","Pesky birds are feasting on wine grapes in Iáphel.","'I have a sickle-fly problem and a bird problem. You would think the birds would eat the sickle-flies for me but no, that would be too convenient.\
\
'The crows have seen fit to roost amongst the trellises along the western slope of the hill, just outside Iáphel's walls. Please shoo them away for me.'","Shoo birds (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Miruhir has asked you to shoo away birds that are eating valuable wine grapes at his vineyard in Iáphel.\
\
Shoo away birds.","You are confident that birds cannot cry, but this bird sounds like it is crying","The bird swears vengeance with a sharp cry. 'You have won this day, but my revenge shall be terrible.'","The bird flies away, forlorn and distraught","'I know they will be back tomorrow, but thank you all the same.'","You should tell Miruhir that you have shooed the birds away.\
\
Miruhir can be found in Iáphel.","The bird seems to say 'Curse you! I wasn't done eating!'"},
[11940]={"'¿Qué has encontrado ahí, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}? ¡Qué interesante! ¿Encontraste algo de importancia en su... esto, en su cuerpo?'\
\
Le muestras la piedra. Un brillo extraño cruza sus ojos.\
\
'¡Qué objeto tan singular! ¡Debería quedármelo! Ah, para mi investigación. Bueno, creo que ya podemos irnos. Lo que sea que matase a Ragnal podría seguir aquí abajo.'\
\
'¿Cómo sabes su nombre?', preguntas preparando tu arma.\
\
'¿Qué? Su... ah, bueno, ¡no hace falta que te pongas tan ${PLAYERNAME:violento[m]|violenta[f]}! Está bien, está bien. No soy ningún historiador. ¿Pero a ti qué te importa? Oh. Ya veo que te importa mucho. ¡Toma! Quédate con el maldito chisme. No necesito morir por una piedra.'","'¡Te doy la bienvenida de nuevo! ¿Has encontrado algo interesante?'\
\
Le entregas la piedra.\
\
'¡Fascinante! Esto es una Gwelumir, una piedra meteorológica. Lamentablemente ha perdido la mayor parte de su función, pero cuando fue creada, habría indicado el clima de una zona determinada. Fueron un experimento que se consideró un fracaso, ya que uno podía mirar fácilmente al cielo para contar las nubes. ¿Dices que encontraste esto en un antiguo smial? ¡Qué uso tan perfecto para un dispositivo así! Debió ser un regalo para un amigo de los Elfos hace mucho tiempo. ¡Gracias por traérmela! Estoy deseando estudiar sus propiedades.'","Llévale la piedra a Narnien","Las salas en ruinas de Glynafon","Los agujeros abandonados de Glynafon están en el este del Ángulo.\
\
Deberías explorar los agujeros abandonados y llevarle a Cedivor cualquier cosa de interés.","Narnien se encuentra en Gaerond, en el norte del Ángulo.\
\
Deberías decirle a Narnien que has encontrado un extraño artefacto.","'Tal vez el veneno fue demasiado. Los huargos hicieron el trabajo por mí. ¡Vaya! ¿Sigues aquí?'\
\
Cedivor tose y parece incómodo.","¡Has encontrado una piedra extrañamente tallada!","Explora los agujeros abandonados","'¡Hola! ¡Vaya, pareces exactamente el tipo de ayuda que necesito! ¡Soy Cedivor Hedgerow, gran historiador y experto en artefactos!'\
\
Hace una pausa, esperando una reacción por tu parte.\
\
'¿No... has oído hablar de mí? Bueno, supongo que alguien como tú no se mantiene al día con este tipo de cosas. ¿Demasiado ${PLAYERNAME:ocupado[m]|ocupada[f]} recorriendo el país siendo ${PLAYERNAME:un héroe[m]|una heroína[f]} y teniendo aventuras? Exactamente la persona que he estado buscando. Verás, estoy explorando las ruinas que salpican las colinas y los bosques del Ángulo, pero necesito ayuda en estas tierras peligrosas.\
\
'No puedo entrar en las guaridas de los huargos, pero sospecho que hay antiguas viviendas enterradas en estas colinas. ¡Un lugar llamado Glynafon! Si encuentras algo de interés allí dentro y me lo traes, ¡te recompensaré enormemente!'","Cedivor Hedgerow, un renombrado historiador y experto en artefactos, busca protección mientras se adentra en las salas en ruinas de Glynafon.","'¿Dónde está? Debe de estar... ¿Qué es eso? No, no te estaba diciendo nada a ti. Solo reflexionaba en voz baja, je, je. ¿Dónde están? Decía... Los... esto, los magníficos hobbits artesanos que una vez llamaron a esta pocilga... eh, a estos espléndidos túneles su hogar.'","Cedivor Hedgerow se encuentra a las afueras de Glynafon, en el este del Ángulo.\
\
Deberías llevarle la piedra a Cedivor.","Muéstrale la piedra a Cedivor"},
[11942]={"Lost pages from the journal of an Angmarim sorceress are scattered across Elderslade.","Lost pages from the Crystal Journal can be found across Elderslade.\
\
You should look for more pages from the Crystal Journal.","Collect the third page","Collected the Crystal Journal's tenth page","Collect the second page","Collect the sixth page","Collected the Crystal Journal's seventh page","Collected the Crystal Journal's sixth page","Collected the Crystal Journal's ninth page","Collected the Crystal Journal's fifth page","Collect the tenth page","The Crystal Journal","Bring your findings to Mother Amma","Collect the fourth page","Collect the seventh page","Collect the new journal","Collect the fifth page","Collected the Crystal Journal's third page","From across the wasted lands of Elderslade you have gathered the missing pages of the Crystal Journal, as well as the sorceress' new records.\
\
Bring your findings to Mother Amma in the forge at Annâk-khurfu.","Collected the Crystal Journal's eighth page","Collect the first page","'The missing pages may help us understand what has happened to these fell stones, and their purpose.'","Collected the Crystal Journal's second page","'You have found more pages from the journal? Excellent! Give them here and let us see what we have.'\
\
You hand Mother Amma the pages and the new journal. Her brow furrows as she reads through them quickly.\
\
'A mysterious spell cast on the sarrowstones makes Wargs even more deadly and vicious... and mad. It is good that you defeated Brágha before she could share her discoveries or find a way to use the crystals on anyone or anything else. \
\
'Give me a moment....'\
\
Mother Amma shuffles the pages, putting them into order then putting them into the new journal. She hands the new crystal journal to you.\
\
'What a wicked person! It is a shame we know not what she found after following her superior into the darkness. There are still many questions, but the answers seem to lie deep in the bowels of Gundabad. Well, we have plans to be there soon, my friend. I have ordered the pages for you.'","Collected the Crystal Journal's first page","Collect the eighth page","'One of the scouts brought back a few pieces of parchment they found scattered around Elderslade. They seem to be part of an account recording a study into the strange crystals. Perhaps if you locate the rest, we might unlock the secrets of the stones and discover their creator.'","Collect the ninth page","Collected the Crystal Journal's fourth page","Collected the new Crystal Journal"},
[11943]={"Derrota a los orcos Ghâsh-hai en Hurmulkezer","Has derrotado a varios orcos Ghâsh-hai en Hurmulkezer, debilitando sus fuerzas y asegurando que ya no representen una amenaza.","Derrota a los orcos Ghâsh-hai en Hurmulkezer (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los Ghâsh-hai de Hurmulkezer son bastante fuertes, lo que convierte a las Profundidades Llameantes en un lugar mortal para los enanos que han intentado recuperarlas.","Debes derrotar a los orcos Ghâsh-hai en Hurmulkezer para diezmar sus filas, ya que representan una amenaza mortal para los enanos de las Profundidades Llameantes.","La Purga","Los orcos Ghâsh-hai se encuentran en Hurmulkezer, al sur del Patio de Durin, en el extremo sureste de las Profundidades Llameantes.\
\
Debes derrotar a los orcos en Hurmulkezer.","Completado","Orco Ghâsh-hai derrotado (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[11944]={"Faeron and Rhadrog can be found in Viznak's hideout.\
\
You should give the disgusting concoction to both of the Rangers.","Collect infected livers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'He wants to be partners?! There must be some ulterior motive. I have never known a goblin to not be a scheming little ball of slime. Regardless of how much I want to strangle him, we must work with him for now, or we stand no chance of survival in this disgusting bog. Perhaps we can even learn enough about Seregost and its leader to report back some useful information before we are inevitably betrayed.'","Viznak mentioned he had a mixing bowl in his hideout.\
\
You should mix the ingredients together in the mixing bowl.","Talk to Faeron","Rhadrog seems less tense almost immediately","Collect Plague Mushrooms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected infected insect guts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Good! We friends now. First thing, fix sickness! I discover making tasty drink from swamp stuff make it go away! Don't know how, don't care. You go get stuff, mix in bowl, and drink! All better. You and grumpy better drink it, too. You not sick now, but you will be! Here, I make you list.'\
\
He hands you some grubby paper with drawings on it. You think you can decipher what this means.","Collected Plague Mushrooms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Drink the disgusting concoction","The disgusting concoction has been created and awaits you in Viznak's hideout.\
\
You should bravely attempt to ingest the disgusting concoction.","Collect swamp water (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected infected livers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Viznak has been rescued and decides to help you save Rhadrog. Gather ingredients from the wilds of Agarnaith and brew a concoction to counteract the virulent disease.","It is the worst thing you have ever tasted!","Talk to Viznak","Faeron can be found in Viznak's hideout.\
\
You should talk to Faeron about Viznak's proposition.","'Glad you are back. Rhadrog's situation is dire. I have managed to get some information out of our new 'friend' here.  Seregost lies to the north-east, at the end of the swamp, and he made it sound massive. He also mentioned that the 'Blight Lady' rules Agarnaith. I know not what manner of creature he speaks of, but he seemed frightened at the mere mention of her.\
\
'I have to drink this liquid, then? Well, you are still alive. I guess I will take my chances.'","The Cure","'You nice guys and save me from nasty infected Orcs. I help you out and fix green-cloak. His name Rhadrog? Yes, but we can do better. We form partnership. You hate Orcs, I hate Orcs, we good team. I the brains, you the muscle! It will be great! Talk it over with grumpy guy.'","'Tasty, right? Why you make faces?\
\
'Rhadrog better soon. Needs sleep now. Let's get to work!'","Mix disgusting concoction in mixing bowl","Collect infected insect guts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected swamp water (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The ingredients mush together into a thick, foul-smelling liquid","Viznak can be found in his hideout.\
\
You should talk to Viznak.","Help Rhadrog take the concoction","Viznak has provided a list of ingredients that can be found in the wilds of Agarnaith.\
\
Infected livers can be collected from gore-crows, wolves, boars, and rats. Infected insect guts can be collected from sickle-flies, nerbyg, and swarming flies. You should collect infected livers, plague mushrooms, swamp water, and infected insect guts."},
[11945]={"Ground razed (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Return to Tálbiral in Laivárth","'The blight continues to seep into the grove. I need your help, ${CLASS}.\
\
'Take this torch and this oil. Outside of Laivárth you will see where I have razed the ground before. I ask that you do this again and stop the saplings from growing and spreading their tainted roots through the earth.\
\
'It pains me to hurt the grove this way, but it must be done to prevent the blight from consuming it.'","Raze ground (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I see that you have returned and that the grounds near Laivárth have been cleansed again. That will allow us more time to do what we can to save the grove.\
\
'I thank you, ${CLASS}. It pains me each time the task must be done. You have spared me of that pain this day.'","The Cure is Flame","Tálbiral has asked that you raze the ground surrounding Laivárth and any blighted saplings you encounter to prevent the spread from getting closer to the grove.","Burn saplings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Tálbiral will want to know that you successfully removed the saplings and razed the ground again. Return to him in Laivárth.","Saplings burned (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[11948]={"Dol Acharn can be found in eastern Dagorlad.\
\
Faramir has asked you to approach the hill to confirm his suspicions about the Wainriders. You should scout the hill carefully.","Talk to Faramir near Dol Acharn","Faramir can be found due west of Dol Acharn in Dagorlad.\
\
You attempted to reach the hill-top of Dol Acharn but found your efforts repelled by an unseen force that sapped your will to press onward. You should return to Faramir and tell him of what you have experienced.","The Wainriders have claimed the hill of Dol Acharn, but they must be challenged if you are to stand between them and the Host of the West.","The Cursed Hill","<rgb=#FF0000>An unseen force saps your will to press forth and your morale begins to waver!</rgb>","Attempt to approach the hill-top of Dol Acharn","'It is as I feared... it seems only the Wainriders themselves can stand upon the hill without succumbing to fear.\
\
'I had hoped you would not encounter such resistance from the Wainriders before even confronting them, but it seems our cause grows more desperate.\
\
'I may know a way to allow you to travel onto Dol Acharn without hindrance, but it shall not be an easy task.'","'Your friends can rest easy for the moment, ${CLASS}, but rest shall not soon come to me.\
\
'Even in this form beyond death, I have done naught to stop the countless horrors I have witnessed, and I can bear it no longer. This fallen man of Númenor, Burudagath, perverts the banner of my father and kills without mercy... and the Wainriders that rose in answer to the strife in these lands have slain the men of your company with fear alone. These two foes stand in defiance of Gondor on the hills of Dagorlad... and there remains no force to stop them.\
\
'Yet, I believe that I have found a means to set our foes upon each other.\
\
'However, such a ruse demands swaying the attention of the Wainriders... and that shall be no simple task.'"},
[11951]={"After aiding the villages of Alagrant and Sardol, you have uncovered dangerous new threats to Blackroot Vale that you must reveal to Malthellam and Rosfin.","Talk to Rosfin","Talk to Malthellam in Morlad","The Cursed Vale","'Come, let us speak inside.'","Talk to Malthellam","Malthellam can be found in Morlad, outside his home.\
\
Malthellam has asked you to speak with him and Rosfin about what you encountered in Alagrant and Sardol.","'It heartens me to know that so much is being done on our behalf, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Yet, I can see that something has troubled you. Come, let us talk of what concerns you.'","'${PLAYER}, I have seldom felt as frightened as I am now.\
\
'You have seen what vile things rise against us, but I fear that there are few options left for us. I beg you, please travel back to Morlad and tell Malthellam of what you have seen!\
\
'I only hope it is not too late!'","DNT -- will not be seen","Malthellam can be found outside his home in Morlad in north-western Blackroot Vale.\
\
You have been urged to return to Malthellam by Gordir, who hopes that your experiences in Alagrant and Sardol will goad the Steward into taking action.","Lady Rosfin can be found outside Malthellam's home in Morlad.\
\
You have finished speaking with Lady Rosfin and Malthellam about the threats you encountered in the south, and should now speak to Rosfin.","'I have heard enough, ${PLAYER}. If we do not act now, we may as well surrender our lives and lands.\
\
'However, I do not plan on giving up so easily....'"},
[11953]={"Alla vitorea mientras te acercas.","Habla con Alla en el noreste de Musgovilla.","Alla te ha dado cinco minutos para llegar al lugar indicado al borde del Aguaestancada, al norte de Musgovilla.","Alla está junto a un pajar en el noreste de Musgovilla. ¡Solo tienes cinco minutos para el viaje de regreso!","'Pareces bastante valiente. No le tienes miedo a nada, ¿verdad?\
\
'Quizá puedas ayudarme, entonces. El bravucón de Musgovilla me ha desafiado a correr hasta cierto lugar al norte del pueblo, justo en el mismo borde del Aguaestancada, y luego regresar... ¡todo en diez minutos! No es que tenga miedo, pero quiero estar segura de que es posible. ¿Qué te parece usar no más de cinco minutos para llegar hasta allí y cinco minutos para volver? Así sabré que puede hacerse antes de intentarlo yo.\
\
'Aquí, lo marcaré en tu mapa. Es justo aquí.'","El Desafío","'¡El tiempo se pierde! Si no puedes llegar a ese lugar en el borde de Aguaestancada en cinco minutos, ¿cómo se supone que lo haga yo?'","'¡Date prisa!'","Alla está junto a un pajar en el noreste de Musgovilla.","'¡Lo lograste! Debo admitir que no estaba segura de que pudieras ir hasta allí y volver a tiempo... ¡pero lo hiciste!\
\
'Entonces, ¿viste algo cuando llegaste allí?'\
\
Le cuentas que había una canasta con un ovillo de hilo dentro junto al Aguaestancada, lo cual parecía bastante extraño.\
\
'Ya veo, sí. Eso es peculiar. Gracias por tu ayuda.'","<rgb=#FF0000>No te quedes sin tiempo antes de llegar al lugar correcto</rgb>","Regresa con Alla en el noreste de Musgovilla sin quedarte sin tiempo.","Se te ha acabado el tiempo","Llega al lugar marcado en el borde del Aguaestancada sin quedarte sin tiempo.","Un niño de Musgovilla ha sido desafiado por el bravucón del pueblo a realizar una carrera peligrosa, y quiere asegurarse de que sea posible antes de intentarlo.","Este es el lugar que Alla describió. De manera extraña, hay aquí una canasta con un ovillo de hilo dentro."},
[11954]={"'Very good, ${PLAYER}! The Nine will surely be angered that one of their favoured slaves has been destroyed, but this should break the spells gathering power against us here.\
\
'Now Fuirgam should be able to focus his attention towards Gathbúrz and Dol Guldur and not have to worry about a strike at his flank from Taur Morvith.'","Talk to Ianudirel","Defeat Mâb Rhûnadan","'I have found where the Enemy conducts the rituals to summon fell spirits to Taur Morvith. There is an altar in the crumbling cellar of one of the ruins to the south-east...but I also found out what power is behind it. There is a Cargûl -- one of the cursed knights of Eärnur -- hiding somewhere in those ruins! I have heard his name whispered by his servants. He is known as Mâb Rhûnadan. \
\
'I consulted Agorin on the matter. It seems that this creature is a favoured apprentice to one of the Nine, and a powerful sorcerer in his own right. Be very careful should you encounter him!\
\
'If you can make your way to the altar and destroy it, that should put an end to their power here for the time being -- barring that, you may have to destroy the Cargûl himself. I also doubt he will allow you to interfere with his place of power unmolested.'","Destroy the corrupted altar","The altar remains undamaged as a cold air sweeps through the ruins...","'Destroy the altar, ${PLAYER}, or if you cannot, defeat the Cargûl himself. To be forced to such corruption must be a terrible thing for a knight such as he once was...free him!'","The Dark Apprentice","The Cargûl, Mâb Rhûnadan, dwells among the ruins of Sâd Morangol, using a corrupt altar to summon fell spirits to Taur Morvith.","Mâb Rhûnadan and his altar may be found at Sâd Morangol.\
\
Ianudirel has asked you to destroy the altar of Mâb Rhûnadan or defeat the Cargûl himself.","Ianudirel is just south of the bridge at Krul Lugu.\
\
You should return to Ianudirel with news of your success.","Defeated Mâb Rhûnadan"},
[11956]={"Speak with Mílgamel","Collected phial of viscous poison (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","A workbench can be found at Henneth Annûn.\
\
You should bring the phials of poison to Henneth Annûn for study.","This grey goo is similar but contains bits of what appear to be a lichen in it","Collect phials of viscous poison (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Mílgamel can be found at Henneth Annûn.\
\
You should take the poisons and what you have learned to her.","Mílgamel is concerned with a decaying corpse of one of the animals brought in from the wilds. She believes Cair Andros may hold the key.","Collect phials of refined poison (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Study the phials of viscous poison at Henneth Annûn","This grey goo is acidic and watered down","Study the phials of refined poison at Henneth Annûn","'The Rangers brought back a mangled animal corpse from the wilds. It was struck with an arrow of Orkish design.\
\
'The peculiar thing is not the arrow, but the state of the animal's body. The corpse is sickened and in a rapid state of decay. The Rangers say the ground surrounding the animal was devoid of flora.\
\
'This is all very concerning. Perhaps it was unwise to pass Cair Andros by, after all. The forces from Mordor at Cair Andros must be coating their arrows with something most vile. Something not seen upon the Pelennor Battlefield (or else I would recognize it), and therefore, perhaps, concocted here in North Ithilien! It is not why Master Galathir sent me, or an inquiry he would approve of, but I must know what this substance is.\
\
'I shall not accompany you to Cair Andros, as my lack of skill in combat would only slow you down - and endanger myself - but I beseech you, go and gather what you can of this poison, so we may study it.'","Collected phial of refined poison (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'A moss you say? That is no lichen of which I ever heard! And so my wonderment grows, and I find myself drawn to stray from the confining course Master Galathir has set for me. Yet if I do all he asks - then what study I make beyond it is no concern of his, do you not agree?'\
\
She meets your eye with a new boldness in hers.\
\
'Let us suppose for a moment that this grey lichen is most deadly and is the main ingredient used in making the poison. Indeed, I recall that I have read of poisonous mosses before. It would not be a stretch. And if we suppose, as well, that the lichen grows native somewhere within these lands east of the Anduin, there is hope we may learn more about it.'","The Dark Lord's Blight","Phials of poison can be found on Uruks and Orcs in Cair Andros.\
\
You should collect phials of poison."},
[11958]={"'Our siege weapons had toppled the tower, and the Scourge sought to admire his handiwork.'","'Balakhôr had little to say for the rest of our journey.'","La oscuridad sobre Lebennin","Talk to the Night-jewel deckhand","Meet the Scourge at the peak of Barad Rill","Balakhôr and the Black Blade of Lebennin can be found atop Barad Rill.\
\
Daxamar is describing the meeting between one of the Nine and Balakhôr. You should listen to his tale.","'My fellow deckhands were still picking away at the wreckage when I entered the ruin...'","Balakhôr can be found atop Barad Rill.\
\
Daxamat then went into Barad Rill to seek Balakhôr at the top.","'Then there he was... looking out onto Dor-en-Ernil with a smile.'","'That took you a while...\
\
'Currents a little rough for you today, Dax?'","The Night-jewel deckhand can be found on the shore of Barad Rill.\
\
Daxamat made landfall with his brethren at Barad Rill and then spoke to a deckhand.","After shattering the lighthouse at Barad Rill, Balakhôr the Scourge has called Daxamat to the peak to look upon the lands he intends to claim.","Balakhôr seems lost in thought as his gaze falls on Dor-en-Ernil, but he swiftly notices your presence.","Observe the meeting of the Black Blade and Balakhôr","The peak of Barad Rill can be found by climbing the stairs in the ruin.\
\
Daxamat searched Barad Rill for Balakhôr and climbed toward the top of the ruin.","Talk to Balakhôr the Scourge","The lighthouse of Barad Rill can be found at the centre of the small shoal off the southern coast of Dor-en-Ernil.\
\
The deckhand has directed Daxamat to enter the lighthouse and speak to the Scourge at his request.","Enter the lighthouse of Barad Rill"},
[11959]={"La oscuridad sobre Lebennin","'Let me tell you my tale, ${CLASS}.'","Talk to Daxamat in Hata Kebir","'I ask again, brother, why have you come here?'\
\
Jajax explains his desire to help Daxamat escape from the Heirs of Castamir before they bring themselves to ruin.\
\
'You will have little trouble convincing me, Jajax, for I have seen things you would not believe... but it is one thing to wish to help me, and another entirely to steal me away under Azgarzôr's gaze.\
\
'These grim clouds hide far worse things... terrible things that weigh heavily on me. Let me tell you my tale, and then we can speak of leaving this place.'","After shattering the lighthouse at Barad Rill, Balakhôr the Scourge has called Daxamat to the peak to look upon the lands he intends to claim.","Daxamat can be found in the northernmost part of Hata Kebir in eastern Lebennin.\
\
Daxamat has finished telling the tale of his encounter with the Black Blade of Lebennin. You should speak to him.","Daxamat can be found in the northernmost part of Hata Kebir in eastern Lebennin.\
\
Daxamat has asked to share his account of an upsetting meeting he witnessed in Dor-en-Ernil. You should listen to his tale.","Listen to Daxamat's recounting of his journey through Dor-en-Ernil","'Now, do you understand? That terrible wraith, one of the Nine, looked upon Balakhôr as a mere tool... how lowly might the rest of us be in the Master's eye?\
\
'Balakhôr has his mind set only on Pelargir, and I fear that if we fail to reach the Guarded City in time, there will be no place for our people to hide from the Dark Lord's gaze.\
\
'I see no way off this course, brother, other than to flee.'"},
[11960]={"Find where the Rhachló flows through Caras Tilion","When you listen, you can hear the sound of running water","Search for artifacts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The waters are still befouled","A strange pile of rust catches your eye","Caras Tilion can be found in the mountains on the southern border of Eryn Lasgalen.\
\
Search Caras Tilion for dark artifacts.","Caras Tilion can be found in the mountains on the southern border of Eryn Lasgalen.\
\
The Rhachló must flow through Caras Tilion.","Radagast has suggested that you should return to Caras Tilion, in the mountains on the southern border of Eryn Lasgalen.","Radagast believes that another source hidden in the ruins of Caras Tilion darkens the Rhachló.","Radagast can be found at the tree nursery just outside of Felegoth.\
\
You should return to Radagast and tell him all that you saw in Caras Tilion.","Could someone have gotten here before you?","'Emptied and broken, every one? Would that it had been some helpful benefactor... but I fear it is not so!\
\
'Not all mysteries are neatly tied up with a ribbon, ${PLAYER}. If the evil that has poisoned the Rhachló is in Caras Tilion no longer, I shall know by watching the plants and rivers, not by running about after wild geese. The corruption will fade and we will call it Lúthir once again. \
\
'That is my purpose and I will keep to it. Yours lies elsewhere, ${PLAYER}. Go where you are needed, but keep open your eyes and ears. Who knows? Perhaps the riddle shall be solved one day!'","Habla con Radagast","There is nothing inside the chest","'All the same, it is well that you defeated that servant of shadow, whoever he may have been. I wonder what brought him to Caras Tilion? Was he sent in advance from Dol Guldur, in overconfidence of their victory? Or in flight from their downfall? Or else...'\
\
Radagast rails off in thought.\
\
'But as I was saying, the river's corruption cannot have been his doing alone. Did you note any evil relics, any talismans of corruption, while you were there? Ah, but you were kept busy in wariness and combat. \
\
'I think... perhaps... I would ask you to go back and see what else might be found in Caras Tilion.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: You will swiftly travel back to Caras Tilion when you accept this quest.</rgb>","Caras Tilion can be found in the mountains on the southern border of Eryn Lasgalen.\
\
Search Caras Tilion for anything from Dol Guldur that isn't broken.","Continue searching","The Darkness Remains","This artifact is broken","Return to Caras Tilion"},
[11961]={"Defeat armoured shadows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Explored the eastern overlook","Explored the southern overlook","'There you are. I had begun to worry. I have wounded my leg somehow - upon some sorcerous trap, most likely.\
\
'But never mind that, ${PLAYER}. There is someone here - a man, an Elf, a wraith, I know not what. I think they have dwelt here some while!'","The Darkness in Caras Tilion","Having explored and dealt with the shadows, you should reconvene with Oroniel in Caras Tilion.","Caras Tilion can be found in the mountains at the southern edge of Eryn Lasgalen.\
\
You should investigate Caras Tilion and defeat any of the darkness within its crumbled walls.","Defeated armoured shadows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You should investigate Caras Tilion, which can be found in the mountains at the southern edge of Eryn Lasgalen.","You hear Oroniel shout your name from somewhere nearby!","Defeat sorcerous spirits (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'This river has been darkly enchanted for many lives of Men, at times more so and at other times less. But that corruption should now be waning - not growing stronger!\
\
'Upstream from here, these waters course past the old ruins of Caras Tilion. The place once was an Elven-hold, but we have long shunned it. I fear we must dare to tread there now, no matter what old memories or new inhabitants there dwell.'","Enter Caras Tilion","Explored the central courtyard","Explored the northern courtyard","Explore the eastern overlook","Reconvene with Oroniel","You should go quickly to Oroniel, where she called out for aid in Caras Tilion.","Explore the central courtyard","Explore the southern overlook","Oroniel suspects the growing corruption of the river Rhachló may come from the abandoned ruins of Caras Tilion.","Defeated sorcerous spirits (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Come to Oroniel's aid","Explore the northern courtyard","The ruins lie deep in shadow. Things move among the darkness."},
[11962]={"Talk to Harnion","Umbarrim sorcerers can be found in Corsair encampments in Tarlang's Crown.\
\
Gondren has asked you to defeat Umbarrim sorcerers to prevent them from bringing forth any more fell spirits in Tarlang's Crown.","Defeat Umbarrim sorcerers in Tarlang's Crown (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Darkness of Númenor","'I do not have much time, ${PLAYER}...\
\
'...so should you wish to honour the last request of a dying man, heed my words! There are Men here that wield foul power - power that no man should ever have. I have seen it with my own eyes, ${PLAYER}... I have seen their sorcerers calling forth vile spirits of the same lot that took hold of the trolls.\
\
'These Men alone could spell doom for Dol Amroth, and they must be defeated before their might grows beyond control. Go now, my friend... let us hope there are brighter days ahead....'","Harnion can be found along the road through Tarlang's Crown, to the north of Edhellond in Belfalas.\
\
You have defeated many Umbarrim sorcerers and stopped them from summoning more vile fell spirits into Gondor. You should now return to Harnion.","DNT -- will not be seen","Vile sorcerers of Umbar serve Azruthor tirelessly and seek to bring forth more fell spirits in Tarlang's Crown.","Defeated Umbarrim sorcerers in Tarlang's Crown (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Gondren's sacrifice may have saved us from ruin, ${PLAYER}. Without his aid, we would have learned of the Heirs' plans far too late to act against them.\
\
'You have done well to weaken their reinforcements and break their resolve. Soon, my friend, we shall strike at Azruthor himself.\
\
'Let us hope that his forces remain weakened when the time comes....'"},
[11963]={"Defeat Iárvereth","The Daughters of Iphantemel are lurking somewhere in Taurlingol.\
\
You should defeat Lhothbad, Iárvereth, and Saeriel.","Defeated Iárvereth","Legolas can be found on a hill near Taurlingol.\
\
You should talk to Legolas.","Iphantemel's own daughters hide in Taurlingol, attempting the retain control of the Mirkwood spiders.","Defeated Lhothbad","The Daughters of Iphantemel","Habla con Legolas.","'You have given my people a great gift with the deaths of these horrible monsters. Their deaths have been avenged.'","Defeat Lhothbad","'The spider you defeated with Atli, Aegarach, was a daughter of Iphantemel herself. If one is here, her sisters will be as well. They are known to me: Lhothbad, Iárvereth, Saeriel. Terrible all. I speculate that they are the reason that some of the Mirkwood spiders have separated themselves from the rest. Perhaps they are attempting to retain control of their brood. Regardless, these sisters must be hunted down. They are responsible for the deaths of many of my people.'","Defeat Saeriel","Defeated Saeriel"},
[11964]={"'Find out what you must, but then let us leave. Make haste!'","'I will tell you everything I can recall from that day, ${PLAYER}.'","'For your help, kind stranger, I have done my best to think back to the day we fled Dunfast.\
\
'If you would like to hear it, I can share my tale.'","Cyneberg hopes that the people from Dunfast will be able to recall what happened when Núrzum arrived, now that their survival is assured.","Gifemund can be found at the refugees' hideout in the Whitshaws.\
\
You should talk to Gifemund to find out more about the refugees' story.","Cyneberg is at the refugees' hideout south-west of Dunfast.\
\
You should speak with Cyneberg.","'It was good of Gifemund to try to remember his tale. What do you think you will do next?'","Speak with Cyneberg","El día que vino el gigante","Listen to Gifemund's tale"},
[11965]={"'¿Bregar sigue intentando desviar mi camino?'\
\
Los ojos del Elfo se abren al leer el pergamino. '\\qY maldita la nave infiel que lo llevó lejos de Nimrodel...\\q Aunque es una historia triste, siempre fue una de mis favoritas. Habla de Amroth y Nimrodel, su separación y la llegada de mucha tristeza a Lothlórien, hogar de nuestra gente.\
\
'Bregar tiene razón. Hay mucho por hacer aquí antes de partir. No llevaré mi dolor a bordo de los Barcos Blancos ni lo llevaré al Oeste. Gracias por ayudarme a entender, ${PLAYER}.'","'Mi hermano y yo nos quedaremos para enfrentar la Sombra en el Este una última vez.'","Langlas te ha dado un pergamino para llevar a Bregar en Duillond. Bregar reconoció el poema como el \\qLamento de Nimrodel\\q y se dio cuenta de que un pasaje del Lamento podría ser suficiente para convencer a Toronn de permanecer en la Tierra Media.","'Habla con mi hermano Toronn. Está en Celondim, al sur.'","'Gracias, ${PLAYER}, por ayudar a mi hermano a entrar en razón.'","Toronn está en Celondim, al sur de Duillond.\
\
Bregar te ha pedido que lleves el pergamino a Toronn con la esperanza de que convenza a su hermano de quedarse.","'Juntos, Bregar y yo nos enfrentaremos a la Sombra de Mordor una última vez.'","Lleva el \\qLamento de Nimrodel\\q a Toronn en Celondim","'Gracias por traerme el pergamino, ${PLAYER}. Mi partida habría traído mucha tristeza.'","'Langlas realmente me ha hecho un gran favor al enviarte esto. El \\qLamento de Nimrodel\\q es una historia triste que tiene relación con nuestra situación. \
\
Por favor, lleva este pergamino a Toronn y pídele que lea este pasaje.' Bregar marca una estrofa y te entrega el pergamino.\
\
'Si esto no le hace entender, entonces estamos destinados a separarnos.'","Los Días Venideros"},
[11966]={"Defeated Ruthless Dead in Ringló Vale (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Arvaethor can be found near a mountain pass in the north-western part of Ringló Vale.\
\
You should speak with Arvaethor.","Strange standing stones can be found north of the river Ringló.\
\
You should destroy any strange standing stones you find.","Arvaethor has asked you to destroy any mysterious stones found within Ringló Vale and then meet him near the newly discovered mountain encampment of the Dead.","Arvaethor can be found in the village of Ethring in Ringló Vale.\
\
You should speak with Arvaethor.","'You have found more of these dark stones, too? I as well. Hopefully we have destroyed the last of them, as the coldness emanating from these stones is unsettling.'","Destroyed an ominous standing stone (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Yes, it is true, the dead are invading the Vale. I know not their plans but can assure you, these are not the dead that followed Aragorn to Dor-en-Ernil. These ruthless creatures follow a much darker road that has materialized from the dawnless sky.'\
\
You tell Arvaethor about the strange dark stone you found in the spiders' den.\
\
'Thank you for telling me this. There may be more around the Vale. Seek them out, then meet me near a mountain pass that is teeming with the Dead. We must stop their foul plan before they make their way out of the Vale and to the conflict in the west.'","'It is good fortune to see you again, ${PLAYER}, for horrible things are afoot. The Dead are descending from the mountain! They walk through the trees and travel with Orcs! Arvaethor has just returned to Ethring. You should speak with him at once.'","Defeat Ruthless Dead in Ringló Vale (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Speak with Arvaethor","The Dead Descend","Destroy the ominous standing stones (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[11967]={"¡Derrota a los espectros de las criptas que te rodean!","Busca en los alrededores de Adakûr cerca de las criptas de Esh-kimâkhi señales del cuarteto de viajeros.","'¿Has terminado con la amenaza de los espectros de las criptas? Eso es una noticia realmente bienvenida. Es una pena lo de los viajeros. Ahora deberíamos abandonar este lugar, y rápido. Hay un escalofrío ominoso cerca de estas criptas.'","Adâru-guzi deja escapar un rugido de desafío","Algunos viajeros han desaparecido después de aventurarse cerca de las criptas de Esh-kimâkhi. Se te ha encomendado investigar el área alrededor de las criptas en busca de señales de estos viajeros.","Derrota al espectro temible Adâru-guzi en Esh-kimâkhi.","Centinelas de las criptas derrotadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Busca en los alrededores de Adakûr","Busca en las grandes tumbas de Esh-kimâkhi cualquier señal del último viajero","Horrores de las criptas derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota a los guardianes de las criptas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Busca en las grandes tumbas de Esh-kimâkhi cualquier señal del último viajero.","Derrota al espectro temible Adâru-guzi","Guardianes de las criptas derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota a los horrores de las criptas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota a las centinelas de las criptas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Encuentras a tres viajeros muertos y escuchas el chillido de horrores de las criptas inquietos cerca de ti","Los muertos guardan sus secretos"},
[11969]={"'¡Saludos! ¿Tienes un momento? He vivido mucho tiempo en las Tierras de Bree, pero en toda mi larga vida nunca me he tomado el tiempo para aprender la historia de esta región. Ahora, cerca del final de mis días, he descubierto que quiero saber qué ocurrió antes.\
\
Me uní a esta expedición hacia las Quebradas de los Túmulos con la esperanza de encontrar algunos recuerdos o hacer algunas impresiones, pero parece que las Quebradas de los Túmulos tenían un diseño propio. Recuerdo haber corrido por las colinas cuando era un niño y haber visto que algunos de los túmulos se habían convertido en ruinas. Recuerdo muchas piedras rotas, cubiertas de runas, esparcidas por el suelo, especialmente cerca de el Pináculo De Los Caídos. Quería algunas de esas piedras para mí.\
\
¿Te interesaría traerme, digamos, tres fragmentos de piedra de cerca de el Pináculo De Los Caídos? Quizá ambos podamos aprender un poco de historia.'","Lleva los fragmentos de piedra a Tobold Cortahoja","Recoge fragmentos de piedra (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿Qué? ¿Criaturas malignas te atacaron mientras intentabas recoger estas piedras? No las había visto. Los guías nos protegieron bien de cualquier cosa que los atacara. Me alegra que hayas salido bien, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}.\
\
Bueno, estas runas no revelan nada nuevo. Cada piedra da un poco de cuenta del hombre que fue enterrado allí. No hay nada que revele por qué estas terribles criaturas se han instalado en esos túmulos. Esto es todo un misterio.'","El Pináculo De Los Caídos se encuentra al sur de la entrada norte de las Quebradas de los Túmulos. Tobold Cortahoja te espera entre los Altos de las Quebradas de los Túmulos y el Bosque Viejo.\
\
Tobold Cortahoja quiere que recojas fragmentos de piedra con inscripciones rúnicas cerca de el Pináculo De Los Caídos y se los lleves.","'Saludos, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}. ¿Has llegado hasta ese túmulo del que te hablé? ¿El Pináculo De Los Caídos? Tráeme tres fragmentos de piedra de allí para que pueda examinar sus runas.'","Fragmentos de piedra recogidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Tobold Cortahoja, un anciano y acomodado residente de Bree, estaba interesado en aprender la historia de las Quebradas de los Túmulos y se unió a la expedición que se dirigía hacia allí.","El Pináculo De Los Caídos"},
[11971]={"Egnir appears lost in thought.\
\
Perhaps it is best if you finish collecting the glimmering dust he mentioned.","Talk to Egnir","Uidor can be found in Morlad, in the Blackroot Vale.\
\
Sarnir informed you that Egnir intended to meet with Ludhír, another bowman of the Blackroot Vale. You should return to Uidor and learn where Ludhír might be found.","'Hail! Take care, traveller, for the road ahead is treacherous. Turn back or...\
\
'Oh, wait a moment, I remember you. You were the one who came through the Paths of the Dead! ${PLAYER}, was it? What can I do for you?'\
\
You ask Ludhír if he has seen a man named Egnir. Ludhír's face sinks and he sighs.\
\
'Yes, I have seen Egnir, but... he is unwell. He's gone up the road toward Fennas Dûr, and he's been loosing arrows at the Ruthless Dead for hours. I do not know what has gotten into him, but he must carry some terrible burden on his heart. I have heard him call out to them, taunt them, scream at them until his voice was hoarse, and still he continued... as if he laboured in service of some unknowable quest.\
\
'The Dead will tire of him sooner or later, and I would not see him throw away his life now after he survived the War. He would not listen to me when I told him he ought to return to Morlad, but perhaps he'll listen to you. If nothing else, at least convince him to leave this place!'","With a bitter gaze fixed upon the Ruthless Dead, Egnir barely acknowledges your approach","Ludhír can be found along the road to the north of Morlad that leads to Fennas Dûr, in the Blackroot Vale.\
\
Uidor informed you that Ludhír patrols the road leading to Fennas Dûr and the Paths of the Dead. You should seek out Ludhír and see if Egnir is with him.","Egnir can be found near Fennas Dûr, in the Blackroot Vale.\
\
You have found Egnir, but he seems almost entirely focused on the Ruthless Dead and there is an anger behind his eyes. You should talk to Egnir.","Collected glimmering dust from the Ruthless Dead at Fennas Dûr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Dead and the Living","Egnir appears lost in thought.","Find Egnir near Fennas Dûr","After learning that the wayward bowman, Egnir, passed through Alagrant, your search continues across the Blackroot Vale.","Talk to Ludhír","Egnir can be found near Fennas Dûr, in the Blackroot Vale.\
\
Ludhír informed you that Egnir has gone to Fennas Dûr to confront the Ruthless Dead. You should find Egnir and ask him to return to Morlad.","Collect glimmering dust from the Ruthless Dead at Fennas Dûr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Ah, ${PLAYER}, I finally recalled the name of that man Egnir meant to meet: Ludhír.\
\
'I believe he's one of the Lord's archers, but I couldn't say where to find him. Who sent you here again? Uidor, was it? You ought to ask him, then. I know him to be one of the Lord's finest captains in Morlad, so he would surely know better than I!\
\
'I do hope you can find Egnir, my friend. It seems his sorrows have taken hold of him, and I know all too well how difficult that embrace can be to break.'","Glimmering dust can be collected from the Ruthless Dead near Fennas Dûr, in the Blackroot Vale.\
\
Egnir has asked you to collect glimmering dust from the Ruthless Dead.","Talk to Uidor","Deliver the glimmering dust to Egnir","'Do you see?'\
\
Egnir takes the dust from you and casts it into the wind. It appears to vanish before it ever touches the ground.\
\
'It seems that no matter how much of this dust I collect, they still remain. How can you take so much of someone and expect anything to be left? How queer to think that I might envy such a fate!'\
\
Egnir chuckles weakly.\
\
'I try and I try to make sense of this world, but how can I do that? Look at these turncoats and murderers! They persist evermore, flitting through the world of the Living, and we are made to think they suffer some terrible curse. But when good men—a good man—perishes, no matter how valiant his deeds or how pure his love, he is simply dead and there is nothing that can be done for it. O, if only Derufin had broken an oath!'\
\
You notice Egnir has begun to weep, and his once-stern countenance has broken. You comfort him as best you can. He begins to sob, and after a time, he steadies himself and turns to face you.\
\
'I... mourn the life I had wished to live, my friend. Derufin had not even told Lord Duinhir of us before—before the War took him. And so, who now am I to the Lord? One of half a thousand bowmen, but perhaps the only one who truly knows his loss. And maybe that is enough.\
\
'You need not ask again, ${PLAYER}. I'll return to Morlad.'","Egnir can be found near Fennas Dûr, in the Blackroot Vale.\
\
You have collected a great deal of glimmering dust from the Ruthless Dead. You should deliver it to Egnir.","'What do you want?'\
\
Egnir does not turn to face you, and his gaze remains fixed on the Ruthless Dead along the road ahead. You tell Egnir that you were sent by Uidor to ask him to return to Morlad, and you mention that Uidor seemed worried about him.\
\
'Uidor is a wise man, but grief does not make a good bedfellow of wisdom. That is the very reason why I left. When my grief turned to anger, I found my own hand destroying something dear to me... something irreplaceable. I stopped myself before it was too late, but even so, I could not shake the anger in my heart. In my journey back from the War, I learned that not all of the Dead heeded the summons of King Elessar and that those wretched spirits still haunted the Vale. And so, I turned my anger upon them, hoping beyond hope that I would find some reprieve from my grief.\
\
'Alas, I have not. I have vanquished dozens of these Ruthless Dead, but always they return and I feel no better for it. And now my anger has all but burned out....\
\
'It is curious, though. Each time I 'slay' one of them, they leave behind a pile of glimmering dust. Is it their essence? It always seems to fade away to naught after a time, and then, there they are again—reborn into restless death.\
\
'Have you ever seen such a thing? If you would gather some of it, I can show you.'","'${PLAYER}! Have you found Egnir?'\
\
You inform Uidor that Egnir passed through Alagrant to deface an old carving on one of its tree, but then left to meet with a man named Ludhír.\
\
'Ludhír? What business could Egnir have with him? Ludhír patrols the northern road that leads to Fennas Dûr—to the Paths of the Dead. After the King pardoned the better-hearted of their kind, we thought the Dead would not trouble us any longer. How wrong we were! Ludhír's even had to shorten his patrols of late, since the Ruthless Dead now dare to drift further from the darkness of the Haunted Mountain. Why would Egnir want to go there? I have not known him and Ludhír to be particularly close, friendly as they are to each other.\
\
'I do not like this at all, my friend. Seek out Ludhír, and see if Egnir is still with him!'"},
[11973]={"'¿Ah, buscas instrucción en los aspectos más refinados de la lucha? ¡Que sepas que tales cosas existen demuestra que eres ${PLAYERNAME:un Luchador como pocos[m]|una Luchadora como pocas[f]}! La mayoría cree que se trata simplemente de golpear primero con la mano izquierda y luego con la derecha, pero hay mucho más que eso, como tú y yo sabemos bien.\
\
'Me complace oír de tu disposición para aprender. Muchos subestiman el peligro de un Luchador competente; a veces, el golpe más letal es el primero que lanzas contra un enemigo así.'","Brom Barbadehalcón ha oído decir que otro Luchador como tú fue visto viajando por las Tierras de Bree, rumbo al norte.","Lleva la carta a Hunward en el Muelle de los Comerciantes","El golpe más letal es el primero","Brom Barbadehalcón te escribió para pedirte que busques a un Luchador rohirrim llamado Hunward. Se vio a Hunward dirigiéndose hacia el Muelle de los Comerciantes, en el Bosque Salvaje.","${PLAYER},\
\
La gente de Bree ha estado comentando acerca de un sujeto curioso que pasó por la ciudad hace poco. Creían que era rohirrim, de nombre Hunward, y se dirigía hacia el norte, en dirección al Bosque Salvaje. Creo que era un Luchador como nosotros, ${PLAYER}. ¡Más te vale ir a ver si puedes encontrarlo! ¡Lo más probable es que tenga algunas habilidades útiles que enseñarte!\
\
Espero que lo encuentres en el Muelle de los Comerciantes.\
\
Brom Barbadehalcón"},
[11974]={"Colmillos de araña trampilla recogidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Las Camadas Letales","Thoroniel cree que los Valles Trenzados están infestados por dos camadas distintas de arañas, y ha ideado un plan para enfrentarlas a ambas.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está pensada para una comunidad completa.</rgb>","Recoge colmillos de araña roñecarne (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Colmillos de araña roñecarne recogidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Parece que no estamos tratando con una sola camada de arañas, ${PLAYER}, ¡sino con dos! No sé con qué propósito estas dos camadas han formado una alianza en los Valles Trenzados, pero puedo imaginarlo: preparan un asalto al resto del Bosque de los Trolls.\
\
'Si estas criaturas realmente pertenecen a camadas distintas, propongo que el veneno de una podría ser letal para la otra. Si es así, podríamos usar sus propias armas contra ellas y destruir a cada una de estas letales camadas. No podemos permitir que estas arañas permanezcan aquí. Si estás preparado para otra aventura, ${PLAYER}, te pido que regreses una vez más a los Valles Trenzados.Derrota arañas de cada camada y recoge sus colmillos. Puede que contengan suficiente veneno como para envenenar sus sacos de huevos.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está pensada para una comunidad completa.</rgb>","Recoge colmillos de araña trampilla (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Dos camadas de arañas habitan los Valles Trenzados del Bosque de los Trolls Norte, al norte del campamento de Thoroniel.\
\
Thoroniel te ha pedido que recojas colmillos de las dos camadas distintas de arañas en el Bosque de los Trolls Norte."},
[11976]={"Un antiguo montículo, el Monte de los Muertos de Amon Firn, indica el lugar donde reyes y ejércitos lucharon, sangraron y perecieron. Ahora los muertos se han levantado y se han alzado en armas fantasmales de nuevo, Minetras tanto, un grupo de hombres con harapos han intentado acampar en la zona.","Calargyl te ha pedido que acabes con enemigos en Amon Firn.\
\
Amon Firn está en el noreste de Cardolan.","Vuelve con Calargyl","Enemigos derrotados en Amon Firn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","El Monte de los Muertos","'La actividad que he visto en Amon Firn me preocupa. Los muertos se han levantado y vagan por el Monte de los Muertos, y hombres extraños deambulan por la zona también. A menudo se les ve luchando entre ellos, y me temo que su lucha afecte al resto de la región.\
\
'Parece que Maeriel confía en ti. Bueno, entonces, haz que los espíritus descansen de nuevo, ${PLAYER}, y haz lo que puedas para expulsar a... los hombres de ese lugar.'","'Antaño hubo una batalla entre dos reyes aquí. Ambos cayeron, y ahora sus nombres apenas se recuerdan. La guerra solo trae muerte, y aquí, una que no descansa, por lo que parece.'","Acaba con enemigos en Amon Firn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Bien hecho. Esperemos que los muertos descansen mejor en ese lugar de pesar.'","Deberías decirle a Calargyl que has acabado con enemigos en Amon Firn.\
\
Calargyl está cerca de Amon Firn, en el este de Cardolan."},
[11979]={"Since the enemy breached the eastern Rammas, many Gondorian farms have been overtaken by foes. Ingold has noticed that some enemies have set up a small encampment upon the wreckage of Pel Forod.","'You have returned, and you have defeated their captain? Good!\
\
'War is inevitable but what we accomplish today may turn the tides in our favour.'","Defeated Chulûr","Pel Forod can be found in the northern section of Pelennor Fields.\
\
You should defeat enemies gathered on the destroyed farmlands.","Speak with Ingold","Ingold can be found at the North-gate of the Rammas.\
\
You should speak with Ingold.","Defeat enemies at Pel Forod (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat Chulûr","The Decimation of the Land","Defeated enemy at Pel Forod (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I have witnessed our farmlands and granaries go up in flame. If that blow was not enough to deal with, now the enemy has set up encampments upon the scorched earth of our farms!\
\
'The closest farm to here is Pel Forod. I want to retaliate but it is too dangerous to attack the enemy directly...\
\
'The farm burnt at the hands of the Easterlings. Their captain, Chulûr, is still close by. Perhaps one ${RACE}, such as yourself, would be able to sneak across enemy lines! Are you willing to defeat the enemies gathered at Pel Forod and find their captain?'"},
[11980]={"Habla con Rhiangar","El pergamino descifrado","Melynis ha terminado de descifrar el pergamino antiguo que encontraste en la base de la estatua de Luilloth.","Melynis le ha dado el pergamino descifrado a Rhiangar, quien quiere hablar contigo.\
\
Rhiangar está en el círculo de caravanas, en el norte de Cardolan.","El pergamino es la prueba de la princesa regente Luilloth de Dol Ernil, y ensalza su carácter y sus hazañas.\
\
\\qPor aquel entonces, una niebla cubría la región, desde la que surgió una plaga de muertos vivientes que acabaron con todos. El más temido de todos era una figura espectral conocida como Hithrengor, el Miedo Gris, quien aterrorizó Dol Ernil. Luilloth llevó a su hijo pequeño Ostir a Fornost para su protección, mientras su marido, el príncipe Ostecthel, acababa con la fuente del mal.\
\
El príncipe Ostecthel se adentró en la niebla como un poderoso guerrero, solo para salir de ella tambaleándose como si hubiera envejecido décadas. Casi sin aire anunció que el mal había sido expulsado de estas tierras y la región estaba a salvo. Angustiada pero orgullosa, Luilloth volvió y sirvió como princesa regente hasta la mayoría de edad de Ostir. La gente la amaba, pues era bondadosa y gobernó sabiamente.\
\
¡Pero las palabras de Ostecthel estaban equivocadas! El gran mal no se había ido, pues volvió en el peor momento de Cardolan. Llamado para la defensa de Amon Sûl, el príncipe Ostir cabalgó al norte con muchos de los suyos. En su ausencia, el Miedo Gris volvió a atacar, y Ostir volvió para encontrarse Dol Ernil en ruinas, su gente masacrada y Luilloth desaparecida.\
\
\\qUna vez más, los muertos se alzaron y asolaron Cardolan, mientras Ostir y sus pocos caballeros se retiraron al norte. No se sabe dónde había estado Luilloth, pero las historias cuentan que cuando Ostir y su ejército no regresaron, ella fue en su ayuda. Solo encontró al perro fiel de su hijo ladrando en las Quebradas, y Luilloth supo que Ostir estaba muerto, pues Astoryn nunca abandonaría a su maestro.\
\
\\qLuilloth juró acabar con los tormentos que asolaron la tierra y a su familia. Ella y Astoryn fueron al norte en busca de consejo, siguiendo los rumores de un gran poder que moraba más allá de las lindes del bosque. Nunca fue vista de nuevo, pero los muertos desaparecieron en la niebla.\
\
\\qEl destino de la princesa Luilloth se desconoce, pero aquellos a quienes dejó atrás construyeron esta estatua en honor a su sacrificio.\\q","Rhiangar te ha sugerido que leas el pergamino descifrado, que está en el banco a su lado en la caravana al sur de Andrath. Deberías hablar con Rhiangar cuando lo hayas leído.","Rhiangar está esperando para hablar contigo en el círculo de caravanas, en el norte de Cardolan.","'¡Saludos! Qué pergamino tan fascinante el que me habéis traído. ¡Luilloth era una persona increíble! Una princesa que luchó por su gente y que parece que fue muy querida. Su historia es como una que se contaría alrededor de una hoguera por la noche. ¡Me dio escalofríos y eso que era de día!\
\
'En cualquier caso, he escrito lo que dice el pergamino y se lo he dado a Rhiangar. Está esperando para hablar contigo. Ah, y ${PLAYER}, si quieres seguir los pasos de Luilloth, ten cuidado.'","'Mi corazón está roto por Luilloth, que perdió tanto y vió su reino asolado.'","'Oh, ${PLAYER}. ¡Hemos encontrado algo increíble! El pergamino habla de los últimos días de Luilloth. Una histora trágica. Mi corazón casi se rompe leyendo sobre sus aventuras y su perdición.\
\
'Puedes leer lo que ha descifrado Melynis, pero aquí está el resumen. Luilloth y su familia estaban luchando contra espíritus alzados también, como esperaba. Lamentablemente, perdió a su hijo y a su marido por culpa de los horrores que se alzaron por todo Cardolan. Ella se fue al bosque cercano a buscar consejo de una anciana que vivía entre los árboles. No sé qué consejo le dio, porque Luilloth desapareció al poco tiempo. Sin embargo, su gente la venera como una heroína, porque sea lo que sea lo que le pasase, los espíritus volvieron a sus tumbas y dejaron de causar problemas en Cardolan.\
\
Adelante, lee el pergamino descifrado si quieres. Después hablaremos de lo que creo que hay que hacer.'","Lee el pergamino descifrado"},
[11981]={"Las Hazañas de Durin","'Durin llegó al final de sus días dentro de Helegrod. Las palabras referentes a Mírdanant eran falsas.'","'Los enanos creen que las palabras pronunciadas en la creación de Mírdanant fueron falsas, pero yo no lo creo así.'","'Los Elfos de Eregion hablaron falsamente de Mírdanant, pues no protegió ni a su señor ni a su pueblo.'","'Fue acertado por parte del maestro Elrond enviarte conmigo, ${PLAYER}, aunque la sombra que crece dentro de Helegrod no es noticia para mi compañía. De hecho, he enviado a dos de los nuestros hacia el norte para explorar la base de la Escalera Amarga que asciende hasta las puertas. Ellos verán lo que sucede en Helegrod.\
\
'¿Elrond te habló del quinto Durin? Es cierto que llegó al final de sus días en Helegrod, antigua gran ciudad de mi pueblo. El dragón Thorog codiciaba las riquezas que allí se guardaban y atacó la ciudad, matando a enanos incontables. Durin tomó a Mírdanant, el hacha que los Elfos de Eregion entregaron a su abuelo, y salió a enfrentar a Thorog en combate. Se pronunciaron palabras al forjar el hacha, palabras que se creían asegurar la protección y el poder de su portador. Pero aquellas palabras eran falsas, pues Durin murió luchando contra Thorog en las puertas de Helegrod.\
\
'Es una canción triste, y confieso que me disgusta relatarla ahora.'","'Glóin quizá no quiera compartir contigo el relato de Durin, que encontró su final en Helegrod, pero debe ser informado de que el mal vuelve a agitarse en ese lugar. Encuéntralo en su campamento al norte de Rivendel, entre las nieves de las Montañas Nubladas.'","El señor Elrond cree que debe advertirse al enano Glóin sobre el mal que podría ocultarse en Helegrod, no muy al norte de su campamento en las Montañas Nubladas.","'Los Elfos de Eregion entregaron Mírdanant al abuelo de Durin y pronunciaron palabras de amistad cuando la forjaron.'","Glóin está en su campamento en las Montañas Nubladas, al norte de Rivendel.\
\
El señor Elrond te ha pedido que adviertas a Glóin de la amenaza que, según los rumores, crece dentro de los muros de Helegrod.","'Glóin y una compañía de enanos de la Montaña Solitaria han establecido un campamento al norte, entre las nieves de las montañas. Cuéntale lo que me has contado a mí, y trazaré algún plan para prepararnos contra el mal que haya surgido en Helegrod.\
\
'Tus noticias me llenan de inquietud, ${PLAYER}, pues la historia de aquel lugar es triste, tan hostil como las montañas en invierno. Durin, el quinto que llevó ese nombre, encontró un final sombrío dentro de los muros de aquella fortaleza, pese a las palabras salidas de Eregion sobre el hacha que portaba: \\qLa oscuridad no caerá sobre Hadhodrond mientras la línea de Durin lleve a Mírdanant en amistad con los Gwaith-i-Mírdain.\\q\
\
'¿Quizá la fuerza de esas palabras se había debilitado durante los largos años transcurridos desde que Mírdanant fue entregada? No lo sé. Glóin podría contarte parte de ese relato, si así lo desea. Parte ahora con presteza. No sé cuánto tiempo tenemos para contrarrestar esta amenaza. Que Helegrod esté habitada de nuevo es un asunto preocupante.'"},
[11983]={"Defeated Ruthless Dead in Nimrond cavern (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated Orc in Nimrond cavern (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat Ruthless Dead in Nimrond cavern (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Deep Dark","The western entrance to Nimrond is located atop the mountain encampment of Dâr Matum.\
\
Enter the western side of the Nimrond caverns.","'The Orc cavern we entered on the eastern slope seemed to delve deep into the mountain. This crevasse may contain passage to the other encampment.\
\
'You have done much and we have made it this far. I shall enter the mountain before you and scout out the passage. Enter after I do and make sure you are not followed. We shall meet up again shortly.'","Arvaethor is nowhere to be found. Perhaps he already went further into the caves","'I was foolish to delve into the darkness alone and let the enemy capture me. I care deeply for my home and you have done so much to help it. I do not wish for you to die for this land. I only ask that you accompany me for one last fight.'","Arvaethor has been captured by a band of ruthless dead and corrupt White Mountain Orcs","Defeat Orcs in Nimrond cavern (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Search deeper into the caverns of Nimrond for Arvaethor","After taking the camp, Arvaethor has asked you to follow him into the maw of the mountain and stop the source of the monsters descending into the Vale.","Arvaethor is located somewhere in the caverns of Nimrond.\
\
Search deeper into the caverns of Nimrond for Arvaethor.","Enter Nimrond cavern"},
[11984]={"El Descenso Profundo espeera","'¡Rápido! ¡Sube a esta cabra y date prisa!'","'¡Mithril! ¿Qué? ¿Tú... has encontrado una pequeña veta de mithril en la Vieja Ciudad del Cuerno de Plata? No me lo puedo creer, de verdad que no. ¡Es una noticia maravillosa, ${PLAYER}! Tendremos que enviar refuerzos allí. ¡Menudo descubrimiento, por mi barba!'","Usa la cabra de Öndótt para viajar hacia el norte y hablar con Thettmárr","La cabra de Öndótt está junto a él en la Vieja Ciudad del Cuerno de Plata.\
\
Deberías usar la cabra para regresar rápidamente al Descenso Profundo y hablar con Thettmárr.","'Has hecho todo lo que podía esperar de ti aquí, ${PLAYER}, y ahora debo encargarme de enviarte al campamento de Descenso Profundo para que les des la maravillosa noticia: ¡por fin se ha encontrado mithril!\
\
'¡No te demores; de hecho, ¡deberías llevarte mi cabra! Yo me quedaré aquí y defenderé el trabajo que has realizado para que la Vieja Ciudad del Cuerno de Plata sea segura para mi gente. ¡Estoy seguro de que Thettmárr querrá montar el campamento aquí de inmediato!'","Ahora que has hecho todo lo posible por los enanos de las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata, Öndótt quiere que le digas a Thettmárr y a los enanos del Descenso Profundo que por fin se ha descubierto mithril."},
[11985]={"Los tambores de las profundidades","Ossur se encuentra en la Guardia Orca.\
\
Ossur te ha pedido que lo ayudes contra los orcos y trolls de la Gran Escalera. Una vez que quede satisfecho, obtendrás parte del respeto necesario para ganarte su favor y cumplir con Avar y su tarea de vigilar la Gran Escalera.","Derrota a los orcos y trolls en la Gran Escalera","'Entre mis responsabilidades se encuentran los trolls y los orcos de fuego. Al vigilarlos como hago, debo pedirte que completes las tareas que te encomiende respecto a cada uno de ellos.\
\
'Los trolls de las profundidades son únicos en el sentido de que, aunque son tan salvajes y brutales como cualquier otro troll, requieren adiestradores que los mantengan a raya, evitando que caigan en una frenesí tan terrible que maten sin juicio ni medida.\
\
'Ahí reside la fuerza de nuestros asaltos. Por supuesto, también está el asunto del gran enemigo entre estos trolls...'","'Me complace saber que los trolls han sido debilitados. Esta noticia agradará a todos los que la oigan. Has hecho un gran trabajo, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}.'","Habla con Ossur en la Guardia Orca","Completa la tarea relacionada con los adiestradores de trolls en la Gran Escalera","Ossur se encuentra en la Guardia Orca.\
\
Debes regresar con Ossur y decirle que has completado las tareas centradas en los trolls de Moria.","La Gran Escalera se alzaba antaño al pie de un gran cruce de caminos dentro de Moria. En el apogeo de la gran ciudad, conducía a todas las zonas de las salas y era una maravilla majestuosa de contemplar. Ahora ha quedado bajo el control de Igash, un lugarteniente de Mazog, el líder de los orcos de Moria. Igash ha reunido en un solo lugar a las fuerzas de orcos y trolls de Moria y ha recaudado tributos de cada uno para llevarlos algún día al líder de los orcos. Por ahora, cada tribu pugna por ganarse el favor del lugarteniente, un seguidor fanático de Mazog.","'Se cree que los trolls de las profundidades son quienes tocan los tambores día y noche… o al menos eso se piensa. Sea como fuere, solo hay un buen troll en este mundo, y es el que está muerto. Entra en la Gran Escalera y completa las tareas que te he encomendado.'"},
[11995]={"Habla con Bahanneth en Talan Fanuidhol","'Welcome to Talan Fanuidhol, ${PLAYER}. The Fanuidhol watch is an onerous duty, but it provides ample target practice...and with a bit of creativity, it can be a fair way to pass the time.\
\
'Do not be fooled, though. Beyond this border, the Enemy is gathering to destroy us. They await the day when their Dark Lord emerges from Barad-dûr to lead them into Caras Galadhon, to the doom of us all.'","The Defence of Fanuidhol","You have been acknowledged as a friend of Lothlórien through your efforts on behalf of the Elves.","Bahanneth is at Talan Fanuidhol to the north.\
\
You have been instructed to speak with Bahanneth, who will tell you how best you might aid the defenders there in thwarting the Orcs that foray out of Moria.","'You have our trust, ${PLAYER}. In return, I would ask that you ply your blade on our behalf once again.\
\
'To the north are the barren slopes of Fanuidhol where Orcs and goblins have crept out of the cracks that run deep into the bowels of Moria. \
\
'Our scouts watch them from the telain that border the forest there and contrive their downfall. It is fair enough sport, but only a prelude of the battles to come should our true hopes fail us.'"},
[11996]={"La defensa de Galtrev","Scouts report that forces of the White Hand have been seen marching on Galtrev, surely as an act of revenge for what was done to the Overseers of Galtrev.","Talk to Bron to defend Galtrev","Bron is at Galtrev.\
\
Talk to Bron to defend Galtrev.","Bron is in Galtrev at the milestone marker in the centre of town.\
\
You should speak with Bron to collect your reward for assisting in the defence of Galtrev.","'Let us prepare for the attack, Duvodiad!'","Talk to Bron in Galtrev","'You were a great help against the marauding villains of Isengard, ${PLAYER}! Please, choose a reward as a token of Galtrev's gratitude.'","'Scouts report that strong forces from Isengard are marching upon Galtrev... surely to take retribution for our defiance of the White Hand Overseers.\
\
'Will you help us to defend the village?'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This is a solo quest and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>"},
[11997]={"The sight of Náin the Slakeless shakes Tuhâl to his core","Grámi Hornhelm can be found in Hammerstead.\
\
You should talk to Grámi Hornhelm.","'Lord Náin's reputation precedes him, but he is even more intimidating in person! Despite my fears, I must find the words to convince him, for the welfare of my people.'","Help Grámi Hornhelm with 'Weapon Repossession'","Bring Tuhâl before Lord Náin","Lord Náin needs to know about the Jangovar threat.\
\
You should bring Tuhâl before Lord Náin in Járnfast.","Talk to Tuhâl","Help Lóssi with 'The Head of the Snake'","Grámi Hornhelm can be found in Olin's Forge, in Hammerstead.\
\
You should talk to Grámi Hornhelm.","'Thanks to your aid, we should be able to repel the rest of these Easterlings. Before you return to Járnfast, you should see this.'\
\
He points at the bound Easterling in the corner. He does not look like a Jangovar.\
\
'This one actually surrendered! He has been blabbering on about being forced into this and wanting to speak to someone of authority. I have no time for such things, so I give you, ${CLASS}, that authority! Go learn what he is going on about!'","Help Lóssi with 'Withstanding the Marauders'","Tuhâl is preparing to stand before Lord Náin and speak his piece.\
\
You should talk to Tuhâl.","Return to Járnfast with Tuhâl","You tell Lóssi that the convoy was destroyed and the weapons stolen. Only Vílur Strayfoot survived.\
\
'Curse these Easterlings! There is not time to grieve. Go up the road to Olin's Forge and speak with the Master Smith, Grámi Hornhelm. We can hold them off for now.'","Talk to Grámi Hornhelm","You tell Grámi all that the Easterling has said. \
\
'Just as I thought; they are arming themselves for another attack. Return to Járnfast with haste and inform Lord Náin! And take that prisoner with you. The last thing I need is some useless oaf taking up space!'","'I am Grámi Hornhelm, son of Grárin, Master smith of Hammerstead. Are you here to help?'\
\
You tell Grámi about the request from Lord Náin, and the destroyed convoy.\
\
'Aye, we knew it was only a matter of time before the Easterlings made their move. We did not expect these tactics, however. They are almost certainly after the weapons we craft here, so that they may arm the refugees coming in from the Stair. Ha! But they will not have them so easily! There is work to do, ${CLASS}. I will not allow this rabble to hobble our production. Report back to Lóssi, and help him however you can.'","Help Lóssi with 'Relieving the Guard'","There is work to do in defence of Hammerstead.\
\
You should complete quests in Hammerstead.","Tuhâl looks wonderstruck at the sight of Járnfast","An Easterling is being held prisoner in Hammerstead.\
\
You should talk to the Easterling prisoner.","Talk to the Easterling prisoner","'I never wanted any of this, you must believe me! The Jangovar, they have my family!'\
\
You ask the Man to calm down and explain himself.\
\
'I am Tuhâl, of the Chayasír. My family and I came from the east. We are refugees, fleeing for our lives! The devastation... it was horrible... \
\
'We came up the stair, following word that there was safe haven among the vales. A man with a kind face told us that we could have a new life in Er Shamol, which you call Utterby. There was plenty of food, and good shelter, he said, but it was a lie. The Jangovar are luring refugees in, and then forcing the strong to fight, under threat to their families! The ones who cannot fight are chained and made to work. The convoy raid and these small strikes are only the beginning. They are planning to attack Dale again when they can!'\
\
You tell Tuhâl that Lord Náin is considering collapsing the stair to prevent the Easterlings from entering the Ironfold.\
\
'He cannot! My people will have nowhere to go! More are coming. Does no one know what took place in Rhûn?'","You should talk to Grámi Hornhelm, who can be found in Hammerstead.","The Defence of Hammerstead","Lord Náin needs to know about the Jangovar threat.\
\
You should return to Járnfast with Tuhâl.","Hammerstead, a small community of miners and smiths in the Ironfold, is under attack. Help the dwarves defend it from the Jangovar!"},
[11998]={"Naethmunn está en el campamento de montaraces de Tinnudir, en Evendim, al suroeste de la Casa Brumbar.\
\
Has defendido la Casa Brumbar del grupo de boggarts que lo amenazaba y ahora deberías volver a Naethmunn con el relato de tu éxito.","'¡Has vuelto, ${PLAYER}! ¡Debo aplaudirte y pedirte disculpas al mismo tiempo!\
\
'Todavía no creía que fueras de fiar. Estos son días oscuros, y los Dúnedain no podemos permitirnos confiar tan a la ligera. ¡Pero me has demostrado que eres de fiar una vez tras otra!\
\
'Le diré a Calenglad que tu misión no debe ser retrasada. ¡No pienses mal de mí! Los Dúnedain no han sobrevivido tantos años por confiar tan alegremente.'","Habla con Pantescal","Naethmunn te ha pedido que ayudes al montaraz Pantescal, defendiendo las ruinas de la Casa Brumbar en Parth Aduial.","Los vestigios de la casa Brumbar están en Parth Aduial, al noreste de Tinnudir. Naethmunn te ha pedido que cruces el puente hacia tierra firme y sigas la línea de la costa hacia el norte hasta que veas algunos del os muros que quedan de la Casa Brumbar.\
\
Naethmunn te ha pedido que ayudes a Pantescal, quien está actualmente planeando la defensa de un punto importante de los Dúnedain contra una horda de boggarts.","Has defendido con éxito la Casa Brumbar de los boggarts","'Mientras te enfrentabas a Jabo Sotosombrío en Tyrn Fornech, un montaraz llamado Pentescal nos avisó de que un gran número de boggarts avanzaba hacia las ruinas de la Casa Brumbar. Brumbar era de un linaje Dúnedain de no poca importancia antes del abandono de Annúminas, y debemos mantener los terrenos de esa antigua mansión segura de los cazatesoros, aunque quede poco de los edificios.\
\
'Pantescal no parecía demasiado preocupado por esta banda de boggards, pero me tranquilizaría que le ayudaras. Estas criaturas son cobardes, pero en gran número incluso el más débil de los enemigos puede suponer una amenaza.\
\
'Las ruinas de la Casa Brumbar están al noreste de Tinnudir, en Parth Aduial. Cruza el puente hacia tierra firme y sigue la costa hacia el norte. Brumbar es poco más que algunos muros ruinosos ahora, pero no podemos permitir que los boggarts mancillen su memoria.'","'Tu misión no debe ser retrasada por más tiempo, ${PLAYER}.'","La defensa de la Casa Brumbar","'¿Naethmunn te envía? No creo que necesite tu ayuda, ¡pero no la rechazaré si me la ofreces!\
\
'Estos boggarts son débiles, pero su gran número les infunde valor. ¡Ese valor está mal fundado, ya que los expulsaremos de la Casa Brumbar fácilmente!\
\
'¡Prepárate!'","'Siento haber tardado tanto en confiar en ti, pero era necesario.'","'Encontrarás la Casa Brumbar al noreste de Tinnudir, en Parth Aduial. Cruza el puente hacia tierra firme y sigue la línea de la costa al norte hasta que encuentres a Pantescal,¡ y ayúdale a defender el lugar de la banda de boggarts!'"},
}
